ion/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/1869", "mandatory_overlay_refs": []}, {"scope019_index": 2483, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/combat_config/procedural.rs", "sha256": "3c8e5fb3460309d571886e03b68f8e50e2e57e03e54180785b2bd721d35fc65a", "actual_EOF": 66, "material_ranges": [[1, 60]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/2483", "mandatory_overlay_refs": []}, {"scope019_index": 2484, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/combat_config/ragdoll.rs", "sha256": "af87991f5cb3f8fd2a6398ea5135c5daacd24c7b9c2b23181ebecec7bc516ad3", "actual_EOF": 112, "material_ranges": [[1, 59], [81, 112]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/2484", "mandatory_overlay_refs": ["CONT-OWNER-RANGE-EXTENSION-042"]}, {"scope019_index": 2485, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/combat_config/playback.rs", "sha256": "6eac571d575402a1ccbcdda6ad103850b9f52fed3f9bc602d558ea5629d23fdd", "actual_EOF": 48, "material_ranges": [[1, 25]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/2485", "mandatory_overlay_refs": []}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete PR config826 and eight child bodies37/19/33/19/48/46/66/112 including original inline tests; entire actual P16 main827/ai37 difference reviewed (seven SignedLength field substitutions/getter extraction; no authority update differences). P16 procedural1-60, playback1-25, ragdoll1-59/81-112 freshly read and actual scoped counterpart bodies compared; no P16 excluded capsules60-80 or procedural61+ body credit. Recovered complete main difference after first output truncation before coverage. Personally consumed CAMERA-ADM03-011/013 actual route facts and current07CONTRACT013 authored-source/install/digest traversal, not prior verdicts.", "authority_trace": ["Top TacticalCombatConfig has authored resolution/autoresolve/realtime/movement/AI/input/targeting/presentation/animation sections. Public Clone/Serde records retain requested configuration; validation computes checks transiently and does not store a second accepted flag. schema_version describes codec shape, not current policy revision. digest749-757 recomputes actual serialized validated content, no retained digest field or stale digest setter.", "Top Default772-775 clones defaults::canonical; AI default33-36, forecast13-19, landing18-22, ragdoll108-112 all project that same canonical object. They do not restate independently maintained numeric literals. Current07CONTRACT013 follows the one LazyLock YAML parse and versioned runtime snapshot installation/getters; mutable authored DTO is distinct from installed snapshot, with no claimed universal App Resource synchronization.", "Animation gait reference speed describes animation calibration, while movement speed config describes actual requested motion; sample_hz for locomotion and pose bake describes different sampling jobs. No same-fact equality is promised merely because defaults coincide. Landing min/max, guard min/max duration, playback activation/deactivation/initial thresholds, pose contact min/max, and response target/cap are independently meaningful limits; validators compare coupled order without storing derived classification.", "Forecast horizon/trend response govern yellow presentation projections, not a second gameplay impairment. Ragdoll capsule dimensions, muscle proportional/derivative gains, relative brake and velocity caps govern distinct articulated presentation facts; Never versus After stores one release policy, and Option<f32> codecs derive one outward representation on demand. No separate enabled flag or duplicate release time retained.", "Body-part hitbox vector is the authored collection; local seen[7]598-613 is ephemeral uniqueness checking, not a second persistent body-part membership table. body_part_index760-770 is a total closed enum adapter for this array, not an independent mutable taxonomy.", "TacticalConfig.validate checks relations and scalar policies but does not compare ten autoresolve mirror fields to movement/AI. F005 remains exact independent authored mirror discrepancy: digest includes them, Core compiled receiver derives canonical shared sections instead. These full bodies substantiate that qualification; no new claim of two live resolver disagreements."], "per_source_dispositions": {"351/1860": "Authored aggregate + computed digest/default/validation routes inventoried; F005 connected mirrors retained. P16 physical wrapper changes preserve same authority chain.", "352/1861": "AI fields are authored thresholds/timing, canonical Default projection; no independently stored classification. PR raw finite-policy admission questions remain03, not07 duplicates.", "1863": "Two orthogonal forecast timings project canonical config; no gameplay penalty duplication.", "1864": "Landing threshold/compliance/min/max/recovery are separate facts; canonical Default and computed order validation.", "1865": "Six distinct maneuver durations, no derived cached duration or local fallback literals.", "1866/2485": "Playback calibration/rate/correction/limits and typed cadence owner; actual PR relation validation only. P16 prefix role limited to fields through25.", "1867": "Pose bake/sampling/contact settings are independent authored bounds; comparisons computed at use validation, no cached validity.", "1868/2483": "Procedural target/cap/rate/divisor settings separate; radian report epsilon is a numerical allowance, not another configured angle cap. P16 prefix partial validation preserved.", "1869/2484": "One ragdoll configuration and canonical Default; one tagged release state; no independent derived strength or boolean cached here. P16 excludes capsule declarations."}, "connected_repair_acceptance": "Only F005 connected mirror removal/derive repair from this inventory; preserve genuinely independent calibration/limits/history and unit distinctions. No extra runtime cache or new duplicate owner required.", "status": "exact source-role inventory with existing finding; no source edits or later-lens clearance"}
