les polygon, recomputes plane and pitch, updates matching surface bounds/catchment centre/elevations/route endpoints, gable enclosures and edge endpoints. These generated fields are views of edited physical geometry and require coordinated recomputation; actual body updates those named projections, not a stored valid flag. Failed partial helper mutations remain private cloned state.", "Gable polygons are derived end sections from current weather faces and host envelope. Two end signs establish two distinct roles; update_pitch recomputes pair when source recipe is available, otherwise scales all polygons. Actual resolver583-591 appends this pair first. Extra clerestory enclosures do not establish generic zip-shorter defect. Arbitrary public reorderings are accepted-graph ownership weakness, not evidence that normal first-two construction is wrong.", "Bearing supports a many-to-many physical contact relation. Its owner/node/bounds are not redundant merely because they accompany a solid; however generated descriptor bounds must describe current physical contact. Editor omits that dependency, yielding F006. Threshold0.001 is an audit contact policy, not an independently cached measurement.", "Network sample/route/outlet/catchment records represent distinct physical path facts. Editor updates selected route/catchment projections; no blanket claim that every unchanged drainage field is stale without exact corresponding producer/use comparison. Network declarations only supporting partial role facts here; full network source remains unfinished."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F006"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Derive or rebuild matching bearing descriptors from edited physical products in cloned state before joint commit; preserve pivot constraints/no-op/error atomicity. Use one coordinated physical projection update rather than a second independent setter/cache rule. Every actually moved physical weather/flashing product has current corresponding descriptor semantics after successful editing; failed reconstruction preserves prior plan; actual many-to-many bearing audit contract remains intact. No new test/case or execution performed.", "qualification": "No actual edit/runtime/audit failure. editor229 and bearing58 blank context only; excluded tests not read. Root retains source/function repair authority.", "status": "exact scoped source inventory with concrete omission; supporting source remainders remain pending"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-017", "at": "2026-10-22T19:25:43.228575+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope019_index": 46, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/build.rs", "sha256": "fc42ea1f2234144e94d6bfac86f254cd059799b9f9e5ae6de7f77e3125f19b7c", "actual_EOF": 509, "material_ranges": [[1, 509]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/46"}, {"scope019_index": 850, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/build.rs", "sha256": "fc42ea1f2234144e94d6bfac86f254cd059799b9f9e5ae6de7f77e3125f19b7c", "actual_EOF": 509, "material_ranges": [[1, 509]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/850"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete PR509 and complete actual P16 body difference (no differing lines), with explicit current build role comparison. Personally consumed actual prior Camera core-build-admission-024 source narrative, then reanalyzed this lens independently.", "authorities_and_updates": ["Build compiler imports runtime vocabulary/schema/validator definitions by exact path rather than maintaining a second build-only enum or policy table. Module inclusion itself gives no called-body credit; those source roles remain separate inventory cells.", "Quest authored files sorted then read once per build loop. Parsed documents/source files/dialogue token source map and digest are generated together from those actual text reads. Raw source map is diagnostic provenance before semantic validation, not accepted identity membership. Output JSON and digest describe immutable deployed build snapshot, not live disk state; changes to external authored files do not imply a stale mutable runtime cache.", "Item source documents/source names/raw source strings are pushed together in same loop, validated then emitted with source map and digest. Source IDs/file/line/column are deliberately retained provenance, not second current ItemDefinition. Temporary sets for icon membership and known reference IDs are derived views within compiler operation, not surviving independently authored copies.", "Road encounters parse once; sources and definitions appended in one foreach; item references derive from authored item IDs, not independent hand-maintained list. Item compiler is called first in main; actual receiving validators are separate policies whose predicate correctness stays with own cells. Multiple catalogue digests describe different source sets, not a same-fact duplicate digest.", "Organization arrays extend source_files repeat_n(relative,values.len) alongside documents.extend(values), singleton branch pushes one each; zip validator lower API gap from03 is not a normal build pairing mismatch. Policies and promotion text are incorporated into same digest and embedded JSON snapshot. Promotion role existence resolves against actual organization documents, not an independent role namespace table.", "Digest covers path+NUL+raw source bytes, so whitespace/location changes may change digest without semantic definition changes by design: source provenance/version identity differs from semantic equality. No cached validity, independent numeric defaults, mutable compiled classification or duplicate accepted source table is authored in these build functions."], "disposition": "No redundant mutable authority established in exact build functions; authored content and coordinated immutable generated projections/provenance are different representations with one construction owner. Existing source-validator/admission gaps and F005 combat emission mirrors remain separately preserved.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one compiler source snapshot and shared vocabulary; no proposed removal of useful source maps/digests or forced semantic-only digest. Runtime catalogue caches/lookup predicates remain separately inventoried, no blanket receiving-source clearance.", "status": "exact full source07 inventory; source freeze; no generator/build run"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-018", "at": "2026-10-22T19:26:53.088756+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope019_index": 48, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/animation_pack_id.rs", "sha256": "f5933a0bf3fad1149d1f10c1e16ae4883fa626338fc6aa29723816dc8ae4e317", "actual_EOF": 43, "material_ranges": [[1, 43]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/48"}, {"scope019_index": 418, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-terrain/src/digest.rs", "sha256": "80e021f45fedb26ff313fe42e19a49503716be0c710173af5285e572bfe5ce98", "actual_EOF": 28, "material_ranges": [[1, 28]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/418"}, {"scope019_index": 854, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/animation_pack_id.rs", "sha256": "f5933a0bf3fad1149d1f10c1e16ae4883fa626338fc6aa29723816dc8ae4e317", "actual_EOF": 43, "material_ranges": [[1, 43]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/854"}, {"scope019_index": 1314, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/capture_ids.rs", "sha256": "79611041d0a1bcee78aa63cf2241262e35d8850da9303a45d9627ba0b78bf8de", "actual_EOF": 29, "material_ranges": [[1, 29]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/1314"}, {"scope019_index": 1317, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/catalog_id.rs", "sha256": "349beedb860eef8c0f4e9b882e10824b343451085d654c20b7c001ea98a3b810", "actual_EOF": 134, "material_ranges": [[1, 134]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/1317"}, {"scope019_index": 2081, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-terrain/src/digest.rs", "sha256": "80e021f45fedb26ff313fe42e19a49503716be0c710173af5285e572bfe5ce98", "actual_EOF": 28, "material_ranges": [[1, 28]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-019.json#/files/2081"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh all43 AnimationPackId/all29 capture IDs/all134 catalog identities/all28 terrain digest. Complete actual P16 counterpart body differences for pack ID and digest reviewed, no deltas; actual open identity/native hashing roles compared explicitly. Personally read Native current03 group004 catalog-identities/native-bind-and-report source narratives for actual source facts, not lens verdict.", "contracts": ["AnimationPackId retains one exact Cow string. Two named constants are convenience authored IDs, not exhaustive membership catalogue; From and transparent Serde remain deliberately open. AsRef/Display/Debug derive current string on demand, no separate cached label or kind. Owned versus borrowed storage is representation, not two independently mutable identities.", "MotionId retains one checked stem and mirrored computes suffix result from it. MotionKey pair namespaces motion by pack; those are orthogonal parts of composite identity, not duplicated current ID. Asset directory and native asset path are different stages; motion_path derives full path from directory+stem at call time. No retained path/name/classification cache can survive independent identity mutation in this file. Directory constants identify different packs; mapping/policy in catalog builder remains separate source inventory, no whole catalogue clearance.", "AuthoredAnimationFrame one u16 coordinate; abs_diff computed on demand. It is authored-frame coordinate at clip rate, not duplicate sample tick/time. No cached frame seconds stored. Content membership remains actual loaded-clip obligation, not current same-fact cache.", "Capture helpers produce diagnostic String from native target/entity and explicit placeholder at moment of capture. Entity encoding includes index AND generation. They retain observation identity in reports, not a second live entity owner; test20-27 is source evidence for output spelling only, no execution.", "Terrain valid_digest delegates canonical SourcePackageDigest constructor rather than duplicating grammar. hex_sha and hex_sha_reader both derive SHA256 from actual bytes/read stream, with output formatted at native boundary. Temporary read buffer and hasher state are streaming operation state; no independently authored digest/cache. Returning raw String is prior propagation gap, not a second current digest authority. Reader error stops computation; no success cache retained."], "disposition": "No redundant current authority inside these exact immutable identity/native hashing definitions; related catalogue lookup, clip reload and diagnostic consumers still separate cells.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Do not close open identities, merge frame/sample/time units, or replace generation-qualified diagnostic IDs with index-only labels. Existing propagation/admission findings remain unchanged; no07 repair proposed from these declarations.", "status": "exact source-role inventory; no later-lens or source clearance"}
