: 390, "material_ranges": [[1, 390]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1326"}, {"scope020_index": 1327, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/loading/motion.rs", "sha256": "6240a63d570d51843113c28182afebe0b156ee558ae60ef960acbe737c308eb6", "actual_EOF": 175, "material_ranges": [[1, 175]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1327"}, {"scope020_index": 1328, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/mod.rs", "sha256": "cd54ed038a4131a947dff4db1a0310069b669800547e2f2b6456566e9c0ec4c4", "actual_EOF": 810, "material_ranges": [[1, 810]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1328"}, {"scope020_index": 1355, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/presentation/plugin.rs", "sha256": "678af470ebedb38a874258f1f27264052978d78d58b438469bc24e25ef4d0b78", "actual_EOF": 109, "material_ranges": [[1, 109]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1355"}, {"scope020_index": 1399, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/resolver.rs", "sha256": "1b0873cd746e039bdbc6d22d4f55b28ffad8141f68f43fbdb9fb3be25eb7eeb0", "actual_EOF": 217, "material_ranges": [[1, 217]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1399"}, {"scope020_index": 1406, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/rig_identity.rs", "sha256": "207d7aff4743dc30e8fd603dd02ca0e9dd83863ac4c65bc53e208949767a7b64", "actual_EOF": 84, "material_ranges": [[1, 84]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1406"}, {"scope020_index": 1408, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/animation/semantic_route.rs", "sha256": "503b335e2aaa99a5cb283b02af958b8990b0e2fce6817b437b56e1bc8900e6e1", "actual_EOF": 145, "material_ranges": [[1, 145]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/1408"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete literal bodies for each member, including existing catalogue/editor/mod inline tests, no execution. Personally consumed Native current03 group004 actual catalog/loading/revision/rig identity narratives and compared current07 construction/update/consumer meaning. Supporting focused existing-scope authored_cadence1-128, pose_buffer70-100/305-349, stride_calibration1-50 and runtime config71 were read; those larger partial sources are NOT credited by this group.", "per_source": {"1315": "Code-owned semantic catalogue is authored policy independent of native glTF animation names; not a cached text reclassification. MotionSource required_last_frame is minimum source acceptance, last_frame is authored anchor extent; deliberately different variable attack values show they are not aliases. Poses versus references have distinct semantic lookup versus calibration anchor roles. Builder derives path from admitted directory/stem once and discards directory; no competing retained path owner. Diagnostic editor counts/route resolutions are observations computed per validation call, not mutable gameplay tables.", "1316": "Builtin pose/motion mapping and frame literals are actual code-owned source. Builder used for both packs, attack helper shared, library existence lists derive pack.poses keys before completeness check. Mirrored file endpoints deliberately carry no independent semantic poses. Actual6/18 contact constants in parent are normalized authored contacts, not copied live contact state. Child lower parser/pack library stays separately scoped.", "1318/1319": "Revision events merge all native event kinds and failures plus changed asset-resource contents, including previous runtime handles so removals are visible before message flush. Source matching checks actual source/path/label. Refresh removes clip/unavailable state together, clears grip processed/unavailable and derived asset-index caches, rebuilds library on affected motions. This is coordinated native asset invalidation, not proof of every cache dependency: FPS/config omitted is F007.", "1326/1327": "Requested source/load task, processed/unavailable state and loaded clip are distinct stages of one asynchronous source operation. Ready(None) is final absent observation versus outer None pending; retained source/path supports failed-first source revisions. Successful clip publication occurs after target/duration/frame admission; derived library rebuilt after changed results. Source identity remains native AssetServer authority. Separate unavailable/success sets require coordinated invalidation (actual source revisions do so), not blanket deletion. F007 captures missing non-asset dependency.", "1328": "Runtime retains requested/admitted/failed state and computed semantic library, not independent authored semantic policy. Clip duration is observed current clip metadata and must invalidate with that clip revision. AnimationPlayback/PlaybackPose/extrapolation data retain current evaluation versus source clips/anchors as distinct pose/time/weight facts; plan/mirror/foot influence copied in apply_playback_pose together. Runtime-grip/HUD/inventory classifications computed on read from actual owner data. Per-joint bind/target-bound and rig-attached markers assume stable native scene generation; initial bind caches exact Name classification/target paths and no Changed<Name>/hierarchy rebind appears in these paths. Conditional generation contract retained alongside F003, no claim normal scene mutates or arbitrary debug Name change changes original authored identity.", "1355": "Actual chained update orders revision invalidation -> collect -> rig binding -> route -> skeleton evaluation -> pose-buffer updates and visibility. This eliminates a claimed ordinary per-frame route/playback race; commands synchronized by chain. Fixed/postupdate stages reflect distinct physical/render timing, not two same-current simulation authorities. No config-generation invalidator is added here.", "1406": "AuthoredRigJoint caches derived body region and optional BoneRole from exact immutable private name only at new; no field setters/Serde/Default expose independent mutation. Getters and includes use that coherent admitted identity. Native Name versus original admitted name is an asset lifecycle question at loading boundary, not local stale-field construction. Lower BoneRole heuristic definition remains own source, no authority from spelling alone.", "1408": "SemanticRouteTrace stores input/evaluation and requested/resolved path as one generated current-frame observation. route_semantic_pose initializes both paths from same requested path; no independent normal setter in file. Telemetry cumulative counts are history, not current pose. Failure removes old trace before chained skeleton evaluation; success replaces whole trace. Cached library attack availability receiver is actual F007 path.", "1399": "ResolvedBodyPlan builds all current weighted/continuation/extrapolated spans before one PlaybackPose publication; whole-body mirror is derived reduction of exactly those contributions rather than independently configured value. Cadence derives whether action samples empty. Source pose/time/layer/mirror dimensions are orthogonal. No independently mutable retained result in resolver helper; lower span functions remain separate sources.", "1323": "Fallback mannequin is explicitly obvious diagnostic T-pose geometry while authored base rig loads. It is not promised equality to projected character body/collider, so separate dimensions are legitimate independent diagnostic assets. Mesh dimensions project once into native constructors, limb anchor arrays are authored geometry and handedness, not duplicate current actor joint positions. Root offset uses same runtime config getter; actual existing roots are generation-time artifacts, not automatic mutable config views."}, "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F007"], "explicit_dependencies": "Core AnimationPackLibrary algorithm, full pose-buffer/baking/calibration config fingerprints, BoneRole classification and scene-generation mutation ownership remain separately inventoried source roles. Supporting reads here do not close those source cells or infer all hidden graph predicates.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Give motion/pose availability cache an explicit configuration dependency (at least authored FPS, plus actual catalog/target generation where relevant), re-admit success AND unavailable entries or derive availability on access. Coordinate library replacement with current clips; preserve optional missing-source fallback and native failure distinctions. Do not replace this with a duplicated validity boolean or copied default FPS.", "status": "exact current source inventory with missing cache dependency; no repairs or other-lens clearance"}
