sha256": "cd6f17bf2bc0925f53292c3a04e552698ba572ae7127aa3ce31430296ca420a4", "actual_EOF": 110, "material_ranges": [[1, 110]], "mandatory_overlay_refs": [], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/2467"}, {"scope020_index": 2557, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/animation/sample_rate.rs", "sha256": "744e4868234738f05d7030c0cbae4c057fcbad21d41987b955e6895f3f9d5093", "actual_EOF": 86, "material_ranges": [[1, 86]], "mandatory_overlay_refs": ["CONT-OWNER-RANGE-EXTENSION-141"], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/2557"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full PR bodies for15 leaf/policy source families. Fresh complete actual P16 counterpart difference comparisons for authored_angle/sample_tick/sample_rate; exact bounded measurement/response comparison after combining mandatory overlays039/001/040, leaving measurement54-62 and response100-125/163-169 excluded. P16sample_rate full86 allowed by mandatory141, not inferred from old1-43. Complete actual P17 authored_angle155/height148/measurement110 differences inspected; added min/max selectors and diagnostic quantity difference explicitly compared. UTF8 stdout recovered sample_tick after first CP1252 print failed; no unobserved body credited.", "per_source_role_comparison": {"authored_angle (345/1752/2465)": "Each angle/speed retains one authored scalar in explicit degrees or radians/second; radian getters derive on demand rather than retain second converted value. Signed versus magnitude and angular speed versus angle are separate policies/units, not same current angle. P17 min/max return selected values; no extra state. P17 error BodyAngle versus PR SignedAngle is diagnostic classification, not duplicate stored angle authority.", "measurement (346/1768/2467)": "NonnegativeLength retains one magnitude; PositiveDuration narrows the existing elapsed owner rather than storing primitive+elapsed duplicates. Half, span and getters derive results, no cached conversions. P17 min/max select admitted operand. P16 exact constructor/getter/helper scopes exclude sample_span54-62; no P16 arithmetic credit there. checked_nonnegative is shared scalar gate; repeated caller gate use is not independently authored physical data.", "response_parameters (348/1774)": "ReferenceAcceleration, ResponseRate, LeanGain, CompressionCompliance, LookDistribution, MuscleTone and AngularStiffness have distinct units/physical roles with one private scalar each; no copied configuration default or cached quotient. Ratios/exponential/step fractions/interpolation/compression/yaw distribution computed from actual arguments at call time. Rate0, tone/gain>1, positive fractional look divisor and finite signed native yaw remain deliberate. P16 excludes compliance operations100-125/163-169, so only actually scoped roles compared; PR full operations remain covered.", "sample_rate (1775/2557)": "Frequency and interval in private AnimationSampleRate are a legitimate coordinated derived cache. Only TryFrom<f32> constructs pair: same admitted original frequency then checked reciprocal duration; no mutable fields/setters or alternate pair constructor. Serde try_from reconstructs both from one raw hertz scalar; From/Serialize emits original frequency bits, not recomputed reciprocal. This preserves original count-before-division rounding in elapsed_for_span. Cannot disagree through declared API; do not collapse frequency into reciprocal-only state or force reciprocal requirement on separate AnimationFrequency.", "sample_tick (349/1776)": "Tick coordinate and sample span are separate absolute/count units with one u64 backing each; elapsed conversion occurs via explicit sample rate. Saturating/wrapping/checked operations compute new values and document different clock/deadline policies. No retained seconds/tick duplicate or mutable cached deadline flag here.", "phase_response (1772)": "Phase correction rate and error limit retain different authored policy facts; no repeated phase coordinate. Native getters project once, no normalized/wrapped state copy; bounds>1 intentional.", "height_measurement (1764/2466)": "HeightDistance/HeightSpeed wrap lower length/speed single backing. Difference yields signed displacement; recovery/absorption/max/over use actual measured/configured operands and return new scalar values. Measured impact versus configured minimum is observation versus threshold, not competing current speed. P17 min/max add selectors only.", "shaping_time (1779)": "One finite signed response-shaping coefficient; no retained elapsed or clamped copy. Advance functions derive progress using current operands and retain only returned typed result. Signed shaping parameter is distinct from nonnegative elapsed or strict-positive duration.", "event_span (1761)": "Event observation count and positive coalescing budget are count versus policy maximum, not second sample-clock span; contains/is_even/is_zero compute classifications on demand. No stored boolean cache.", "calibration_parameters (1754)": "Positive contact height scale and grid interval count are independent authored policy inputs, not cached observed foot range or grid contents. Getters/native outputs only; no duplicate defaults.", "ik_parameters (1765)": "Knee amplification and settle progress are different dimensionless meanings. is_complete computes from progress, no redundant completion flag; COMPLETE/ZERO constants express valid values, not independently mutable copied state.", "cadence_limit (1753)": "Authored cap maximum, transition width and minimum calibrated distance describe independent policy components; no cached transition start/end. Constructor retains them atomically with relation gate, Serde source input delegates same constructor. CadenceSelection retains requested demand versus actually applied capped result as distinct operational facts; is_capped derives their relation, not independently set flag. ExceedsScalarRange distinguishes demand beyond representation from applied finite cap.", "sample_values (1777)": "CyclePhase coordinate, CycleDelta displacement, BlendWeight contribution and ClipMirror binary choice are distinct. One scalar/tag each; wrapped/checked arithmetic computes new state. Bilateral contact helper references canonical LOCOMOTION_SECOND_CONTACT_PHASE rather than copying another editable table. No primitive+typed cached phase or stored absence flag; is_absent derives factor.", "pose_coordinates (1773)": "Attack pose coordinate intentionally supports drawback/overshoot; action progress delta is signed difference, not same phase. Clamping reads AttackCurve owner at operation time rather than copies limits. deserialize_progress normalizes at owned decode route; no stored raw+normalized pair.", "continuation_parameters (1756)": "Readiness location, incoming tangent and start coordinate describe distinct spline conditions. FOLLOW_READY derives from measured preparation fraction; preparation_fraction getter converts on demand, no retained duplicate. AttackContinuation is one current observation pair, no cached independently mutable completion/classification. Decode normalization is operation policy, not parallel authority."}, "actual_receiving_context": "Current07CONTRACT015 configuration retains these typed parameters and canonical defaults; CONTRACT019 reads actual current FPS/native frame conversion and semantic routes. Operations in each leaf body project operands only at numeric kernels; contextual native output is not a retained second authoritative quantity. Other actual consuming/state sources remain separately inventoried; no leaf verdict substitutes for cache invalidation there.", "disposition": "No redundant current mutable authority in these exact scalar/policy families. Explicit SampleRate pair is coherent derived cache. Existing source propagation/invalid admission/arithmetic/aggregate findings remain separate lenses, not waived by this judgment.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve canonical authored scalar bits, distinct units/history/request-versus-application facts and private coordinated SampleRate construction. No07 scalar repair proposed. Do not replace good caches with duplicate owner types or collapsed units.", "status": "exact source-role inventory; no source/other-lens clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-021", "at": "2026-10-22T19:36:01.460954+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope020_index": 49, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autopsy.rs", "sha256": "590a02732db6f33532c882ce0d6a6686de3f4bad9e3368242999cc3c30f9fd35", "actual_EOF": 648, "material_ranges": [[1, 648]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/49"}, {"scope020_index": 856, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autopsy.rs", "sha256": "590a02732db6f33532c882ce0d6a6686de3f4bad9e3368242999cc3c30f9fd35", "actual_EOF": 648, "material_ranges": [[1, 648]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/856"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete PR autopsy648 including every inline original test. Complete actual P16 body difference reviewed, no deltas; current retained snapshot/pure observation roles compared. Personally consumed prior current03 CAMERA-ADM03-047 actual factory/gate/receiver facts, not prior lens verdict.", "authorities_and_lifecycle": ["PostCombatBody and SystemicPathologySnapshot capture physical/systemic state at death, not a cache of living actor current health. Redacted attacker/weapon/disease identity is intentionally absent. Subject identity identifies historical observation; it does not independently mutate a current actor. Dynamic actor/world updates must not rewrite historical pathology as if cache refresh were required.", "Body injuries derive from matching defender log entries, sort by sequence and truncate32 at factory; retained health/blood and injuries are orthogonal final condition versus injury observations, not necessarily mutually derivable. projectile flag replaces deliberately discarded source kind/attacker identity; no same retained kind plus competing flag in BodyInjury.", "Corpse custody derives at call time from discovery-to-now, explicit burial/exhumation history and precedence; decomposition derives separately from death-to-now plus handling damage. These are different clocks/facts. Test current source explicitly admits buried AND exhumed together and gives Exhumed priority, so do not collapse them as impossible duplicate current-state booleans just from names.", "AutopsyEvidenceContext carries one examination observation of decomposition/scene/opening obscuration. Pure finding methods compute current call quality/strongest injury/physical morphology/systemic interpretation from supplied evidence; they do not retain a separate editable canonical cause or diagnosis. Surgery, Physiology and Bestiary lenses deliberately provide different interpretations, not competing authoritative culprit IDs.", "Quality skill/obscuration differ: skill is examination competence, obscuration is tissue damage caused by opening, entropy is input variation. They are not copies required to equal. Upper evidence thresholds are authored interpretability policies; accompanying fever/air-hunger/wasting are independent observations, not derivable solely from four systemic severity axes.", "Death-required incident derives bounded deterministic battle attempts and checks actual victim lethality. It does not write a corpse flag alongside live body state here; selected successful outcome remains canonical source. Incapacitation and lethality intentionally differ. Full battle producer/DB retention rules remain their separate source inventory."], "disposition": "No redundant mutable current authority in these exact corpse snapshot and pure interpretation definitions. Raw public snapshot/quality admission bounds from03 remain actionable, not cleared; DB caches or context lifecycle cannot be assumed from this source.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve historical snapshots, redaction and interpretive uncertainty. Do not replace contextual physical evidence with a stored canonical diagnosis or refresh death snapshot from live actor. Actual persistence/examination context construction will be separately traced; no07 repair proposed here.", "status": "exact full source07 inventory; no source/other-lens clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-022", "at": "2026-10-22T19:41:52.318639+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope020_index": 51, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/authored_weapon.rs", "sha256": "d51000403c3e70e523d5bdfe690114fcf0781449dabb10a52ee3dc006b00f5ca", "actual_EOF": 130, "material_ranges": [[1, 130]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/51"}, {"scope020_index": 52, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/classification.rs", "sha256": "7699fe2b1452a7aff4551999b62c6ed6764dc5dddabf8bce8d8d74e8bf1ebd78", "actual_EOF": 65, "material_ranges": [[1, 65]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/52"}, {"scope020_index": 53, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/error.rs", "sha256": "877b773ae83bec290966d406d2aae3f84f7e5d804970e4f7771faa63e7b1d318", "actual_EOF": 21, "material_ranges": [[1, 21]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/53"}, {"scope020_index": 70, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/power.rs", "sha256": "7469ca1e1a2a0c7bfa49292adac667ebbf5323f3dfd5f0e39e368e18f118d2a7", "actual_EOF": 168, "material_ranges": [[1, 168]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/70"}, {"scope020_index": 71, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/threat.rs", "sha256": "bf72fdd14fdc1fc1e4196b4c65172f6c71d0658f4bad6896cb41495acf889798", "actual_EOF": 190, "material_ranges": [[1, 190]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/71"}, {"scope020_index": 858, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/authored_weapon.rs", "sha256": "446d7c751bfec9680b1aaf74efb82a38f44b145076a521b5bd5c0ea14844003c", "actual_EOF": 127, "material_ranges": [[1, 127]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/858"}, {"scope020_index": 859, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/classification.rs", "sha256": "7699fe2b1452a7aff4551999b62c6ed6764dc5dddabf8bce8d8d74e8bf1ebd78", "actual_EOF": 65, "material_ranges": [[1, 65]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/859"}, {"scope020_index": 860, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/error.rs", "sha256": "e3bd3bd8fb753b33e583e5cba64967ca07539dd8b4b0032a2153a330b59a01df", "actual_EOF": 19, "material_ranges": [[1, 19]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/860"}, {"scope020_index": 876, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/power.rs", "sha256": "76922a00bc1d4bf13c6d972aaba83258551ce853fff438f2edc3f0d295ae025a", "actual_EOF": 168, "material_ranges": [[1, 168]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/876"}, {"scope020_index": 877, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/threat.rs", "sha256": "58a5e53d2fdf5283f4e7ba8a58f1335f894bb6b4ab4524f3684f92bbca8dc106", "actual_EOF": 187, "material_ranges": [[1, 187]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/877"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full PR authored130/classification65/error19/power168/threat187 source bodies; complete actual P16 differences reviewed for every listed family, including additional Geometry error variants, SignedLength fields/getters at native equations and typed authored head conversion. Supporting fresh full PR model363 and bounded contact_geometry45-115/mobility90-150 are actual facts, but whole model and those larger helper source cells remain unfinished.", "per_family": {"authored_weapon": "One shared factory snapshots authored definition and generated recipe; timing/balance/geometry fields derive from actual typed sources. This construction is coordinated; retained derived distal flag becomes latent independent authority only at public record mutation (F008). Semantic source-versus-snapshot distinction means immutable catalogue source is not a live synchronized clone requirement. No duplicate new input defaults introduced in factory; recipe/physical current ownership remains own source inventory.", "classification": "Closed battle kind and movement request enum; realized displacement/velocity are separate facts. Display and Serde are current native diagnostic/replay projections of closed cases, not mutable classification caches. Exact existing source tests lock vocabulary without claiming all independent adapters globally removed. Close/Hold/Retreat computes signed target velocity from supplied nonnegative maximum; no duplicated measured velocity stored.", "error": "BattleResolutionError wraps actual underlying Speed/Timing/BattleTime/Performance causes; P16 also Geometry. These observed typed failure categories are not current physical state flags. Formatting is actual error boundary, not competing acceptance predicate or default.", "power": "Conservative observer combat power is recomputed each call from current snapshot; no retained power cache or independent authoritative battle outcome. Physical/output/skill/armor/health/readiness terms are intentionally a decision aid, not outcome oracle. Current incapacitation obtained from canonical combatant method at use. for_melee/for_ranged produce immediate mode-specific equipment views; requested/base versus per-mode selection not automatically stale duplicates. Armor scalar coverage input semantics remain pending in model producer graph, not silently equated with interval geometry by this observer function.", "threat": "ThreatId canonical member parse resolves one authored profile; physical/training ratings derive base difficulty and actual multipliers. Attributes/skills/body/equipment are a simulation snapshot, not a second mutable bestiary catalogue. ranged flag controls both weapon and sidearm/ammunition initialization; initial_ammunition is historical start count versus current mutable ammunition. Innate versus worn armor are different sources, current producer initializes full or half geometry/scalar together. Hard-coded abstract threat training/loadout coefficients are authored projection policy, not copied unknown human body defaults; no forced equality to player generation asserted."}, "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F008"], "explicit_remaining_obligations": "CombatWeapon/CombatEquipment model full current-authority inventory remains pending, specifically scalar armor.coverage versus authored interval union producer/receiver semantics, and selected base weapon lifecycle. Main autoresolve2879 and actual battle state operations are unaccounted. Source partial reads do not constitute whole helper/model credit.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Derive distal classification from canonical weapon geometry/materials on access, or retain it only inside an immutable admitted geometry owner with all dependent fields private and coordinated operations. Propagate same owner to movement/contact/evidence recipients; do not add another independent flag or duplicate equivalent geometry type.", "status": "exact listed source-role inventory; model/supporting remainder explicitly unfinished"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-023", "at": "2026-10-22T19:44:55.449844+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope020_index": 69, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/model.rs", "sha256": "b1b76643680707125e6bd040b60703127a2ed09cc460e226b2c4f08c90724ffe", "actual_EOF": 364, "material_ranges": [[1, 364]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/69"}, {"scope020_index": 875, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/model.rs", "sha256": "20d6bb98602db1d3dbc649b575e54c27fb766279d064deed4a13fcc0c695af72", "actual_EOF": 363, "material_ranges": [[1, 363]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/875"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete PR model363 and entire actual P16 model364 difference reviewed in CONTRACT022; current07 supporting critical producer/recipient followthrough now resolves earlier candidate meaning. Fresh item_catalog1-115, validator485-506/882-900, melee_iteration285-357, targeting160-265 and PlayerEquipment580-650; only these bounded supporting source facts, no whole source coverage for their larger files.", "retained_state_comparisons": ["Body/skills/essentials/equipment represent pure battle snapshot inputs. Limb health versus weight versus handedness, individual skills and specialist Bestiary hours are different facts. total_damage derives health; no retained total-damage cache. Skill trait adapter derives outputs on request, not independently stored aggregate effective Bestiary. CombatEssentials explicitly returns physical condition1 because fatigue/burden already belong live combat incapacitation; no hidden second fatigue reduction from this adapter.", "CombatEquipment.weapon is selected PlayerEquipment adapter state; melee_weapon/ranged_weapon are separate available choices, holding sides belong each choice. for_melee/for_ranged clone once and select matching weapon+holding side together for immediate equations. A hybrid may legitimately retain ranged base weapon and melee sidearm, so no invented requirement all three weapon values equal. Stronger borrowed-view/type structure may be assessed in11; no same-current-value drift established in normal adapter chain here.", "Weapon ID versus physical weapon descriptor are identity versus simulation projection, not derivable from each other in absence of catalogue/query context. Ammo mutable remaining versus initial count in combatant is temporal history. Shield side/bonus versus separate melee holding side represent different occupied hands. Battle snapshot raw public correlation gaps remain05/03 material, not automatically redundant numeric copies.", "CombatWeapon.distal_headed IS entirely derivable from neighboring geometry/material fields and actual factory computes it once, so F008 remains. Other balance/derived physical values originate authored/recipe projection; actual complete geometry recipe is not retained here, so do not assume every observed coefficient is reconstructible from truncated neighboring values or collapse distinct reach/grip/total/head extents.", "Armor coverage scalar versus coverage_geometry are not identical coordinates. Fresh actual item_catalog64-99 computes scalar mean across every placement weighted by each span region count. Fresh melee_iteration299-357 copies that whole-item aggregate for observer estimate while interval geometry filters selected placement to a particular coarse body part. Parent power armor_power uses scalar estimate; model347-358 actual armor_surface tests per-part interval occupancy. Whole-item mean and selected-part union can legitimately differ. No new duplicate-authority finding/equality requirement; public correlation/semantic naming can be strengthened separately.", "Armor material/resistance/padding/flexibility/range of motion and interval identity metadata describe different physical/association properties, not one redundantly represented truth. innate and Default construct local snapshots atomically; defaults full-body health/70kg are abstract starting snapshot values, not proven duplicated authored human generation policy. Actual callers overriding physical state remain own cells."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F008"], "previous_pending_disposition": "CONTRACT022 model hold now resolved by explicit actual aggregate-versus-selected-interval producer/receiver comparison and selected-mode adapter lifecycle. No prior pending chronology erased; no proof by name/hash/count.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Derive or seal distal classification in one canonical geometry owner as F008; preserve orthogonal aggregate/interval coverage and actual per-mode selection. Do not force broad physical equality or introduce raw compatibility paths.", "status": "exact full source07 inventory with latent derived-flag finding"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-025", "at": "2026-10-22T19:50:20.008275+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope020_index": 66, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_round/mobility.rs", "sha256": "6807ada697c587ffd96f625c61692de55a4ae1548d7dcd9e5d2d539e5f6187c0", "actual_EOF": 234, "material_ranges": [[1, 234]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/66"}, {"scope020_index": 68, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_round/scheduling.rs", "sha256": "170846de4c534120087f3f12c2fd365b8f2103c97d270ff28d71bee179d6e147", "actual_EOF": 391, "material_ranges": [[1, 391]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/68"}, {"scope020_index": 872, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_round/mobility.rs", "sha256": "201e0aa26a4ceec81c0caa799acc2dae96ad3d1600ed6184aef8f671e3becf1c", "actual_EOF": 226, "material_ranges": [[1, 226]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/872"}, {"scope020_index": 874, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_round/scheduling.rs", "sha256": "9c56fb8232e356e6e204ba7c1065597c6063b0b25572d6f0e7cb131b2a7eb320", "actual_EOF": 391, "material_ranges": [[1, 391]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-020.json#/files/874"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full PR mobility226/scheduling391; complete actual P16 mobility234/scheduling391 body differences personally reviewed. P16 replaces raw lengths with canonical SignedLength, checked GeometryResults and private MeleePairMovement preview result; selected-weapon source choice remains BASE in effective reach and movement intent. Fresh actual current main1-1332 and existing switch fixture2090-2117 support operation context but do NOT complete whole main2878/P162879 source cells.", "retained_relationships": ["Movement intent versus integrated displacement/velocity are requested versus realized physical facts. Per-actor signed velocity contributions are different participants, not duplicate global pair velocity. Centre separation versus surface gap explicitly adds/subtracts canonical two-radius constant, not a second independently authored radius.", "Engagement target associates each retained distance with its counterpart. Observe ignores old distance for a different target, uses current associated distances and an explicit min reconciliation policy. Commit initializes changed target associations; advance pair rebinds both when needed and publishes SAME computed after-distance to both, each own velocity. Distances may differ temporarily after one new association before movement reconciles them; no unqualified equality invariant or normal-stale-distance defect invented.", "Schedule retains start/contact/recovery times as different phase coordinates; jitter/adaptation are sampled or response history, not cached global config copies. Existing current attack returns captured timing; scheduled_attack_is_current compares captured start/contact against retained current generation to ignore invalidated work. Trace stores before/after/readiness as event history with one construction owner, not alternate mutable live schedule.", "Initialization samples delay/jitter once then installs current schedule; schema/numeric policy remains owned canonical elapsed/time leaves. window/round timing derived from same actual parameters at call, no independent round-duration table here.", "AttackStartTrace records request/distance/readiness/window/adaptation and computed timing together. Distinct before/after phases and tick encodings are immutable observations of scheduled operation, not current cache flags.", "Actual melee geometry source selection is inconsistent across retained base/per-mode weapon representations: F009. This explicitly narrows prior CONTRACT023 local-view conclusion; private for_melee exists but these readers bypass it."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F009", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F008 actual stored distal flag receiver support"], "explicit_dependencies": "Main battle inventory remains pending child commitment/defense/joint/turn mutation bodies and actual main counterpart comparison; lower opposed movement kernels remain separately inventoried. No source coverage from rg search or fixture count.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Use one explicit selected melee/ranged equipment view through ALL geometry, movement, targeting, workload and contact readers. Prefer remove independent base weapon/holding-side selection from retained loadout or make transient views borrow canonical mode choice. Do not sync extra mutable copies opportunistically or patch only this getter with conversion. Keep genuine alternate weapons/IDs/ammunition history and trait/numeric ports.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory with concrete selected-owner mismatch"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-029", "at": "2026-10-22T19:53:27.222931+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope021_index": 55, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/joint_melee.rs", "sha256": "7373a905f23ab3075cfb464c0a936ce1ebc33ba6c5c6ad23866b1a1479c5b983", "actual_EOF": 329, "material_ranges": [[1, 329]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/55"}, {"scope021_index": 56, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_defense.rs", "sha256": "6fffe49da3ec9f55c7b6dfcdeb723ef065569b78b004db991367d44329ee7fe9", "actual_EOF": 221, "material_ranges": [[1, 221]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/56"}, {"scope021_index": 72, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/timeline.rs", "sha256": "97e87014b1ece1247d03e8e2a7e1e36db3c28ccae7b17b95dd7857ca13075406", "actual_EOF": 139, "material_ranges": [[1, 139]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/72"}, {"scope021_index": 862, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/joint_melee.rs", "sha256": "7373a905f23ab3075cfb464c0a936ce1ebc33ba6c5c6ad23866b1a1479c5b983", "actual_EOF": 329, "material_ranges": [[1, 329]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/862"}, {"scope021_index": 863, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/melee_defense.rs", "sha256": "6c64790c60c4ad2b52d4e3a18e312b8be73cb714ec27aa194f9a345d17eda293", "actual_EOF": 221, "material_ranges": [[1, 221]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/863"}, {"scope021_index": 878, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/autoresolve/timeline.rs", "sha256": "4e83c1f6cda9e4f7a8f9a19ac6c54119c67701f6d4dae37641c5e6b7b94b753d", "actual_EOF": 139, "material_ranges": [[1, 139]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-021.json#/files/878"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh all current PR joint329/defense221/timeline139. Complete actual P16 body differences reviewed: joint same code/current fixed-window role; defender timing commit distance typed SignedLength only; timeline distances/displacement typed SignedLength, other observations and construction unchanged. Current007 constructors/updates/recipient logic analyzed directly, not prior lens verdict.", "contracts": ["Joint window computes source contact set from both sides, sorts by actual contact time then actor ID, captures batches from that immutable sorted set before mutating combatants. Batch ID/members/order are coordinated projections of same collection, not separately authored independent sets. First ID is deliberate stable representative; later public-in-module record access is stronger aggregate ownership concern, not an actual partial membership update in these functions.", "Captured ScheduledMeleeTiming is operation identity, while Combatant timing is current mutable action state. scheduled_attack_is_current rejects stale snapshots before turn; joint completion clears start/contact/scheduled-measure together. These two copies intentionally distinguish queued work from active state and must not be collapsed. A canceled/changed attack invalidates pending snapshot rather than synchronizing history into it.", "Joint movement interval and contact batches are different domains; simultaneous contacts may still apply for defeated actor when captured batch contains other simultaneous attacks. This preserves temporal simultaneity; do not relabel as stale defeated flag. Old timeline events are history, not live source of action readiness.", "Defender decision contains actual physical response plus optional committed-trade decision/probability/work observations. FinishTrade derives no physical defense, other committed choices derive reciprocal intercept; fallback recovery/dodge/nonblocked cases have no committed payload. Normal actual constructors produce these together. No separate mutable stored availability flag; can_block derives equipment and defender phase is observed current timing.", "ScheduledMeleeTiming commit installs jitter/start/contact/measure/recovery/adaptation reset as one method. Start/contact/recovery are independent phase coordinates; reaction input reflex and displacement time derive different functions of one observed sampled delay, not duplicate elapsed values. Recovery effectiveness computed at call, not cached through later recovery mutation.", "Timeline at() computes tick from exact time then retains both as historical event. Quantized nonnegative tick and finite signed seconds are different coordinates and intentionally lossy (negative time maps0); no inverse equality promised. Phase before/after, readiness before/after and previous/current counters describe transition history, not duplicated present facts. No event setter changes time after at() in these source paths; public record representation is separately broader than actual factory.", "Joint integration subdivision uses local64 steps/second, timeline native tick encoding also uses64. Numerically equal literals alone do not prove redundant authority: integration discretization and native report coordinate can be independent policies. No change demanded until actual intended tactical-clock ownership/relationship is established by its source inventory; current constants are explicitly recorded as a calibration comparison dependency, not a confirmed drift finding."], "explicit_dependencies": "Current main battle state inventory still waits actual roundmod/commitment update paths. Shared Core defense numeric probability/choice bodies remain separately scoped source roles. Physical fixed-step/native clock ownership comparison remains explicit at source frontier; no SDK or gameplay clock inferred from same number64.", "findings": "F009 selected-owner graph remains active; no new proven duplicate current state from these coordinated operation/history records.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve queued-work identity checks, atomic timing field update/clear and immutable event/batch observations. Any aggregate seal may make relationships explicit without deleting required temporal copies. No current07 source edit or new default/type introduced.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory; no other lens credit"}
