eview fixture assembled from actual canonical character/item definitions, not independently authored weapon physical parameters. purpose_build authors controlled attributes/training and textual scenario context; stable hash labels diagnostic actor/item provenance, not persisted membership. build_from_spec installs combatant and descriptive metadata once. Body75kg is explicit controlled specimen, not a claim all characters derive mass from same spec.", "authored_equipment constructs the same projected weapon into base/melee slots together and installs stable sourceID, inventory weight, shield bonus/side/identity and authored armor in one factory. This melee-only fixture is coherent and does not disprove F009 hybrid path. Description/name/source-ID context remains report provenance, not another resolver reading physical stats from text.", "Armor scalar coverage stays canonical whole-item mean while geometry is selected occurrence placement for bodypart; they serve different observers023. Multiple authored placements chosen by occurrence, iteminstanceIDs distinguish samecataloguedefinition. Armor material/resistance/padding/flexibility and range-of-motion copied from one definition. Inventorymass sums actual requested equipment even if per-bodypart projection keeps last armor; total carried mass and contacted surface are distinct facts, not duplicate authority.", "Acceptance evidence reports selected controlled samples with canonical helper results. Energy69.5/76.788/101.4 is explicit reviewed incident input, transformed energy computes from returned fraction and retained input in same operation. It is not a recomputed live weapon-damage cache; repeated101.4 for polearm scenario is controlled calibration observation, no demonstrated policy table disagreement. Classification/edge_contact, capability-string/attack_available and defended/attack_value are emitted together for immutable report epoch, not used as mutable current gameplay flags.", "Forced armor records retain input coordinate, source geometry and resulting selected/intersected observations. Mirrored vambrace cases intentionally distinguish side/bodypart/placement and preserve canonical symmetric spans; no independent copied side-classifier table. Current native error wrappers preserve real variants, while display strings are output labels, not reparsed authority.", "Timeline evidence derives side-swap equality, canceledIDs and canceledIDs-that-contacted from actual retained event sequences in one factory. It runs pure simulator when explicitly invoked; no run occurred during audit. Historical cancellation versus later contact correlation is diagnostic result, not current pending attack collection. Simultaneous fixture explicitly coordinates both actors timing and gap before resolver; bounded cancellation seed search and firstcontact prefix are review sampling policy, not runtime scheduler authority.", "Existing inline tests assert source physics/cadence projections, deterministic bounded progress, latest readiness event use after cancellation, shared defense/contact equations and armor gaps. They are source oracle evidence only; no test execution or new assertion. Assertion equality does not remove F008 computed flag or F009 selection duplication from actual public/live graph."], "explicit_dependencies": "Lower item catalogue/generated weapon/placement and canonical starting-character definitions remain own whole07 source roles. Native report/presentation may serialize observations; no whole-feature clearance or unscoped render receipt inferred.", "findings": "Existing F008/F009 remain; no new proven independently mutable current authority in these fixture/report factories.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Maintain canonical factories and report epoch. If fixture metadata is redesigned derive source labels from single fixture descriptor without collapsing controlled scenario inputs or deleting evidence. No source edits/later-lens credit.", "status": "exact source07 inventory complete"}
