ource_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/body.rs", "sha256": "febe5d8b193afe3cefa2292965bb42c15d4a5d25aef8a2f3c9fea757b3720317", "actual_EOF": 179, "material_ranges": [[1, 179]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/884"}, {"scope022_index": 907, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/composite.rs", "sha256": "d12458450a9186177a47c1b404529e9f6128dfd204fd63817b8a4fd8cf27e72f", "actual_EOF": 386, "material_ranges": [[1, 386]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/907"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh all PR rewards31/clock95/body179/composite386, complete actual P16 counterparts reviewed no body delta; actual same source roles individually compared below, not hash-only credit.", "contracts": ["Recorded battle participation is historical membership, living list is current commit eligibility; living_participant_ids derives intersection each benefit commit while preserving recorded order and duplicate behavior. Do not collapse historical participation to current alive cache or remove delayed loot recheck.", "BattleTime stores one finite signed second coordinate; getter returns backing value, duration difference derives transiently and origin placement explicitly uses checked elapsed. Zero/default and negative coordinate intentional. Tactical authority clock is explicitly independent; timestamp/micros conversion elsewhere is native projection, not automatic duplicate clock authority. Checked result arithmetic and margin comparisons retain no redundant intermediate.", "BodyPart closed enum, flags sets and body-side enum represent identity/membership not parallel health. LimbWeights contains four independently selected contributions, computes normalize and by_part on demand; presets are intentional operation policy rather than copies of one mutable current owner. Both-arm weight depends primary side, so equal arm preset and handed policy cannot be collapsed just because some cases coincide. Zero raw default/normalize admission issue stays other lens, no extra current norm/sum stored.", "PlayerInfo stores each supplied component once in private generic slots. with_* consumes prior composite, carries unrelated components and inserts exactly one previously empty component; no independently synchronized copied summary. fatigue/attributes/skill/attack/contact methods delegate current supplied components to canonical by_parts helpers every call, not retained cached derived skills or damage. Examples compare calls and copied primitive inputs, not two runtime formula owners.", "Composite gap targeting combines freshly computed accuracy with actual weapon precision then native contact helper; selected equipment choice comes from caller. Current F009 caller ambiguity remains, no adapter reclassification from weapon text here. Actual derive target annotations identify intended trait backing; no uninspected foreign macro whole-body proof claimed."], "explicit_dependencies": "Canonical lower skill, essentials, equipment and combat equations retain own scoped07 roles; body mass/dependency admission and foreign derive expansion not inferred from type names or current delegates.", "findings": "No new redundant current authority in exact listed sources; F009 remains at selected-view caller.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve temporal participant revalidation and single component backing; derive operations from current canonical inputs. No edits/tests/later-lens credit.", "status": "exact source07 inventory complete"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-036", "at": "2026-10-22T20:04:22.036854+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope022_index": 75, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/bestiary.rs", "sha256": "223a264abf8a0c920de6dbe26b12c3b013dfb0cd8e7161c0a5614db5eb3294b7", "actual_EOF": 1558, "material_ranges": [[1, 137], [139, 191], [210, 294], [311, 338], [345, 396], [484, 803]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/75"}, {"scope022_index": 76, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/bestiary/error.rs", "sha256": "279813fa320c4ce35bbef2229faa4367af4c93d97f074cec46e6984974245b6c", "actual_EOF": 51, "material_ranges": [[1, 51]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/76"}, {"scope022_index": 881, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/bestiary.rs", "sha256": "223a264abf8a0c920de6dbe26b12c3b013dfb0cd8e7161c0a5614db5eb3294b7", "actual_EOF": 1558, "material_ranges": [[1, 1558]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/881"}, {"scope022_index": 882, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/bestiary/error.rs", "sha256": "279813fa320c4ce35bbef2229faa4367af4c93d97f074cec46e6984974245b6c", "actual_EOF": 51, "material_ranges": [[1, 51]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/882"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual full PR Root source facts ROOT-ADM-BESTIARY-024 then fresh all material PR1-137/139-712/713-803/804-1225/1226-1558 (omitted138 blank only). Fresh error51. Actual P16 comparison ONLY exact scoped ranges listed, including newly scoped habitat745-803; equal source ranges compared actual cache/identity/profile semantics, not byte credit. P16 unscoped397-483/804+ and neighboring enums excluded, no whole1558 P16 claim.", "contracts": ["ThreatId private length/63-byte capacity is one coordinated compact string encoding, not independently mutable public length authority. Both constructors write bytes+length together, no setter; as_str derives view. ReportDescription and EvidenceKind reuse representation but have distinct open evidence/report semantics and syntax-only admission. ThreatId member parse is separate operation, existing syntax-vs-membership admission finding remains; do not conflate public constants with complete catalogue roster.", "profile uses one process-lifetime OnceLock map compiled from immutable embedded authored catalogue. Key and profile.id created from same id at compile; public returned value is a Copy snapshot and cannot mutate cache. Default placeholder fields are overwritten before private function returns, not separately published live profiles. Names, aliases, investigation lists and combat fields derive from authored source; no hotreload mutation route defined here. Process/catalog rebuild recreates cache, so no missing invalidation from hypothetical live authoring edits.", "PR profiles_for_category reads actual source facets then gets compiled profile from same immutable catalogue; is_primary records query-relative role, not a second stored absolute category. Primary and secondary are distinct intentional facets (current existing tests confirm multi-category werewolf/skeleton), not redundant labels. Display/singular/plural are separately authored irregular grammatical forms; no deriving by naive suffix or merging display text with identity.", "Typed runtime rig/attack/protection/temperament/activity/habitat/countermeasure compile from authored text once. This is catalogue-to-runtime representation boundary, not two independently updated active resolver tables. Full primitive-to-enum propagation remains producer/ownership finding, but no claim current process hot mutates raw catalogue beneath typed cache. Raw profile literal can be broader; existing admission/aggregate findings stay distinct.", "Habitat weight combines canonical allowed habitats with id/habitat-specific selection calibration; bridge requirement/evidence derive separately and select_habitat_relation returns coordinated matching observation. Allowed membership, rarity weight and required explanation are different rule facts, not derivable solely from each other. No forced weight10000 and no new fixed habitat relation narrowing; actual maximum900 preserved.", "PR lore derives explanatory text from fields actually consumed by combat each call; investigation hypotheses explicitly do not claim implemented modifiers. Candidate ranking derives from forward likelihood, contextual observation, canonical regional prior and deduplicated evidence; plausibility and curated distributions intentionally differ by curation_weight. Both are computed per query, not independently authored inverse-probability tables. Derived diagnostic cardinalities/scores do not retain current hidden truth for preparation; evidence_limited_preparation takes only observable inputs.", "PR validate_catalog is diagnostic crosscheck over actual compiled/source data; tests detect drift but are not the source of runtime authority. Thresholds and all-habitat list serve different diagnostic roles. Existing source tests expressly cover regional plausibility versus curation, ambiguous reports and irregular plurals; no execution. Extra catalog_tests child declaration1558 is navigation only and its separate body remains pending own source role."], "explicit_dependencies": "Actual quest_catalog immutable install/build/schema validation source roles still pending07, as are report_quality/catalog_tests and downstream selected observer source inventories. Full PR observer conclusions do not credit excluded P16 observers. Constructor syntax/member and derived len-first vs lexical ordering findings preserved, no new policy inference.", "findings": "No new07 competing live authority proven in exact current profile cache; original admission/producer findings retained without clearance.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep immutable catalogue generation explicit and compile one canonical typed runtime owner; avoid recursive membership lookup during startup and keep open report/evidence grammar. If future mutability introduced use explicit generation/invalidation rather than equality tests. No source edits/new tests/later-lens credit.", "status": "exact source07 inventory complete"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-037", "at": "2026-10-22T20:06:09.320917+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope022_index": 78, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/capability.rs", "sha256": "80bba40bb933f538a8ad43a88ab0d13bb1cea44bf19486687e27896363dae7f0", "actual_EOF": 554, "material_ranges": [[1, 554]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/78"}, {"scope022_index": 886, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/capability.rs", "sha256": "6e0a321cc3add825f92a96426d7bd4b3af413ad02381e547a2db66fdd8676d82", "actual_EOF": 552, "material_ranges": [[1, 552]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/886"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full PR552 incl original tests, complete actual P16diff554 (test typedReach only), same actual computation/query roles explicitly compared. Fresh direct PRDB capability694 and complete P16diff555 read as supporting caller, not yet counted whole DB source because cache refresh lifecycle/held projection dependencies remain.", "contracts": ["Capability evaluation derives melee/ranged/precision/heavy, armor tiers and scalar skill/checks from currently supplied component inputs in one calculation. No underlying body/equipment/skills retained inside CharacterCapabilities, so fields are projections rather than neighboring independent live flags. meets consumes actual snapshot versus independently authored required thresholds; desired role requirements and measured capabilities are different facts, not one state.", "Armor tier booleans are nested predicates computed together from cuirass/helmet/shield/paired limbs and current per-region coverage; quarter can be shield without armor, so not a naive single monotonic percentage. Full threshold0.75 is explicit tier policy, not canonical armor geometry identity. Rounded numeric rating, precision labels and raw measured skill values are distinct UI/query resolutions, computed on access.", "Unbounded harmonic party aggregation, bounded complementary geometric medical aggregation and command lead/support-neutral-baseline aggregation intentionally have different policies; contribution is derived before/after difference with command allowed negative effect. Their shared sample constants/max5 do not make these interchangeable formulas. No cached sorted list or max stored alongside independent contributors.", "Religion and Bestiary helpers share finite head-health policy but call distinct canonical Skill aptitude identities; generic rule factoring is maintainability candidate, no actual competing rule divergence shown. Explicit ignored instinct/focus are source policy, not independent hidden penalty. Existing tests are source evidence only, not run or new assertions.", "Direct PRDB receiving table is a real retained derived cache: refresh computes whole capabilities then power and publishes row only on changed value, with physiology band transition hooks. This is not cleared by pure evaluator proof; actual invalidation/dependent consumers are explicit still-open DB lifecycle obligation in partial038. Source-level Core contract does not claim all callers refresh correctly."], "explicit_dependencies": "DB cache all mutation/refresh paths and receiving consumers plus StrategicEquipment/held projection remain exact pending07 roles. No stale table defect claimed from lazy-refresh comment or rg references alone.", "findings": "No new confirmed07 defect in pure Core evaluator; DB lifecycle not yet classified.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep canonical evaluation functions and distinct party aggregation policies; any retained capability cache must have explicit current dependency generation/refresh semantics. No source/later-lens credit beyond listed Core variants.", "status": "exact Core source07 inventory complete; explicit receiver lifecycle pending"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-039", "at": "2026-10-22T20:09:29.185554+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope022_index": 79, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "eb7dbfbe0a6f8fa81675d14434401b41bc0949b693b56338129c6c778af82284", "actual_EOF": 1137, "material_ranges": [[1, 1137]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/79"}, {"scope022_index": 891, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "7d00629a7da937cf41b5bc49a86df7119cc7054743dce1f70ac2507a7aba59b0", "actual_EOF": 1137, "material_ranges": [[1, 1137]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/891"}, {"scope022_index": 892, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/armor.rs", "sha256": "3aeb6961c084a063132b1d1302d006c8cbf59cacaf960081e799b7ce46d37930", "actual_EOF": 138, "material_ranges": [[1, 138]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/892"}], "additional_source": {"source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/armor.rs", "sha256": "3aeb6961c084a063132b1d1302d006c8cbf59cacaf960081e799b7ce46d37930", "actual_EOF": 138, "material_ranges": [[1, 138]], "registration": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-REG004", "source_status": "fresh full actualbody after prospective registration; global queue delta pending; not counted in current2772"}, "actual_source_proof": "Fresh current PRcombat1-513 and complete P16actualdiff1137; personally consumed actual full-source facts CAMERA-ADM03-068 including all existing514-1137 fixture source and reanalyzed07 semantics, no admission verdict credit. Fresh full PRarmor138 and prospectively registered P16armor138 then complete actual counterpart comparison: same canonical partition/classification/current caller meaning, not equalhash credit. Fresh actual main588-624 item-contact recipient.", "contracts": ["Combat starting condition removes strategic pain/blood contributions once, then current battle incapacitation recomputes pain and remaining blood from live damage/current integral. This is deliberate strategic baseline\u2192transient authority handoff, not independent accumulating old+new penalty. Imbalance recovery derives current value, no separate recovered flag. Health damage returns actual applied amount after clamp, separating requested from applied.", "AttackResult represents resolved contact/effects, distinct from later clamped body health. Physical-contact bool on ToAttacker differentiates cleanmiss/dodge from physical equipment interception even when scalar work differs. ToDefender damage channels and contact force are related but not identical (edge/blunt transfer, unarmed injury scale, armor resistance). No simple total-damage field stored for independent mutation in actual factory.", "Armor solver constructs one contact observation from actual chosen surface, incident energy/precision and attack quality. Resisted/transmitted/penetrated partition conserves incident via one equation; cut/blunt return components copy actual penetration/transmission for downstream injury conversion. They are coordinated output projections, not independently authored tables. Surface stores physical material/resistance/padding provenance while observed energy depends incident/precision too; native raw field admission issues remain separately open.", "ArmorImpact.outcome Penetrated depends positive penetration, otherwise Deflected depends attack<1 versus Stopped. Complete outcome cannot derive solely from stored energy partition because attack quality is not retained. AttackResult::Mul scales effect channels/contact/three impact energies together while preserving surface/outcome. Safe multiply0 can therefore preserve original Penetrated label with0 energy; normal exchange post-resolution performance/power scaling exists. Actual current main retains impact as log/contact identity and selects contacted item from surface, not by recomputing current damage from outcome. This is explicitly original-contact-versus-scaled-effect semantic qualification, not proven two live authority bug; no new finding or forced reclassification policy. Root independently confirms no contrary existing04 classification proof.", "Ranged and melee use shared defense/armor/damage path rather than separate durability/health policy. Ranged miss has no attacker balance penalty intentionally; native zero contact returns ToAttacker with no physical contact. Strength/weapon inertia/precision and region capacity are distinct authored calibrations, with health derived fresh from energy. apportion computes current applied cut/blunt shares from actual clamped health once, preserving conserved applied total.", "Contact/health telemetry retains historical contact and later applied effects together; before/after health not interchangeable with energy. Existing actual fixture source covers precision4, armor padding/gaps, unarmed force/imbalance and energy conservation; source evidence only, no runtime/new assertions. Raw precision panic/energy admission and surface propagation remain prior findings, not cleared by coordinate arithmetic."], "explicit_dependencies": "Other combat child modules/contact geometry/defense/fatigue/wounds/targeting, underlying equipment and morale canonical policies remain own07 scope. P16armor exact newly registered source pending globaldelta; no unrelatedP16geometry/SDK authority inferred.", "findings": "No new07 finding from post-resolution outcome retention without stronger same-current-fact semantics; existingF008/F009 and prior admission/operation findings preserved.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one authoritative contact partition and explicit stage/provenance for scaled effects. Connected representation repair should make contact observation versus applied effect clear without deleting real armor/health distinctions or inventing finite-all-native policy. Source frozen.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory; additional source awaiting global accounting"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-040", "at": "2026-10-22T20:10:50.509959+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope022_index": 81, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/contact_geometry.rs", "sha256": "49172abd688b3e643d98f8214b92848a339da49622b13331988449baffcb93f5", "actual_EOF": 489, "material_ranges": [[1, 489]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/81"}, {"scope022_index": 82, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/contact_timing.rs", "sha256": "3b347473e5083f9fd02f59949b49f45eb7bf03e75c288b167cf003e2acc6ca89", "actual_EOF": 57, "material_ranges": [[1, 57]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/82"}, {"scope022_index": 895, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/contact_geometry.rs", "sha256": "8be98e18f4aa0d7bb6fbc302c7a10e6df912a744927240f6a4618ce41541e75f", "actual_EOF": 488, "material_ranges": [[1, 488]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/895"}, {"scope022_index": 896, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/combat/contact_timing.rs", "sha256": "3b347473e5083f9fd02f59949b49f45eb7bf03e75c288b167cf003e2acc6ca89", "actual_EOF": 57, "material_ranges": [[1, 57]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-022.json#/files/896"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh all current PR contact_geometry488, first combined output truncated and explicitly recovered PR411-488 plus entire P16production difference1-304. Full actual test differences were observed in first output; checked fixture conversions/Result only. P16actual489 uses typed SignedLength and completed native result readmission; actual current role comparison preserves error boundaries. Fresh PRtiming57+complete P16diff empty with same signed contact-time role compared.", "contracts": ["Scheduled measure is historical commitment, actual measure is current contact gap, ideal measure is authored preferred band; current source test explicitly changes scheduled only and observes identical ideal/accuracy. They intentionally do not collapse to one current distance. Grip/total/head dimensions and selected material are independent geometry facts, not interchangeable reach aliases.", "Classification/material/lever/energyfraction/accuracy and optional invalidation cause are constructed together from actual facts at contact instant. No mutation method updates a single retained derived field after source geometry change in these source paths. InvalidGeometry/OutsideReach classify actual input failure, while IntendedSurface/Haft/Pommel preserve current physical sub-surface and use different material; shortened reach changes energy and handling, not an independent hit oracle.", "has_distal_striking_surface derives exact length/material predicate; actual CombatWeapon separately stores distal_headed so F008 remains. Contact facts deliberately receive that choice and current helper does not prove it matches all supplied dimensions after public mutation. Canonical selected owner F009 must propagate through this whole fact bundle, no independent conversion-only fix.", "Energyfraction depends squared actual/intended lever ratio; measure_accuracy depends ideal deviation and style/head tolerance. Those are different physical effects and cannot be collapsed because both are dimensionless. Intended helper is explicit conventional full-contact observation, not actual revalidation of arbitrary geometry; preserve original callers which supply this unvalidated observation under native policy and keep admission/aggregate issue separate.", "HUMANOID minimum-center separation derives2*canonical radius. Fresh direct existing scoped PR receivers: tactical server player_projection2150-2152 uses same Core radius for cylinder; tactical CharacterDimensions42-64 default uses same Core reference arm reach. This is shared authority rather than duplicate numerical literals. Actual per-instance dimensions remain tactical fact; generic autoresolve reference fallback explicitly documented when no per-instance dimensions. No full player source credit or inferred variable-height/collider consistency.", "ContactTimingOffset retains one finite signed difference in seconds; between_contacts derives own-incoming coordinates in actual order, negative means earlier not invalid elapsed duration. Native Duration conversion is nonnegative authoritative-clock difference projection, not a second stored coordinate. No cached own/incoming timestamps inside offset; current BattleTime remains distinct origin.", "Existing geometry tests document continuous energy across head/haft, low-energy pommel, inside-vs-outside spatial miss and authored ideal independent scheduling. Source evidence only, no tests run/added. Public raw composite fields/Serde admit correlations broader than factory and remain aggregate/admission findings, not automatically a normal stale-current mutation."], "supporting_reads": [{"source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/player.rs", "sha256": "7950d432247add4cf942e8eaf9a0dfeed6199326e4518094a1d616d1cd89a645", "ranges": [[42, 80]], "whole_source_credit": false}, {"source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/player_projection.rs", "sha256": "53a298dded98b5419e757b7b6ae3907346d3e566b5d4210be7329834d2b5e331", "ranges": [[2142, 2156]], "whole_source_credit": false}], "findings": "F008/F009 retained; no new07 stale-current classification from coordinated contact observation.", "explicit_dependencies": "All actual tactical dimension/collider construction/update paths retain own07 source inventory; bounded shared-constant receiver proof is not whole caller clearance. Native ContactPrecision/targeting/source geometry still own sources.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Carry one selected geometry authority and explicit scheduled/current/ideal roles; keep contact projections coordinated and preserve canonical radius/reference-arm ownership. No source or later-lens edits.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory complete"}
