{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-052", "at": "2026-10-22T20:32:44.385949+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope025_index": 97, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter.rs", "sha256": "aad69b12c6ade6caa59828876caede30c0a0fe2577b11fdd91f84594d2471dd5", "actual_EOF": 1019, "material_ranges": [[1, 1019]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/97"}, {"scope025_index": 98, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter/choice.rs", "sha256": "3a327aeb8ec9f72d67960b0cdc94f7ece677c4a963d5ce8e1db7af3fd8025206", "actual_EOF": 72, "material_ranges": [[1, 72]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/98"}, {"scope025_index": 99, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter/receipt.rs", "sha256": "79edfeebdc4b5bdd4dfd8272b5b15981bf986c1acdcc4bca4b92d3fe3022b1b1", "actual_EOF": 36, "material_ranges": [[1, 36]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/99"}, {"scope025_index": 917, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter.rs", "sha256": "aad69b12c6ade6caa59828876caede30c0a0fe2577b11fdd91f84594d2471dd5", "actual_EOF": 1019, "material_ranges": [[1, 1019]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/917"}, {"scope025_index": 918, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter/choice.rs", "sha256": "3a327aeb8ec9f72d67960b0cdc94f7ece677c4a963d5ce8e1db7af3fd8025206", "actual_EOF": 72, "material_ranges": [[1, 72]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/918"}, {"scope025_index": 919, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/encounter/receipt.rs", "sha256": "79edfeebdc4b5bdd4dfd8272b5b15981bf986c1acdcc4bca4b92d3fe3022b1b1", "actual_EOF": 36, "material_ranges": [[1, 36]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/919"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed current03 CAMERA-ADM03-083 actual full body/test facts; freshly read PR encounter1-620 plus full choice72/receipt36 and complete actual PR/P16 body differences for all three sources (empty). Reanalyzed authoritative producer/state/receiver meaning under07; no prior verdict carry. Remaining encounter621-1019 existing test bodies rely on explicit current03 full-source facts, no new execution.", "contracts": ["EncounterContext is an input snapshot. EncounterSelection stores same-boundary randomized rolls, computed Awareness, archetype/count, minute/index as event evidence, rather than retaining a live awareness cache. context_at and problem_at are sampled at the same canonical boundary200-213; actual selection232-322 constructs all related output values together. Future party speed/membership changes do not retroactively rewrite this event history. DB accepted-state and current response preconditions remain separately inventoried.", "Archetype.enemy_speed delegates canonical Threat profile76-78. Ecological forward weight344-355, primary archetype mapping67-74, quest attraction267-278 and local-problem attraction279-290 represent different selection factors; no alternative cached enemy speed. Weight vector slot mapping is a repeated closed three-archetype roster, currently aligned at262-266/270-274/282-286/336-340; potential future membership/order strengthening, not a current contradictory selection or a new functional defect.", "available_choices162-184 derives current permitted choices from awareness/archetype/speed, rather than persisting an independently mutable eligibility bool. Run permission126-128 delegates profile speed. Strategic sustainable speed133-159 is a separate overland policy from tactical movement/incapacitation; numerical overlap does not establish duplicate authority.", "Awareness stores the historical classified outcome and rolls; rolls alone are insufficient to recompute without the sampled context/perception. A raw public literal can be inconsistent, but this is not evidence of two normal producing routes disagreeing; actual constructor304-322 coordinates them. sneak_succeeds uses separate random domains intentionally, not a second stale awareness result. Existing overflow findings remain admission/operation concerns, not invented07 cache bugs.", "Narrative travel/rest boundaries, chance and trigger membership are different event types. Source catalogue owns definitions; candidates526-550 are derived fresh for each query and sorted by ID; selected catalog_id is a captured event reference, not an independently authored copied description/weight. Catalogue live revisions/DB use must be compared at their own source roles, not assumed from this helper.", "EncounterChoice stable_id is the only token mapping; FromStr iterates variants and calls it, so no duplicated inverse mapping as in F010. The explicit complete variant list can be derived mechanically but currently contains all five. Tests repeat expected tokens as regression evidence, not another live parser. Opaque encounter ID is one deterministic native text projection from two domain-separated words; retry helper compares request evidence exactly, it does not create a second owner or authenticate raw text."], "findings": [], "qualifications": "No duplicate live encounter authority proven in these exact Core contracts. Existing raw aggregate admission, score overflow and DB receipt/provenance findings remain. Repeated roster listing is a membership-strengthening opportunity without current disagreement; not a claim that intentional subsets must become the full enum.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Retain canonical profile-derived speed, one token mapping and explicit immutable boundary snapshots; derive complete closed roster where intended instead of maintaining ordered identity arrays. Do not replace historical event observations with current recomputation.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory complete with qualifications; no source edits or other lens credit"}
