#/files/921"}, {"scope025_index": 2776, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/equipment/armor.rs", "sha256": "1eb52192b9ef4b1d23b4a696a3f4b370baf3076b3184e4b576ec681f426e47f1", "actual_EOF": 94, "material_ranges": [[1, 39]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-025.json#/files/2776"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed substantive current03 CAMERA-ADM03-077/079 full source/test facts, then freshly read PR equipment1-673 in bounded chunks (truncated602-644 recovered explicitly), full timing97, P16 parametric geometry65 and all94 armor. Complete actual PR/P16 differences for equipment/timing and parametric declarations/constructors compared; geometry typed length substitutions preserve each actual meaning. PR parametric66 first display uncredited, then registered REG006 before fresh full reread. PR armor40-94 first display uncredited, REG007 then fresh bounded reread; PR1-39 remains Rig015 existing role. No fresh literal claim for equipment existing675-1182 tests; actual current03 full-source facts reanalyzed for07.", "contracts": ["EquipmentGraph retains one node->placement graph. Children/occupied cells/edge keys/ancestors are derived per operation, not separately mutable cached sets. equip215-278 performs all checks against a local proposed placement then inserts once; unequip281-286 rejects children before removing. Direct public map writes remain admission/encapsulation exposure, not evidence of a second normal graph authority. Point capacity/source fit remains actual higher-caller responsibility, not inferred from this structural graph.", "InputAddressMapping keyboard row/column and input labels are intentionally two UI coordinates describing one action layout; table50-195 owns this mapping. Many-to-many locations and outside-to-inside channels describe selection traversal, not a second live occupancy graph. Actual channel canonical order and downstream UI bindings require their own source-role comparison; tests checking disjoint cells are evidence, not mechanical removal of policy duplication.", "WeaponSkillDistribution field order, SKILLS365-375 and weights377-389 repeat nine fixed identity positions; all currently agree. weighted_check426-431 joins them by zip, so adding/reordering one alone can silently associate a weight with another skill. Treat as source membership/order strengthening under the same F011 family, not a claimed current wrong authored distribution. total/melee/ranged totals and validity are derived immediately, not retained competing sums; UNARMED is deliberate bludgeon calibration.", "EncumbranceSummary retains physical burden and capacity, computes remaining/penalty on request. Combined summaries use the same saturating finite-nonnegative native rule; remaining versus penalty are complementary observations, not independently stored flags. Carrying capacity derives canonical lower-muscle/leg-strength policy; one encumbrance contribution to incapacitation remains intentional, and no fatigue movement penalty added here.", "PlayerEquipment is an interface with neutral/limited defaults, not a blanket certificate that every implementation has authored timing/geometry. The shared timing function derives preparation/recovery together from physical inertia/style/unarmed status, without an independent weapon-family cadence table. Default0.3 values for implementations with no realtime pacing are a different declared fallback role; actual tactical clients/server must be compared for delegation, not cleared by interface documentation alone.", "WearableProtection is an actual layer snapshot; LayeredArmor is a derived whole-body-part aggregate; ArmorSurface is a single intersected contact surface/native observation. aggregate_layered_armor53-81 combines current pieces while outermost_wearable86-94 selects one wear recipient with deterministic order. The aggregate resistance/coverage and selected item identity/material are not the same fact. DB capability storing aggregate physics alongside outermost identity/coverage requires exact downstream contact comparison and remains partial038; this Core inventory does not clear that parent.", "Parametric geometry preserves total length versus grip-to-tip versus distinct head length as separate geometrical facts; melee_reach is a getter for controlling grip length, not another stored reach. Factory checks correlated positive/order conditions but public field mutation remains the existing03 gap. balance is retained alongside mass/inertia/grip; actual authored weapon119-123 and starting_character915-919 derive handling from canonical helper439-453, while this geometry constructor accepts a supplied value. Do not assert every generic balance input has identical derivation until the actual per-instance producer/recipient policy is compared. This is an explicit same-fact candidate for upcoming DB/client roles, not a proven normal divergence.", "conditioned_precision retains base per-instance geometry and applies current condition as an explicit ratio at59-64; base catalogue precision and effective conditioned precision represent different epochs/roles. Its provenance/lookup expect remains prior03 finding, not evidence that catalogue and instance precision must be numerically identical."], "findings": [], "qualification": "New local REG006 PR geometry1-66 and REG007 PR armor40-94 have substantive fresh proofs here but await global scope reconciliation; no source count from their registration. PR armor coverage row credits existing1-39 only until overlay integrated. Catalogue projection122 and current starting_character890-929/autoresolve authored98-127 were actual bounded supporting reads, no whole parent/source credit. Geometry balance dependency and DB capability038 remain explicit.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Prefer one skill-identity keyed representation where all nine complete entries are intended; derive transient totals, occupancy and cadence. Keep independent physical dimensions, layer aggregation/contact observations and historical snapshots distinct. Any cached instance handling must bind all actual dependencies to one owner and update atomically; no speculative raw equality imposed.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventory complete with qualified dependencies; no source edits or later lens credit"}
