surementKind distinguishes whether an empty recoverable object remains; the source explicitly documents adapter supplying the measured object kind snapshot130-132. The optional remaining amount and required instance basis are validated together, not a separate unchecked has_contents flag. Raw public combinations remain prior03 state-admission concerns, but normal kernel rejects contradictory basis/quantity before calculation.", "Effective mass and intrinsic value use one prorating helper and shared immutable basis. Intrinsic value differs from merchant price; factor composition and floor/ceil purchase/sale policy are applied once to a whole line. Aggregation is transient, ratio reduction derives equivalent numerical coordinates, and no second cached quoted-price field is authored in this module. Error enum is diagnostic output, not duplicate live accounting.", "Existing tests encode conservation and rounding expectations as source evidence. Header persistent schema not implemented yet is historical documentation, not a reason to ignore actual current DB consumers of fractions; those receiver sources remain separately inventoried with F027 and related admission findings preserved."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one immutable instance measurement basis and current remaining amount, derive effective mass/value and final merchant quote from correct epoch. Strengthening admitted aggregate routes must preserve stock/recipe distinctions, zero-valid fraction and one-rounding policy.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with source-specific nonapplicability; no repairs or other lens credit"}
