{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-062", "at": "2026-10-22T20:46:02.210826+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 113, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog.rs", "sha256": "12a6191433c61dae833826429a9ebacc2c043cce0fe593831e65f6ec10a132f6", "actual_EOF": 544, "material_ranges": [[1, 544]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/113"}, {"scope026_index": 114, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog_physical_serde.rs", "sha256": "f260cac7fddd136d2fd754e6f147a3fcecaa67eb107b87d506121e3c60016671", "actual_EOF": 18, "material_ranges": [[1, 18]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/114"}, {"scope026_index": 115, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog_projection.rs", "sha256": "771a265b992561a0094e1b16784b8ca544e4192546e3f06396d35b4bde8b3e30", "actual_EOF": 122, "material_ranges": [[1, 122]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/115"}, {"scope026_index": 937, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog.rs", "sha256": "de7dd72013aa3af8ae0aae8691011a8aaa2d168db670188bcc1064cac9a23d18", "actual_EOF": 614, "material_ranges": [[1, 614]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/937"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual source-specific Rig current03 contracts048/049/050/052 all narratives, including original full catalogue test facts. Fresh PR catalogue production1-203 plus existing test source204-290, complete actual PR/P16 catalogue diff, full P16 projection122 already fresh in current07 supporting053 and reanalyzed current role, fresh full physical Serde18. Fresh exact PR main validator499-507/886-903/1076-1103/1210-1260 provides authored-versus-derived counterqualification, no whole validator07 credit.", "contracts": ["Catalogue and source map are private once-initialized immutable vectors. Their lookups and authored-document order views derive from that same backing; metadata source coordinates deliberately differ from ID-sort lookup order. Production does not read loose files, and source-map diagnostic strings preserve authored provenance rather than becoming a second definition authority. There is no supported current mutation/hot reload requiring a per-entry invalidation key in these exact APIs.", "Generated melee projection updates precision/reach/inertia/mass and physical grip/Y before publishing the entire sorted vector into OnceLock. P16 fallible projection prevents publication on geometry/recipe error; PR fail-fast initialization also publishes only the completed closure. A partially projected local vector is not a second observable cached generation. Raw public ItemDefinition clones remain broader; this does not prove arbitrary external decoder output is validated.", "Authored coverage and melee precision must NOT be called ignored duplicate authoring here: actual main499-503 and891-895 rejects explicit scalar coverage, and1081-1086 rejects explicit melee precision. Their default DTO slots are filled from canonical surfaces/recipe. Armor body-part average coverage versus exact occupied anatomical spans remains an intentionally lossy aggregate, not an alternative hit geometry oracle. Zero/empty placement projection is handled explicitly.", "Melee reach/inertia remain required finite raw source fields1076-1078 and mass/grip/Y belong raw item physical DTO, but runtime loader overwrites those coordinates from the generated recipe before normal catalogue access. These accepted input slots can diverge from final runtime values; the same authored-mirror issue asF005 applies only to these exact still-editable fields. Do not include forbidden scalar coverage/precision in that claim. Distinguish raw source evidence from the compiled generated-weapon representation so the recipe alone owns its derived physical properties. No proof of two live resolvers consuming different values or current bad mesh is asserted.", "P16 physical array Serde is an actual native boundary over the same checked Cuboid backing; axis array serialization does not introduce another persistent dimensions owner. Projection changes only intended Y while preserving authored X/Z, whose placeholder geometry purpose is documented in schema; do not require equality to all detailed mesh extents without an actual contract.", "revision returns the compiled catalogue digest while physical synthesis also reads generated design/contact policy. Cross-process persistent receiver caches must be compared for all actual inputs before treating that digest as a complete physical generation key. This is an explicit future receiver obligation, not a current cache bug from a process-static value. Existing build/source-map and physical-output admission findings remain separate."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "One compiled generated-weapon projection should derive physical data from its recipe; keep raw authoring/diagnostics separate and remove ignored editable coordinates from the generated-melee input variant where appropriate. Preserve atomic publication, P16 typed failures, intentional authored placeholder axes and aggregate-versus-contact distinction. Actual persistent cache users remain independently inventoried.", "status": "exact listed current07 sources complete with qualified migration opportunity; no implementation/other lens credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-063", "at": "2026-10-22T20:46:02.210826+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 116, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog_schema.rs", "sha256": "115d9400063d89f5782dc3c34be2b9f2af774ca438768a9059f815b531d71b1f", "actual_EOF": 623, "material_ranges": [[1, 623]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/116"}, {"scope026_index": 939, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_catalog_schema.rs", "sha256": "96546aef4b24312d582f896fd925045cf4e37dd0eed7229d063e659f2ffa3013", "actual_EOF": 618, "material_ranges": [[1, 618]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/939"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual source-specific Rig current03 contracts051/053 full schema/source-test narratives. Fresh P16 definitions1-200/380-557 and complete actual PR counterpart body diff; remaining topology/book/material capability declarations and existing tests are explicit full-source facts from051/053 reanalyzed current07, not blanket Serde or old verdict. Actual receiving projection/current07 053/057/062 compared for retained-state roles.", "contracts": ["ItemKind describes base gameplay kind while capabilities provide composition; an Ingredient or Simple item can legitimately carry food/alcohol/book capability. Equipment topology also applies independently to simple accessories, containers, armor and weapons. Do not derive all capabilities/topology from a flat kind or treat these orthogonal facts as duplicates. Current missing-required-capability admission finding remains separate from this design distinction.", "Body material and striking material are distinct physical parts; attachment tags define allowed parent relationships and must not be inferred from item kind. Parent requirements, body occupancy, layer precedence exceptions, protected body parts and visible anatomical surface spans each describe different topology/coverage relationships. The schema deliberately states locations do not imply protection.", "outermost_channel computes from the current placement occupancy/parents and canonical EquipmentChannel.order, no cached order field. Per-entry order handles repetitions within a channel, not a second absolute channel-rank authority. Input-address OUTSIDE_TO_INSIDE list from053 differs for Containment; exact receiver comparison is still required before calling selection priority a physical-order defect.", "WeaponHandling required hands differs from carried slot and WeaponCarry sheathability; melee/ranged capability differs from skill-weight distribution, because mixed weapons and handling contexts are valid. Generic raw schema fields do not prove their correlations, but separate concepts must not be collapsed by numeric or name similarity.", "WeaponSkills repeats the same nine numerical fields copied by WeaponSkillDistribution; current From copies field-by-field while weighted_check uses positional list, so one canonical identity-indexed owner could remove source roster drift (F011 support053). Raw authored DTO may remain text/numerical input; retained compiled entries should preserve canonical skill identity.", "Food class string versus typed FoodClass remains057 migration opportunity. Book target typed languages/religion/bestiary versus open terrain/skill ID is an explicit vocabulary boundary; actual book-catalogue validation/receiver must own canonical membership, not derive it from display text. Durability quality/physical yield/fracture/wear/failure fractions represent distinct condition inputs, not independently stored current condition.", "Schema defaults represent neutral/absent authoring input and do not create a second current source of truth. Derived coverage and melee precision default fields are filled by canonical projection, with explicit authorship rejection proven062. Native Spacetime unit codecs and physical axis codec preserve exact shapes; they do not define an alternative gameplay owner."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep source DTOs separate from a coherent compiled catalogue, propagate canonical purpose-specific identities through retained records, and derive only values proven to represent the same fact. Preserve composition, topology, material distinctions, native codecs and actual raw diagnostics.", "status": "exact full schema current07 inventories complete with qualifications; no source edits or other lens credit"}
