nt distinct admissible sign domains; PositiveSpeed composes the nonnegative owner and adds zero exclusion. Each retains one actual scalar coordinate, getters/native conversions expose that coordinate, and sign/magnitude/nonnegative-part derive views instead of retaining separately mutable magnitude or moving flags. No speed/direction cache is constructed.", "checked_scale/lerp re-admit the completed result through one constructor; min/max choose existing admitted operands. TryFrom and Serde delegate the same constructors; the unit/sign policies are not independently reimplemented wire tables. Different native error formatting and scalar value are separate. No7 redundant live authority found in these exact leaves."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve one scalar backing and delegation, distinct sign/zero contracts and same concrete owners through all reexports; no duplicate wrapper solely for a new import path.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with source-specific nonapplicability"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-065", "at": "2026-10-22T20:47:38.199786+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 120, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission.rs", "sha256": "998416982a504559c519dabf8fecf7612eb946283441b9644c073ac500a62e62", "actual_EOF": 106, "material_ranges": [[1, 106]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/120"}, {"scope026_index": 121, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission/enemy_roster.rs", "sha256": "c83ace93cc95cb243c86bf6bc02bea9954953b433db0ab7790ea890ac7251642", "actual_EOF": 96, "material_ranges": [[1, 96]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/121"}, {"scope026_index": 122, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission/roster.rs", "sha256": "2b4baf6c921fd489d497a5f002c8ee5a84e48014c6932e1bd4153754501759dd", "actual_EOF": 91, "material_ranges": [[1, 91]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/122"}, {"scope026_index": 955, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission.rs", "sha256": "998416982a504559c519dabf8fecf7612eb946283441b9644c073ac500a62e62", "actual_EOF": 106, "material_ranges": [[1, 106]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/955"}, {"scope026_index": 956, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission/enemy_roster.rs", "sha256": "c83ace93cc95cb243c86bf6bc02bea9954953b433db0ab7790ea890ac7251642", "actual_EOF": 96, "material_ranges": [[1, 96]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/956"}, {"scope026_index": 957, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/mission/roster.rs", "sha256": "2b4baf6c921fd489d497a5f002c8ee5a84e48014c6932e1bd4153754501759dd", "actual_EOF": 91, "material_ranges": [[1, 91]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/957"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full P16 mission106/enemy roster96/party roster91 including all existing tests; complete actual PR differences empty and each constructor, read operation, receipt-domain role and native count recipient compared. Original false EOF114 stays qualified to actual106; no nonexistent credit. Actual current03 facts088 used only for preserved decoding findings.", "contracts": ["Captured party/enemy ID lists are the sole backing membership authority. Public scalar expected_members/enemy_count are derived each call from private immutable vectors and actual checked lengths; they are not separately maintained stored counts. Consuming extraction transfers the whole list, immutable access cannot silently alter its count. Source uniqueness sets are temporary constructor checks.", "Party participation count limit16 is an authenticated receipt transport bound; hostile cardinality has only representable-u32/nonempty bound and is intentionally not16-limited. Applying the same participant scalar to enemies would erase the distinct ownership policy. ID0 and input ordering are deliberate source semantics.", "MissionId, BattleId, HostileGroupId and OutcomeSourceId bind different entities/associations, despite sharing ASCII grammar implementation. Macro keeps one grammar implementation with exact prefixes as input, rather than four drifting string validators. Their transparent Serde admission bypass remains a concrete earlier finding; it is not a competing normal identity authority created by a formatter.", "HostileGroupBinding Unbound versus Bound is one enum state, not parallel has-group flag plus optional ID. Victor versus prebound hostile resolution represents battle outcome and strategic consequence, not synonyms; actual terminal DB/server association and request replay policy require separate source inventory. Receipt limit constants are one policy source here; equality to other future native constants requires actual recipient comparison."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep immutable captured rosters and derive transport counts from them at actual ports; preserve distinct mission/battle/group/outcome identity meaning and live-capture provenance. Fix constructor/decoder route findings within their own connected graph; no synthetic stored count or duplicate membership cache.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete, actual database/live membership dependency explicit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-066", "at": "2026-10-22T20:47:38.199786+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 123, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/morale.rs", "sha256": "f902bb0b1067c0247c8309ac84bd8bb4af3ea9443be399780e82223ebf122750", "actual_EOF": 527, "material_ranges": [[1, 527]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/123"}, {"scope026_index": 958, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/morale.rs", "sha256": "f902bb0b1067c0247c8309ac84bd8bb4af3ea9443be399780e82223ebf122750", "actual_EOF": 527, "material_ranges": [[1, 527]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/958"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed current03 CAMERA-ADM03-091 actual full P16527 and existing tests, freshly read P16 production1-325; complete actual PR body diff empty and current event/source/derived impairment/cache roles compared. Remaining physiological formula/test source facts are explicit same current source proof, not reused verdict.", "contracts": ["Durable MoraleEventKind and current MoraleSourceKind are distinct taxonomies: current sources include ongoing injury/cleanliness/religion/power/ally while events describe historical occurrences. Exhaustive From maps historical events into current contributor kinds; it does not imply current sources can all be converted back to events.", "Manual MoraleEventKind.as_str and IncapacitationStatus.as_str repeat their Serde snake-case wire spellings, currently equal. They support F010 source-vocabulary strengthening only; human prose and source/event taxonomy remain separate. Display delegates status.as_str, so no third independently maintained status formatter.", "StrategicIncapacitation retains seven actual persistent-contributor inputs and derives total/status/check_multiplier on request. It stores no independent total or Ready flag that can become stale after component update. One fatigue contribution and separate pain/blood/fear/needs/thermal are intentional; transient combat imbalance/knockdown remain tactical. Raw nonfinite total can misclassify Ready under prior03 finding, not a second live classifier with different current formula.", "Morale resolution combines positive and negative effect magnitudes differently using Will; signed morale is not an unsigned unit score. Ally bonus explicitly uses pre-bonus surplus to avoid recursive current feedback, a distinct epoch from post-bonus morale. Source DB must preserve that distinction; function itself retains no cache.", "Mastery enjoyment uses starting interval value plus decayed prior history and new excess hours to produce one endpoint award; event age/duration decay helpers are pure policy functions, not retained alternative current morale values. Similar linear decay formulas alone do not prove independent event types must have identical future policy. Religious discord, fervor, neglect costs and incapacity components represent different mechanical/observer facts, not duplicate conviction counters."], "findings": [], "qualification": "Current07 does not clear DB persisted summaries/event caches or wheel receiver projections. Existing NaN/admission and total>1/display100% policies remain preserved. No new hidden penalty, fatigue pool or pre-incapacitation movement rule introduced.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep current morale/impairment totals derived from explicit input epoch; one native vocabulary owner can supply matching serializations. Preserve event history versus current sources, pre-bonus surplus, signed/over100% values and tactical authority boundary.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with qualifications"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-067", "at": "2026-10-22T20:49:18.375997+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 124, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/npc_policy.rs", "sha256": "51c449efd5edf6380249bcc04ebf5a9a38cc9a1f20cab731e2bf80d6b958e18a", "actual_EOF": 296, "material_ranges": [[1, 296]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/124"}, {"scope026_index": 959, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/npc_policy.rs", "sha256": "51c449efd5edf6380249bcc04ebf5a9a38cc9a1f20cab731e2bf80d6b958e18a", "actual_EOF": 296, "material_ranges": [[1, 296]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/959"}, {"scope026_index": 126, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/personality.rs", "sha256": "3251416fba119a8dbdfb3ce1f48abfd7bda014d55dd3ec2b3e38e4dd7e3e9b15", "actual_EOF": 202, "material_ranges": [[1, 202]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/126"}, {"scope026_index": 962, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/personality.rs", "sha256": "3251416fba119a8dbdfb3ce1f48abfd7bda014d55dd3ec2b3e38e4dd7e3e9b15", "actual_EOF": 202, "material_ranges": [[1, 202]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/962"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual full current03 CAMERA-ADM03-093 NPC296/personality202 source/test facts; fresh P16 NPC1-211 and full personality202, complete actual PR body diffs empty, each selection/provenance/personality policy role compared. NPC212-296 existing tests rely on the explicit original full body proof, no execution.", "contracts": ["NpcCandidate is an identity+policy-seed snapshot; stable_candidate_order rejects same identity with conflicting seed before deduplicating identical snapshots. Random rank is recomputed from actor/day/candidate coordinates, not a retained competing candidate-priority cache. Seed and durable identity are distinct provenance/entropy roles, not two interchangeable IDs.", "NpcCourtshipEligibility is an adapter-supplied current snapshot of independent biological/social/location/permission facts. It computes Formal/Informal/Ineligible once by explicit precedence, not separate cached flags owned here. bool input admission/authentication and later DB selection-before-time advance remain caller obligations, not certified by public raw structs. Housing comfort rank versus actual initial/recurring budget costs are independent concepts; derived affordability does not retain another funds balance.", "Initial NPC schedule is one saved initial plan, not a permanently competing default recomputed each refresh. NPC_SCHEDULE_QUANTUM_MINUTES13 and literal15 at128 currently agree but the generator does not delegate to its named quantum constant; same unit-policy derivation opportunity, not a current invalid schedule or reason to recompute edited NPC schedules. Canonical admitted allocation/quarter-hour owner remains separate lower source inventory.", "Personality axes are intentionally independent. neutral() chooses a concrete baseline across sex/presentation/inclination without making those independent axes redundant or requiring a fixed relation. non_neutral_count169-183 derives only thirteen temperament axes, deliberately excluding the three identity/attraction coordinates; no separately mutable count can go stale.", "Conviction.strength is one typed-axis mechanical projection; Presentation.stable_id lower-case matches Serde today while stable_variant_id uses Rust-style deterministic identity spelling for a different protocol purpose. Preserve exact bytes for both, do not collapse distinct wire/entropy vocabularies. Current native lower-case mapping supports F010 only where the declared protocol is actually the same."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Retain captured provenance and derived candidate ordering, one initial saved plan, independent personality axes and canonical quantum policy delegation where intended. Distinguish raw eligibility snapshot evidence from actual DB authority and preserve current RNG frames/selection order.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with qualifications"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-068", "at": "2026-10-22T20:49:18.375997+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 127, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/physical_object.rs", "sha256": "906e67eed5acc9fbf6ab98e2e4bc7df11b8e9742c1ee148092c7d2061f64afab", "actual_EOF": 383, "material_ranges": [[1, 383]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/127"}, {"scope026_index": 963, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/physical_object.rs", "sha256": "906e67eed5acc9fbf6ab98e2e4bc7df11b8e9742c1ee148092c7d2061f64afab", "actual_EOF": 383, "material_ranges": [[1, 383]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/963"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual current03 CAMERA-ADM03-094 full383 source and all existing tests. Fresh P16 definitions/operations1-331; complete actual PR body diff empty and all identity/custody/backing-location/transfer receiver roles compared. Remaining tests332-383 facts explicitly reused from actual prior full source, not verdict.", "contracts": ["PhysicalObjectId is explicitly the same stable InventoryObject.id coordinate, not a newly generated competing identifier. ObjectCustody keeps that identity fixed through consuming transfer and reconstructs custody via the same direct-self-containment guard; getters do not expose mutation. No separately cached owner label/count exists inside it.", "InventoryLocation is persisted backing storage association; OperationalCustody is the direct physical holder/location. Descendants can share carried backing row scope while direct custody names their container. These are deliberately different relationships; do not force every child custody to equal its carried inventory location or conflate a row ID with physical-object identity. Actual rehome/update operations must coordinate the projections at their own DB source roles.", "Custody says neither legal title nor access rights; Character/Party/Container/Place/Fixture are explicit distinct current physical states. Legal-owner history and rights decisions must not be deleted as redundant merely because they mention the same actor or place. Fixture custody differs from its containing place; matching carried inventory intentionally rejects both.", "InventoryLocation.scope/row_id/is_fireplace and has_same_carried_custody derive from one variant and its actual payload rather than retain independent kind/owner flags. Raw persisted record fields do not certify canonical checked IDs; prior03 strengthening/provenance findings remain.", "CarriedInventoryScope.as_str and TryFrom repeat the two lowercase URL/form keys, current agreement only; ordinary Serde uses intentionally different Personal/Party names. This is F010 inverse-mapping strengthening, not a request to silently change JSON protocol or eliminate rejected raw scope evidence."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one physical object identity, distinct backing inventory and direct custody relations, derive query flags from the state enum, and coordinate actual DB rehome paths. A canonical transport mapping may share inverse vocabulary while preserving distinct Serde protocol bytes.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete; actual persistence projection update graph remains separately inventoried"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-069", "at": "2026-10-22T20:51:24.378214+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope026_index": 125, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/organization.rs", "sha256": "cb410372fbb5a1f8b61fad2bf447bcd93512725560fb69338ec024ed3135b0e1", "actual_EOF": 1251, "material_ranges": [[1, 36], [88, 246], [316, 645]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-026.json#/files/125"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual current03 CAMERA-ADM03-095 exact P16 ranges and Native root-support/contracts-002.json#organization-open-content-versus-validatedcatalogue actual PR definitions1-635. Fresh P16 exact1-36/88-246/316-645 in two bounded reads. No P1637-87/247-315/646+ body coverage. PR direct37-87/247-315 supporting definitions separately read within existing PR scope; no whole PR960 accounting here, its original full-versus-bounded material scope query is explicit.", "contracts": ["OrganizationDefinition/roles/recognition/privileges and settlement-specific chapters are one authored content model, not institution-specific closed type tables. Role profession belongs to an organization instance; address priority differs deliberately from social precedence and from publicly recognizable role disclosure. A known private role must not automatically become public dialogue identity.", "Recognition may extend beyond chapter presence; base privileges and additive role privileges are distinct policy levels. Promotion transitions are queried from one canonical catalogue edge list; can_transition and promotion_targets derive from that same list and do not cache independent transition rules. Initial social assignment is a deliberate creation policy over authored role references, not inference from display/profession prose.", "OnceLock catalogue has one immutable embedded initialization, exact current lookups return shared references. has_chapter delegates chapter rather than maintain a presence flag; service chapter expect follows an actual same-object chapter filter. Source raw DTO acceptance remains prior03 issue; no second mutable runtime catalogue is established.", "Chapter stable institutional location differs explicitly from physical NPC service venue. chapter_effective_location_id derives current available service location or falls back to authored stable chapter identity; chapter_has_standalone_building derives from that result. Do not merge these coordinates or generate a new representative identity when co-location changes.", "Service native venue and availability matches548-579 repeat the same eight service keys, currently aligned, but each returns a different property. A shared typed service descriptor could remove a future one-sided membership edit; this is a bounded migration opportunity, not current divergence or proof all open organization IDs must become enums. Exact storefront/action availability predicates remain upcoming settlement_economy source obligations.", "Representative ID derives stable settlement+organization coordinates, deliberately independent of provider ordinal/physical venue. exact_representative_fields_match compares the same expected ID/home/org/conversation facts, not a second ID generator. Stable derived ID versus stored durable actor identity must remain coordinated by actual population/DB producer; helper itself stores no extra counter/flag."], "findings": [], "qualification": "Partial test context634-645 read as originally recorded; no complete test-function assertion or test646+ credit. organization starting-role definition and second-person helper outside P16 scope remain excluded despite PR supporting facts. Current07 does not infer runtime acceptance from compiled-message strings or clear actual DB membership caches.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one authored catalogue with derived current views, separate institutional identity from physical venue, preserve privacy and role-context distinctions, and propagate canonical service identifiers to both native property projections where appropriate.", "status": "exact listed bounded P16 source07 inventory complete with explicit lower receiver dependencies"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-070", "at": "2026-10-22T20:55:34.644767+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope027_index": 128, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/physiology.rs", "sha256": "58161910d9518bcdd9c32f0833899fe03e1ab544cfe745838dafbc81c23550bb", "actual_EOF": 1169, "material_ranges": [[1, 407], [447, 790], [850, 935]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-027.json#/files/128"}, {"scope027_index": 964, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/physiology.rs", "sha256": "58161910d9518bcdd9c32f0833899fe03e1ab544cfe745838dafbc81c23550bb", "actual_EOF": 1169, "material_ranges": [[1, 1169]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-027.json#/files/964"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual current03 CAMERA-ADM03-096 bounded P16 facts plus Native contract-groups-073 full currentPR1169/all tests. Fresh P16 actual1-407/447-788/850-929, including complete14 profile table487-655; exact full same-role PR differences empty for1-407/447-788/850-935. Fresh PR-only409-445/789-849/937-959 functions close its remaining full production roles. P16 excluded functions409-445/789-849/937-959 receive NO body credit; old789-790 signature/930-935 comment attributes remain context only. PR test961-1169 actual source facts explicitly reused, no new execution.", "contracts": ["Private physiological meters are authoritative simulation inputs; public humours are explicitly many-to-one projections and never treatment-selection inputs. humours/regional_humours/quantize/disclosure all derive from the same meter-to-humour weight table. Equal public readings intentionally do not imply equal causes, so four humours must not become a parallel reconstructed treatment state.", "Ten Meter, seven BodyRegion and four Humour enum order/ALL/count constants bind positional vectors/matrix rows. They currently agree; table HUMOUR_WEIGHTS comments encode the same row association and actual terminal tie-break uses Meter order. F011 source-order/member-binding strengthening applies: derive intended complete roster/count and explicit typed associations while preserving deterministic order and clinical versus tactical anatomical distinctions. This is not a current wrong index.", "Body mass owns one kg backing and derives estimated blood volume at the actual unit-specific70ml/kg conversion. Its DEFAULT70kg is unrelated to70ml/kg despite equal numbers. Dose owns milliunits and derives standard-dose magnitude/is_zero from one backing. Ruleset version, phenotype key version and intervention profile version name different revision namespaces, not copies of one version counter.", "Administration pins exact preparation/profile version, administered/stopped time and secret-derived sensitivity/adverse evidence for replay. current_intervention_profile finds latest only for a new course, exact lookup preserves old course semantics. Do not replace historical pinned profile/sensitivity with current recomputation after configuration/key changes. Recorded actual route versus profile required route is checked before effect; a mismatched route yields no effect rather than silently becoming the prescribed route.", "Clinical presence pins historical observer skill at the joint-clock boundary. Later training must not sharpen past readings. Chart readings, gaps and known intervention labels are notebook evidence rather than private causal state. Region/observer/day-specific noise is deliberate observation policy on PR full role; it is not another private meter or retained illness cache.", "InterventionProfile.preparation_id currently uses positional MEDICATION_IDS[0..13]. Exact array binding was freshly read in071, and all current identities align with the intended effects. One reordered reference list could silently reassign treatment effects because the profile table retains numeric indices rather than explicit semantic references; same F011 binding-strengthening family. Current source no wrong treatment claim.", "PR-only disease_meter_state and combined_meter_state derive current private state from curves/phenotype/actual administration effects; first_terminal_crossing derives an earliest event from actual state_at samples over structural boundaries. No separately mutable terminal flag exists here. This does not clear P16 excluded counterpart bodies or DB generated chronology reconciliation F012. Raw public vector, curve, span and chart admission findings remain separate."], "findings": [], "qualification": "P16 source role range record preserves original envelopes; actual material1-407/447-788/851-928, with789-790 and929-935 incidental upcoming declaration context uncredited. No P16 whole1169 claim; original curve/combined/noise lower roles remain outside its current material scope unless directly registered later. Full current DB treatment/terminal/notebook cache receivers remain separately inventoried.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one private causal state and derived public observations, immutable historical profile/observer bindings, canonical typed meter/region/member associations and single dose/mass unit backings. Do not merge lossy public humours with treatment authority or alter replay entropy/version ordering.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with qualified membership/order strengthening"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-071", "at": "2026-10-22T20:55:34.644767+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope027_index": 2744, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_references.rs", "sha256": "e794dc0ede51c9d53d64155ee9ce8d551347ec8f659e2461c0b3d5d31b34cb6b", "actual_EOF": 76, "material_ranges": [[12, 27], [30, 37]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-027.json#/files/2744"}, {"scope027_index": 946, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/item_references.rs", "sha256": "e794dc0ede51c9d53d64155ee9ce8d551347ec8f659e2461c0b3d5d31b34cb6b", "actual_EOF": 76, "material_ranges": [[1, 76]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-027.json#/files/946"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh exact P16 registered12-27/30-37 and full currentPR76 body; complete actual same-role counterpart differences empty. Actual current07 profile table487-642 in070 consumes these exact ordered IDs; no P16 unrelated reference/constants1-11/28-29/38+ credit.", "contracts": ["MEDICATION_IDS is the reference vocabulary, while physiology profiles attach actual effects by numeric index. Current14 ID order matches profile table, but the semantic binding is manually maintained across sources; F011 support070 requires explicit identity-keyed references or one declaration producing both projections, preserving open authored IDs/versioning where intended. Do not create a duplicate equivalent intervention owner or assume an enum is required.", "Carry-kit constants own item, placement and attachment-point identity in different namespaces; WEAPON_CARRY_HIP_PLACEMENTS derives its entries from the named constants, so it does not duplicate literal left/right spelling. Inventory row/physical object IDs must not replace these authored definition-local IDs.", "PR REQUIRED_GAMEPLAY_ITEM_IDS repeats some literal spellings also exposed as named constants, currently agreeing. Reference validation list can consume those actual canonical constants instead of independently authored literal copies; required list membership itself is a different purpose from all possible item catalogue membership. Currency/medication sets are intentional subsets, not exhaustive whole catalogue enums.", "Reexport of gameplay validation is a source reference to the same function, not a second validator. That actual child has its own current source inventory; full catalogue membership/current fixture behavior is not inferred from a constant list alone."], "findings": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Bind profile effects and known reference lists by canonical semantic identity, preserve namespace distinctions and derive repeated native literal spellings from the same constants. Retain intentional subset membership and raw unknown diagnostics.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with qualified reference-binding migration opportunities"}
