atalogue role responsibility."], "findings": [], "qualification": "Explicit production-only current-role scope. No PR test636-1251 semantic/body credit claimed. Historical broader owner read extents remain preserved as prior source evidence, not automatically current07 material expansion.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one immutable content catalogue and context-specific role/linguistic projections, derive complete canonical creation vocabulary without merging open institution IDs or different age-role links.", "status": "exact qualified PR production role07 inventory complete"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-074", "at": "2026-10-22T20:59:39.530438+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope028_index": 129, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/quest_catalog.rs", "sha256": "49f76eeee235f7458511523a247a9feabe167d5f84ba7ebe9a5a48d002f4f8f3", "actual_EOF": 1630, "material_ranges": [[1, 67], [89, 670], [731, 791], [793, 840], [842, 860]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-028.json#/files/129"}, {"scope028_index": 130, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/quest_catalog_validation.rs", "sha256": "738146c8cbe20bfd3aace0f834635051a93fd8b1b68e010819bbb012c1542428", "actual_EOF": 1526, "material_ranges": [[1, 1516]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-028.json#/files/130"}, {"scope028_index": 966, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/quest_catalog.rs", "sha256": "49f76eeee235f7458511523a247a9feabe167d5f84ba7ebe9a5a48d002f4f8f3", "actual_EOF": 1630, "material_ranges": [[1, 1630]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-028.json#/files/966"}, {"scope028_index": 967, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/quest_catalog_validation.rs", "sha256": "738146c8cbe20bfd3aace0f834635051a93fd8b1b68e010819bbb012c1542428", "actual_EOF": 1526, "material_ranges": [[1, 1526]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-028.json#/files/967"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual current03 CAMERA-ADM03-097/098 and Native root-support/contracts-004 BOTH fullPR1630/1526 source-specific groups incl original tests; current07 reanalysis covers raw schema/policy, private compilation, indexed state and actual observer roles. Fresh P16 catalogue1-67/89-154/324-668/731-791/793-840/842-860, P16 validator427-447/558-603/640-680/1495-1516 (small truncation558-568 recovered explicitly), PR-only render68-88/dialogue671-730, actual complete P16 scoped catalogue range diffs and entire production validator1-1516 difference empty. Remaining exact declarations/compiler facts are explicit prior actual full/current source narratives, not fresh literal claims. Fresh already-scoped PR/P16 bestiary compile_profile502-636 semantic counterpart comparison supports F014; no extra whole profile source credit.", "contracts": ["Installed Catalog stores authored documents plus private ID-indexed clones. It has private compile, no public owned factory/Clone/Deserialize/Default, and public runtime access is shared static. All indices/documents are produced and published in one immutable generation; public documents field does not supply a normal mutable installed-cache route. Therefore copied indices are justified immutable caches under actual API, not automatically duplicate mutable authority.", "Catalogue descriptions iterator derives the complete authored population from document order, while lookup indices provide key order; current named examples do not define an alternative report roster. Source locations, source-map IDs and document indices are diagnostic provenance separate from the content IDs they describe. IDs are checked unique before constructing variant source indexing.", "Raw authored policies and typed private acceptance overlap intentionally across representation stages. Runtime startup calls the same raw validator as build, then typed decoding and private compile. Earlier03 F024 identifies an actual target-representation gap between these stages: source-positive f64 weight can decode0 and later fail typed positive check. This is exact existing admission defect support, not a separate invented07 functional bug or an instruction to delete source diagnostics/shape checks. Shared target semantic owner should be used by both final acceptance paths.", "Monster ranged copy F014 is a current equality-checked derived flag; raw/typed/current profile facts traced separately. Negotiable implies sapient but sapient need not imply negotiable, so those booleans are different capabilities and must not be merged. Primary versus secondary categories also have distinct roles; categories() derives their union rather than retain another collection.", "Closed mechanics are independently listed in raw validator, typed validate_monster and String->typed bestiary adapters. Current accepted attack/protection/temperament/habitat/activity vocabularies align, with intentional tusk-to-Blunt normalization; a canonical typed parser can own the mapping without making aliases/different semantic categories identical. This is F010/F011-style vocabulary strengthening, not a present unknown mechanic admitted by private startup.", "Templates declare a route/objective footprint and private/raw compilers compare it with the actual three typed graph assemblers. Current guards prevent inconsistent normal templates, but the repeated assembler footprint declarations are a maintenance dependency; one actual assembler definition should supply its supported signature if strengthened. Cause-finales, scheduled incidents, relations and consequences represent different graph/selection/effect roles, not duplicate hidden case truth.", "Consequence frequency/archetype/intensity and buy/sell modifiers are policies for the same accepted cause but affect different systems. Required bridge eligibility, plausibility and curation are distinct selection decisions. Structural namespace sets/lookup maps are temporary compilation aids; no retained second current occurrence/event log is authored by these helpers.", "Witness demographic selection derives from actual age/optional private Sex/profession/local-role facts; presentation is not private Sex and visible callers intentionally supply None. Specific priority before fallback is one query policy, not independent cached demographic labels. Raw selector validation and actual selector_matches_fact must preserve whole-token equality semantics; no substring reclassification based on arbitrary display names.", "PR-only dialogue variant selection derives a single highest-priority matching presentation from actual FactContext, rejects ties, and renders an output String with bounded input values. This is presentation-only, has no generated-case effects, and does not replace semantic quest truth. Persisted generated/dialogue receipts and live dependency revisions require their own source-specific comparison."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F014"], "qualification": "P16 excludes render68-88/selected-response671-730/test862+;669-670 next signature remains incidental only, not its unscoped body. P16 rawvalidator production1-1516 only, test1518+ excluded. PR all original test facts are explicit Native actual full-source evidence. No project execution or normal current inconsistent cache/flag claimed.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one immutable compiled catalogue and typed mechanics owner, derive duplicate complete vocabularies/flags/graph footprints where actual invariant proves identity, and retain raw source diagnostics plus separate observation/selection/consequence roles. Preserve exact current errors, deterministic order and signed/bounded policy domains.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with findings and explicit receiver qualifications"}
