l-032.json#/files/2130"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh P16 exact Skill9-117/720-777/892-981/1010-1105, smithing78 and stock38; actual current counterpart scoped body diffs empty. Personally consumed full Native actual PRskill contract-groups-074 plus prioractual CAMERA-ADM03-117 and Root actual stock063; fresh PRSkill591-706/1101-1165 critical roster/actual recipient. Original PRskill tests119-589 source facts from explicit Native full1165 receipt, no P16test credit.", "contracts": ["Skill current training hours are retained direct investment; rank and effective transfer are calculated from them, not independently persisted caches. PR effective_skill_hours explicitly performs one nonrecursive pass over source direct hours and caps transferred hours to direct hours for trained targets; no feedback amplification from a retained transfer pool. Healthy governing aptitudes control learning/mastery, while current injury/armor/condition affect performance separately; merging these would change intentional gameplay and violate the stated healthy-learning contract.", "Governing percentages intelligence/instinct/agility are independent weighted contributors coordinated by private constructor sum100; total_percent is derived, not retained. Surgery30/20/50 is deliberately not a pure Mental/Physical classification. SkillKind determines performance channels, is_trained determines direct-investment prerequisite, governing-aptitude owner determines learning; these correlated facts are not all interchangeable. Actual full authored max_hours declaration and PR ALL roster repeat complete membership; F011 strengthening supports deriving ALL from canonical enum, while preserving stable training IDs and player-facing labels as different protocols.", "TrainingGain accepted and excess are complementary observations of one new effective budget, returned together; stored prior hours may exceed current lowered aptitude cap intentionally and are not erased. Language linear1000hours/rank and ordinary skill asymptote are different curves; do not unify them by common f32 representation or force mastery5 finite. Invalid/nonpositive input no-op does not sanitize existing state; existing03 numerical/retention qualifications remain, not a new07 stale-cache finding.", "ForgeQuote kilograms, rounded inventory microunits and minutes are different projections of the same immutable input design, constructed in one loop/function. Requirements round up per construction-material contribution BEFORE shared-stock merging, while displayed kilograms aggregate without ceiling. Recomputing requirements by ceiling aggregated kilograms would change valid existing stock semantics. Materials that map to same traded stock deliberately merge via actual ForgeStock owner, not separate material-to-item authorities. Minutes derive from physical mass and component work, not from monetary value or rounded stock count.", "ForgeStock has one closed four-member owner with canonical item IDs and unit masses. Material::forge_stock intentionally maps Steel/DarkSteel and Leather/DarkLeather to shared traded stock, returns None for other valid authoring materials. These classifications are many-to-one policy, not an erroneous duplicate Material enum. A missing trade stock is a domain error, not invalid authoring geometry. Actual quote consumes both canonical ID and positive unit mass from same stock variant; no duplicated independently authored stock conversion table exists in this scope.", "Quote public fields/raw physical projections remain prior admission/finite-operation qualifications; &WeaponDesign immutable borrow feeds both derivations, so no concurrent replacement input causing different quoted physical generations is established. Existing actual derived-property factory limits remain separate source inventories, no global finite guarantee from a Result or type name."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F011 support: PRSkill complete ALL32 repeats enum membership"], "qualification": "P1