"}, {"scope032_index": 160, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-core/src/unit_interval.rs", "sha256": "268891d7d5556895ace4c6ce33b14953e35d5973bfce9b042e4b9d2dbc721a86", "actual_EOF": 58, "material_ranges": [[1, 58]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-032.json#/files/160"}, {"scope032_index": 1022, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/unit_interval.rs", "sha256": "268891d7d5556895ace4c6ce33b14953e35d5973bfce9b042e4b9d2dbc721a86", "actual_EOF": 58, "material_ranges": [[1, 58]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-032.json#/files/1022"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete P16currency40/economy143/stub117/UnitInterval58 incl original inline tests; complete actual matchingPRcurrency/economy/fraction body comparison empty and current07roles independently compared. PRstub ONLY exact1-45 freshread and actualattributes/body/Essentials prefix semantic counterpart toP16; wholePRdiff laterbody context explicitly uncredited. REG014 P16itemrefs1-10 freshread AFTER registration, exactPRcurrent1-10 also fresh for currency producer. Prioractual Camera114/023 are only source facts, no oldverdictcredit.", "contracts": ["Currency catalog membership/name are queried from actual ItemKind::Currency, while assigned_currency_id draws from explicit six stable gameplay denominations. REG014 actual six-entry array supplies nonempty index bound and canonical byte identities; documentation identifies outside-gameplay references, not necessarily all future authored currency items. These are reference/selection set versus general kind membership roles. Additional authored currency selection policy should be decided explicitly rather than assume current whitelist is a generated exhaustive catalogue roster. Equal-value denominations and deferred exchange policy mean no parallel exchange-rate authority exists in this source.", "Merchant base value, buy/sell quote, language-adjusted price, fractional remaining food value and line/transaction total are different price stages. All are derived at call time; no retained parallel price cache or independent live balance is stored here. Whole-item sell minimum1 intentionally differs from fractionalfood0 and inputprice0 preservation. Exact count/mass/value units and rounding order must remain separate; type-strengthening should not equate every money-like number.", "Margin/tax/exam/inn constants are canonical named policies, and inn cost derives full/partial day count using the calendar day constant before multiplying once. Shared/personal balances are independent ownership, coordinated returned split uses party-first amount then exact shortfall; it does not define a second pooled account. Ingredient-values11 table is documented canonical shared seed/quote policy; actual seeding/catalogue consumers remain separate source inventories before declaring a competing independently authored base-price resolver. No equality or two-live-resolver claim from table text alone.", "Stubs explicitly provide examples/internal testing implementations, not production compatibility fallback authority. Their health/mass/focus/weights/hours are fixed inputs to example traits, not caches of actual actor state. P16 typed finite reach1 and broader raw trait implementations remain separate API propagation/admission facts. PRscopeonlyattributes/body/Essentials prefix, no PRweapon getter credit from unscoped complete diff output.", "UnitInterval retains one private finitefraction backing, default/constants are admitted values, max selects an admitted operand and getter/nativeconversion derives output. No separately retained percent/BPS/boolean classification can drift here. Producer-specific clamp and canonical finite[0,1]admission are intentionally different policies; selecting max is operation on existing admitted values rather than an alternate authority."], "findings": [], "qualification": "PRstub material1-45 only, body further than45 excluded; premature laterdiff context uncredited. REG014 itemrefs1-10 additional exactcurrency roster role pendingglobal, no fullP16itemrefs widening. Native raw price saturation/numeric extreme limits belong existing03/04 scopes, no runtime actor/item/balance guarantee here.", "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve canonical current catalogue membership vs explicit authored reference selection, one live price policy and distinct quote stages/ownership balances/rounding. Carry checked fraction through firstparty state and unwrap at actual numeric port; retain intentional fixed examples separately from production trait authority.", "status": "exact listed source07 inventories complete with explicit receiver qualifications"}
