son#/files/1138"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed actual Rig552 fullPR957 source narrative and CameraADM03-138 exactP16item role168,133 exacttest169/module170, all current source role facts. Fresh07 P16item1-305/305-426/426-468/650-690, fullauthoritytest44/lib95; complete actual PR/P16 source diffs reviewed: P16typed reach/balance input/native extraction, canonicalfalliblegrant/refresh versus PRswallowedwrapper, source assertion spellings and2 module exports. Every current role compared, no hash-only verdict.", "contracts": ["Item is a persistence projection of immutable compiled catalogue, not independent authored gameplay source. Init290-302 inserts every projected definition; surgeryupsert305-319 uses exact same project_definition and replaces complete rows. No live catalogue hot-reload contract is defined here. Per-source fields quality/balance/repairable/melee/ranged are evaluated at projection; consumers reading DB versus catalogue require same installed revision/one full projection. Do not infer stale row merely from hypothetical deployment or public arbitrary literal, but retain exact lifecycle dependency for all actual Item writers/callers elsewhere.", "Balance104-106 explicitly derives from inertia/weight/grip and is shown to user; P16typed grip input and reach extraction are actual DBnative seams244-248, not a reason to create second physical owner. Item does not retain grip itself, so balance cannot be derived solely from neighboring DBfields. One versioned immutable catalogue projection or boundary projection on demand can justify this cache; no actual caller mutation/invalidation mismatch proven in this file.", "Item.kind is closed projection of payload-bearing ItemKind182-253; enum classification itself is canonical reexport, no separate enum clone. Equipment.protection174-179 populates five protection fields, then Armor kind205-219 overwrites those same fields. This is explicit precedence, not proof two live resolver outcomes: canonical