mponents, but no source normal writer independently changes receiptidentity. ScheduleInitialized/Preserved historical outcome180-193 deliberately prevents resetting manually emptied saved schedule again; not simply derivable from current allocation==0.", "Saved schedule initial policy is canonical Core npc_policy result230-245, copied coherently once. Existing saved allocation independent current state, unallocated predicate174-178 derived from current minutes/orgtags; no separate stored unallocatedflag. Empty child schedule is deliberate underage policy; one-time initialization guard and daily receipts have distinct purposes. Actual Coreinitialpolicy source queue required for final exhaustiveclosure, no unrelated adjacent scope inferred.", "Scheduleeligibility reads effective_age_years205-207, housing282 andromance359-361 read cached Character.age_years. These are demonstrably two source representations of adulthood; exact birth/current-age updater and relevant historical/current timepolicy in relationshipchronology/time source queues remain explicit before concluding whether normal values disagree. No normal postbirthday failure or fabricated stalecache claim without that updater. Existing Character105 family source sets birth-based cache; whole07 must compose actual advancement operation.", "Housing current query resolves owned/occupied/affordable outcome and records past choice; ownervsoccupancy is orthogonal property state, not automatically duplicate authority. Romance uses actualpresence at same personalfrontier and canonical relationshipoperation, then maps outcome to historicaldecisionenum. Public kind labels are not parsed for eligibility. Directional suitor/partner normalization basedSex452-461 is actualformalpolicy context, distinct arbitrary candidate order; preserve deterministic entropy and canonical relationship eligibility, no newpolicy inference from label."], "findings": [], "remaining_source_questions": ["Current age_years cache versus effective_