"scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-042.json#/files/1185"}, {"scope042_index": 1186, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/residence/properties/materialization.rs", "sha256": "89be43ab5a91d96b96077c6950b9159b25f61165e938395ab54774540711b688", "actual_EOF": 111, "material_ranges": [[1, 111]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-042.json#/files/1186"}, {"scope042_index": 1187, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/residence/view.rs", "sha256": "b481076a43b5a9e15f7ee78deb63fb3e81cf97989061300fa34168d9182c6053", "actual_EOF": 57, "material_ranges": [[1, 57]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-042.json#/files/1187"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed Rig396-399 full PR acquisition99/fixture242/occupancy282/properties377 and CameraADM03-123 current P16 source facts. Fresh07 complete P16 acquisition99/occupancy282/properties377/households62/materialization111/view57; fixture1-25/95-112/191-242 focused, remaining actual source facts from full Rig397. Complete current PR/P16 seven-file diffs reviewed empty and each semantic role compared. Parent1455 Rig570 facts support meaning only; parent07 inventory pending.", "contracts": ["Property geometry is an immutable registered catalogue snapshot (properties24-25). Registration141-222 validates settlement/population and rejects a changed digest before allocation. Property rows plus digest represent one installed geometry generation. No live mutable generator or supported hot reload is established. Canonical GeneratedHomeCatalog geometry/allocation remains a separate07 source; a String digest alone is not admission proof.", "ResidenceOccupant is the current pointer derived from PropertyOccupancyTransition history165-189. Historical at110-138 folds only events<=requested minute; current pointer folds all effective events and can point to a future move, deliberately distinct from an earlier observer home. Same-minute order uses ordinal; removal is scoped to matching property+holding. Backdated admission refreshes the full pointer rather than overwriting a future move. Normal admit currently coordinates ledger and pointer.", "Ownership, primary choice, physical occupancy and household membership are explicitly different facts. Available property225-262 combines legal reservation/history/current pointer/unmaterialized census by defined policy. Capacity265-310 recomputes every intervening frontier and adds unnamed census counts. Aggregate population and named residents are disjoint granularities when normal materialization transfers the conserved count.", "GeneratedResidentHome5-12 is explicit one-time census provenance, not a current-home cache. Materialization14-111 skips already-bound residents and subtracts required abstract residents before adding named occupancy. Later moves must not reset the marker and allocate again. HouseholdPropertyOccupancy counts remaining abstract population; its gateway view derives named residents from current household and occupancy. Census household identity versus named family identity is not automatically one current fact merely because both use the same property.", "Initial allocate313-377 writes occupancy history and current pointer at ZERO once, using canonical census allocation rather than later per-person admission. Newborn inheritance74-108 uses the parent's occupied home and optional active holding; capacity failure does not prevent birth. Seeded physical homes legitimately have no legal holding. Birth127's exact optional-home recipient now joins this actual body, without inferring all occupancy from title.", "View57 enumerates possible actors from pointer/owner/primary/history, then the parent view must resolve their frontier. Legal holders remain able to inspect unoccupied property that still bills; former actors remain discoverable through historical transitions. Available-property DTOs derive from immutable property plus current offer and retain no second mutable price authority. Parent residence245 remains a separate07 obligation.", "Original authority fixtures242 are isolated dual-guarded source oracles for census conservation, legal title versus occupancy and backdated capacity. Existing raw setup/trusted internal acquisition does not establish a second normal production admission path. All original source facts supplied by personally consumed Rig397; no execution, new cases or assertions."], "findings": [], "remaining_source_questions": ["Parent ResidenceHolding status/history/primary/billing/current view245/1180", "Canonical GeneratedHomeCatalog allocation/geometry and household-generation sources"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Encapsulate one occupancy ledger/current-pointer projection across every normal write. Preserve historical frontiers, same-minute order, scoped removal, immutable geometry generation and one-time census marker. Keep legal title/primary/family distinct; retain aggregate-to-named conservation and optional newborn housing.", "status": "Exact14 child-source inventories; parent/canonical dependencies explicit, no parent/global clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-132", "at": "2026-10-23T01:16:28.267143+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope043_index": 245, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/residence.rs", "sha256": "c7ba3678d9c73cdd365cf91f5e8b4d115c161f1b454f4508128e6dd16408461a", "actual_EOF": 1455, "material_ranges": [[1, 1455]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/245"}, {"scope043_index": 1180, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/residence.rs", "sha256": "df7d47666e333785437d381321a5e7b85cd6e4c453067c83f8d86ea00a30ce35", "actual_EOF": 1455, "material_ranges": [[1, 1455]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1180"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed Rig570 actual fullPR1455 and CameraADM03-139 exactP16residence192 narrative. Fresh07 P16residence1-184/193-216/245-310/339-394/418-529/548-609/736-783/824-943/962-1157; complete actual PR/P16diff only morale Result alias and all current roles compared. Child131 current actual constructors/ledger/current-pointer bodies joined. Remaining NPC/admission/test facts use personally consumed full actual source proof, not prior verdict.", "contracts": ["Legal holding, elected primary residence, chronological occupancy and family membership are different authorities. Current status is a materialized checkpoint coordinated with transition history; holding_active_at and its view counterpart fold effective events at requested personal time. They must not use the latest status for a lagging observer. Actual relinquish751-780 and dormant/recovered849-907/1115-1154 update history and checkpoint together; current-pointer mutation is encapsulated by occupancy131.", "PrimaryResidence is a current explicit choice among legal holdings. Designation1042-1080 writes choice, attempts actual physical move, then records transition. A later different primary choice need not revoke prior property ownership or billing. Historical legal access still derives transitions; pointer designated time is not automatically a full historical primary-choice ledger. No blanket guarantee of historical selection from current pointer alone.", "ResidenceCharge is immutable per-period evidence. Base, adult and dependent components plus total are an audit decomposition, created from one ResidencePeriodCharge value849-883; outcome and recorded/due time are past processing facts. Current occupancy may differ from supported adults/dependents captured at the charged frontier. Billing next_due and last_billed checkpoint processed charges rather than elapsed real time; unpaid periods retain the due frontier and dormancy, so they cannot simply derive from now.", "The current billing and acquisition price paths have a duplicate canonical-economy question, F027. Three offers initialize from HousingTier.economy, but acquisition uses stored offer while period_charge uses tier.economy directly. Normal construction agrees. Preserve immutable past receipts; do not blindly make ignored mutable fields authoritative or claim a current bad price without a normal mutation route.", "Gateway status derives active/occupied at each character frontier and primary from elected pointer. Guests receive ZERO for private owner billing timestamps293-305; this is deliberate redaction, not an observed real date or competing clock authority. Owner still sees multiple nonprimary holdings because they remain billable. The pure transition fold policy repeats in reducer/view193-215/491-517; current cases agree and can share one canonical fold while context adapters collect rows, rather than separate policy changes.", "Residence leisure morale is one bounded refreshable source, not an additional unshown combat penalty. Actual source identity fixes replacement instead of stacking; current stored magnitude is the earned decaying effect, distinct current home comfort and baseline morale. Source applies condition refresh1038. The called Core bounded-morale and tier economy source contracts remain separate07 queue obligations; do not narrow morale to UnitInterval or infer all raw events are finite.", "Whole parent1455 source facts include NPC home recovery/acquisition, adult/dependent co-location admission and original inline tests from personally consumed Rig570/Camera139; fresh current critical bodies establish the authority roles above. Actual normal holding/current pointer writes observed are coordinated. Raw record fabrication and late fallible paths remain prior admission/operation issues, not a newly proven host transaction or ordinary stale housing failure."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F027"], "remaining_source_questions": ["Actual canonical Core HousingTier economy, period_charge and bounded morale operations source roles", "Other direct holding/estate lifecycle writers must join before whole07 acceptance"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Choose the actual canonical economy owner. For immutable universal tier policy derive query/charge projections from it; for intended contract/offer snapshots bind a typed offer/version and use it consistently in acquisition/billing/morale. Preserve distinct purchase/rent/maintenance/tax/support components, fixed past charge receipts and current explicit zero/clock policies. Do not add a compatibility dual path or equality-test-only synchronization.", "status": "Exact2 parent source07 inventories WITH_FINDINGS; child and historical/current meanings reconciled, no global clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-133", "at": "2026-10-23T01:19:20.345941+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope043_index": 253, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population.rs", "sha256": "99cd12b58bafddf20c526c07061a1c822636fc87670178ddb36eda2587275fcc", "actual_EOF": 759, "material_ranges": [[1, 759]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/253"}, {"scope043_index": 254, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population/resident_drafts.rs", "sha256": "0bdbeb8d3d35fb200d35d06429d177a9311b5e71207f89a3644fadcd6e72d959", "actual_EOF": 585, "material_ranges": [[1, 585]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/254"}, {"scope043_index": 255, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population/resident_persistence.rs", "sha256": "40ec2a78bdcbb5225ff5558a6bb8f186af189dc527eef024048495ec10df0e94", "actual_EOF": 299, "material_ranges": [[1, 299]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/255"}, {"scope043_index": 1188, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population.rs", "sha256": "99cd12b58bafddf20c526c07061a1c822636fc87670178ddb36eda2587275fcc", "actual_EOF": 759, "material_ranges": [[1, 759]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1188"}, {"scope043_index": 1189, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population/resident_drafts.rs", "sha256": "0bdbeb8d3d35fb200d35d06429d177a9311b5e71207f89a3644fadcd6e72d959", "actual_EOF": 585, "material_ranges": [[1, 585]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1189"}, {"scope043_index": 1190, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/settlement_population/resident_persistence.rs", "sha256": "577af433807bf7c8a4cc22f46f82ed318d2d365ca79e61a66eaaf6d1b408c5e7", "actual_EOF": 299, "material_ranges": [[1, 299]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1190"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed Root camera-support/contracts-002 actual full759/585/299 source narratives. Fresh07 P16population1-271/387-572, full persistence299, drafts1-483 complete production; original tail tests source facts from actual full Root002. Complete actual PR/P16 three-file diffs reviewed: population/drafts empty, persistence2 Result aliases; current semantic roles compared. Fresh direct PR investigation/projections1291-1360 already scoped1128 actual receiver supports only this bounded role, no whole1801 coverage.", "contracts": ["ResolvedSettlementResident53-118 is explicitly a reducer-local join of profile plus current Character/name/age and personality demographics. Backend148-178 also joins current components. Name and age are not independently stored again in resident profile; generation explanation256-262 is immutable provenance and must not be refreshed from current person. Current name/demographic edits should affect the join rather than rewrite historical explanation.", "Profile physical appearance strings, local trade/service role and home settlement are presentation/configuration facts. Do not infer all descriptions equal current physical geometry or canonical organization role without actual receiving semantics. Profession-to-social-role reconciliation occurs through explicit ensure_roles; exact source267 social-role authority remains a separate07 obligation. Organization representative postprocessing441-456 intentionally changes service/conversation/clothing metadata together for institution representation, not person identity.", "Draft seed/characterID and provider flag/private prepared age are calculated once before persistence. Finalize_household_demographics204-221 sets sex/presentation/exactage together before surname and identity generation; preparation uses the finalized draft. Sex and visible presentation are independent canonical fields despite same initial defaults. Core input/profile explanation captures the chosen seed/policy result; private local provider/age mirrors remain immutable for one operation and cannot independently drift through a public updater here.", "SettlementResidentPresence context_suppressed and health_suppressed are separate latest checkpoints, authored daily window is retained. Actual actor-relative npc_is_present461-466 uses historical suppression through remaining_at, not raw current flags. ScheduledStrategicPresence487-512 binds canonical exact place, observer frontier, daily window and actual alive/suppression evidence. Current outbreak125 and age/chronology126 facts now join the actual receiver; no clearing of raw checkpoint semantics from type name alone.", "The raw latest-flags helper557-570 has an actual PR investigation recipient1323-1359. Fresh scoped PRprojections body shows the wrapper first computes historical suppression and rejects it, then clears cloned latest flags before invoking the public schedule-only helper. Thus this actual caller does not accidentally use future health flags for a lagging observer. P16projections is absent current scope and was not read or credited by counterpart inference. Other callers remain source-specific queue responsibilities.", "Business operator identity is one stable canonical BusinessId plus native formatted key/settlement projection. ensure387-419 checks existing business/operator association and unique operator before insert; it does not derive current owner from profession wording. One canonical structured identity can drive codec projections, but no normal conflicting writer established. Immutable generation metadata must remain distinct from actual current business operator/person state.", "Population binding does not create a second person or second household census: actual identity insertion114-166 initializes Character, name identity, private personality and NPC policy once; reuse88-112 uses existing profile/current canonical person. Explicit age override versus generated age band is intended input precedence, not a second live age source. Presence schedule241-264 maps canonical Schedule to one concrete daily window; source time policy has one actual table transition. All original inline tests were personally consumed through Root002 actual source proof, not executed."], "supporting_actual_receivers": [{"source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/investigation/projections.rs", "sha256": "4277df1f4841a51dafe10f9ef950ca7dec6f434358cc8aa5a98f742766825102", "material_ranges": [[1291, 1360]], "qualification": "Already global full1801; bounded supporting current07 role only, source1128 whole inventory remains incomplete"}], "findings": [], "remaining_source_questions": ["Canonical Core population/profile definitions and social role lifecycle267", "Full personality projection lifecycle234 and source-generation role; this packet does not clear it"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep current identity/demographics joined from canonical components, generation explanation immutable, and profile presentation/configuration distinct. Retain one canonical business identity and explicit source-generation precedence. Historical presence must derive suppression at the observer frontier; pure schedule adapters may receive explicitly cleared current flags only after that check.", "status": "Exact6 population source07 inventories; direct caller qualification retained, no global clearance"}
