"actual_EOF": 85, "material_ranges": [[1, 85]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1199"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full P16 action154/authority379/automatic85 existing fixtures and complete actual PR counterpart body comparisons. Root004 source_roles11/13/14 actual source facts reanalyzed against current07 parent137. Existing source only, no tests executed/added.", "contracts": ["These fixtures deliberately construct scenario rows, capture before/after relationship/time/session revisions and compare exact replay behavior. Captured before/after values are temporal observations, not independently authoritative current records. Expected string action keys are acceptance oracles for the external protocol; they must not be removed by deriving expected values from the implementation being checked. The ten-item action fixture intentionally repeats commiserate for a different concern case, so deduplicating this roster would delete scenario coverage.", "Automatic preference fixture exercises row-existence ownership: repeated opt-in exactly one row, disable deletes, automatic attempt absent when disabled; party/death mutations explicitly call pruning and then check no row. This is current source evidence of intended lifecycle, not proof every production party/death caller invokes it or a runtime result. Parent137 retains the external lifecycle dependency.", "Witness fixtures use immutable challenge/receipt coordinates and actual session revision, then deliberately retry with stale expected revision and conflicting request key. Receipt resulting_revision is captured history; session revision is current authority. Both should agree at first commit but must not remain equal after unrelated subsequent actions. Resolution/current admission gates are checked separately from heard authored response snapshots. Preserve these distinctions and existing qualitative useful-answer/did-not-yield expectations."], "findings": [], "existing_f