{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-139", "at": "2026-10-23T01:29:25.947680+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope043_index": 267, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/social_roles.rs", "sha256": "328d8285856568995cc423bb2ec74bb88bfa690af6e4defcbfc4aa8f9a355415", "actual_EOF": 579, "material_ranges": [[1, 579]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/267"}, {"scope043_index": 1202, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/social_roles.rs", "sha256": "328d8285856568995cc423bb2ec74bb88bfa690af6e4defcbfc4aa8f9a355415", "actual_EOF": 579, "material_ranges": [[1, 579]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1202"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete P16 social_roles579 including original tests as source; complete actual PR counterpart body comparison. Personally consumed RIG-CAMERA-ADM03-582 actual source narrative and current07 social137 recipient353\u2013369 for precedence.", "contracts": ["Organization instance is the identity/definition/local-scope owner, while CharacterOrganizationRole stores one current association per character/instance. Insert274 validates canonical definition role and existing canonical key, explicitly rejects duplicate other IDs; update312 changes only role_id through the same actual definition lookup. Display profession/literacy/precedence are derived from current catalog-backed roles, not stored as independent estate/noble booleans.", "Birth-family organization intentionally survives household movement. Provisional origin family is removed when stable family identity is assigned160\u2013225; newborn copy228\u2013271 retains actual parent family associations, not current household. These are independent social lineage and residence facts. noble input selects the actual authored family definition/role once, not a second retained noble flag. Existing F023 corpse-family binding must choose actual policy rather than treating every household member as kin.", "character_social_precedence_view425 chooses one recognizable titled role by (address_priority, roleID), then returns that same role social_precedence. This avoids mixing one role title with another role precedence; current social137 familiar-address receiver uses the derived precedence rather than a cached scalar. Canonical public address/title winner in other consumers still requires exact receiving comparison before whole-graph equivalence, no current mismatch asserted here. Literacy intentionally selects among literacy-bearing roles, a different objective from public title winner.", "Instance creation and cleanup manually repeat the three settlement template IDs91\u201395/510\u2013514, while scope-ID mapping34\u201342 is another closed local template mapping. Currently agree. This is narrow consolidation support for existing F011 repeated roster graph; a shared typed local-template policy should drive lifecycle enumeration without altering open authored organization IDs. Religion-to-learned-organization375\u2013385 is an explicit authored association, not derivable from string shape; preserve it unless canonical catalog itself owns that relation. Cleanup removes only unreferenced instances, not live family history."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F011", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F023"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep role associations canonical and derive profession/precedence/address from one selected current role policy. Share repeated local template lifecycle enumeration; preserve stable family versus household distinction, authored religion association and literacy-specific selection. No compatibility aliases or extra cached status booleans.", "status": "Exact2 source inventories complete; external title selection and corpse-contact policy remain explicit receiving dependencies"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-140", "at": "2026-10-23T01:31:02.467206+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope043_index": 268, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/approved_action.rs", "sha256": "d950b13458eeb9181a8e5c13187b252a25adee7f26374e42ace4a85dd58c243f", "actual_EOF": 173, "material_ranges": [[1, 173]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/268"}, {"scope043_index": 270, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/battle_combatants.rs", "sha256": "761099a162f432296e633e8d5a6f3e4092c08fb664bebb89dc3be7d725988444", "actual_EOF": 24, "material_ranges": [[1, 24]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/270"}, {"scope043_index": 1203, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/approved_action.rs", "sha256": "dc45100de7c1f6bfa836ee8b4634f1b502be0aab07d778f21595785bf2eadca1", "actual_EOF": 173, "material_ranges": [[1, 173]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1203"}, {"scope043_index": 1206, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/battle_combatants.rs", "sha256": "85a9cdeb34de89b6b81a65c512747b50771666aae4d1e6616345a617767a6706", "actual_EOF": 24, "material_ranges": [[1, 24]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1206"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete approved_action173 and battle_combatants24, actual complete PR/P16 counterpart diffs reviewed (error carriers only). Actual P16 governance60\u2013133/180\u2013212/235\u2013265 and complete counterpart diff (one error alias), encounters1000\u20131035/mission_bootstrap185\u2013212 freshly traced as bounded supporting callers; no whole-source credit for those parents.", "contracts": ["ApprovedPartyAction is one closed executable action sum. kind derives a broader category (both travel variants share