{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-141", "at": "2026-10-23T01:31:39.216994+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope043_index": 272, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/combat_error.rs", "sha256": null, "base_sha256": "58e6e2c18b7b24c5ca48112d598be60bec75a889ebfbf494562073baa85b318f", "actual_EOF": 0, "material_ranges": [], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/272"}, {"scope043_index": 1208, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/combat_error.rs", "sha256": "58e6e2c18b7b24c5ca48112d598be60bec75a889ebfbf494562073baa85b318f", "base_sha256": null, "actual_EOF": 29, "material_ranges": [[1, 29]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-043.json#/files/1208"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete PR combat_error29 and explicit actual absence of P16 deleted path. Base SHA equals current PR source pin as source location only; no fictional current P16 lines1\u201329. Current actual approved_action/battle140 counterpart diff traces migration from old error alias to canonical StrategicOperationResult.", "contracts": ["PR StrategicCombatError is an operation failure sum preserving AuthoredThreat and BattleResolution typed causes plus explicit RequiredDeathUnavailable and native Operation text. It does not store gameplay outcome flags or duplicate current battle state; error classification is causal diagnostic evidence. Transparent source causes and text formatting are different representations at the eventual reducer error port, not multiple executable combat authorities.", "The P16 source variant is deleted, so it has no current body, constructors, cached state or observers. Actual migrated140 callers use canonical StrategicOperationResult rather than retaining a forwarding alias. Preserve typed cause until actual native rendering; do not restore deleted compatibility error hierarchy. Exact lower new shared error definition inventory remains separately queued, no blanket error graph clearance from this deletion."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Retain a single connected strategic operation error model with typed causes through first-party operations to native reducer rendering. Do not add deprecated forwarding aliases or duplicate raw failure classifiers.", "status": "Exact2 variants inventoried, one current PR body and one explicitly deleted P16 variant"}
