{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-144", "at": "2026-10-23T01:39:58.252120+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope045_index": 273, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/custody_objectives.rs", "sha256": "7274d8bedc95fa40cee64bda7b7dda0c32b6d02aa01e44e754f77e1bd171bc5b", "actual_EOF": 1677, "material_ranges": [[1225, 1305], [1460, 1645]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/273"}, {"scope045_index": 1209, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/custody_objectives.rs", "sha256": "7274d8bedc95fa40cee64bda7b7dda0c32b6d02aa01e44e754f77e1bd171bc5b", "actual_EOF": 1677, "material_ranges": [[1, 1677]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/1209"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally reanalyzed substantive RIG-CAMERA-ADM03-589 complete PR1677 actual transition/ingestion/binding facts for current07; fresh PR461\u2013673/957\u20131241/1640\u20131677. Fresh P16 exact bounded1225\u20131305/1460\u20131645 and exact counterpart-role bodies compared; no P16whole1677, no P16caller prefix1419\u20131459, no tail1646\u20131677 credit. Same bytes only locate actual equivalent fragment roles, not producer preconditions.", "contracts": ["PR objective continuity stores historical start/through/custody-version and broken/completed checkpoints. Actual ensure461 only starts currently valid, nonexpired objectives; reconcile561 checks live place or exact holder/version, marks break on invalid, then validates unchanged objective before ingest642 and only after successful ingest sets completed649. Therefore completed is actual effect checkpoint, not cached now>=deadline; broken history cannot be reconstructed from current custody after it returns. Actual departure/custody caller coverage is still required before universal continuity guarantee; paired current metadata is not a competing history authority.", "PR ingest957 constructs canonical typed OutcomeFact and indexed identity columns together1020\u20131025, compares complete encoded retry then evaluates actual facts/expression, updates case status/contracts and appends immutable CaseOutcome. Case status and outcome status agree at terminal commit by this actual coordinated path; mutable contract agreement stages differ intentionally from resolved world case. Finales select deterministically priority+ID1139, mark selected/ineligible together, then execute effect before Executed and immutable receipt1231\u20131239. Exact receipt governs replay; historical execution must not be inferred merely from current eligible/selected status. Actual world_event retained effects remain separately queued recipient, no full effect graph clearance.", "Mission candidate1263 copies one exact capability including custody version and objective coordinates into immutable mission snapshot. P16reached1460\u20131645 constructs/compares exact current capabilities from authoritative provenance/objective/facts, so no independent handwritten candidate resolution table is introduced there. PRtail1651\u20131677 filters tactical subset, captures actual hostile snapshot and inserts candidates via this helper. Bound snapshots intentionally survive later live capabilities/hostile changes. P16 scoped fragment ends at1645 before insert continuation: no P16wholebinding or tail ownership proof is invented; actual P16caller/tail is explicitly untraced if later materially needed.", "Typed objective-to-hostile resolution1243 is an actual policy mapping between distinct accepted requirement variants and resolution weights, not duplicate current hostile status. Generated site group1284 derives unique exact eligible finale group and checks actual same-site group declaration; typed source IDs should propagate to native storage without English reclassification. Empty/unattributedparty and independent operation source versus fact ID coordinates in PR actual589 proof are deliberate attribution/identity facts; prefix stripping may collide but no current collision producer/recipient established, no new07 defect claimed."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve canonical typed fact and exact mission snapshot through true storage adapters. Share current correlated lifecycle updates, retain durable history/checkpoint meanings and deterministic selection. Final07 must close actual custody/departure/world-event callers and any newly required P16bound-parent/tail role before graph acceptance; no blanket private-helper safety claim.", "status": "Exact2 scoped source inventories with explicit P16fragment and external-operation limits; no wholeP16call credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-145", "at": "2026-10-23T01:42:03.558376+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope045_index": 274, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/development_gallery.rs", "sha256": "7e32bec846ebe3fc303be4c3aa4ed846146465c0bed45ed4f3426ed80caf9a3d", "actual_EOF": 312, "material_ranges": [[1, 312]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/274"}, {"scope045_index": 275, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/development_scenarios.rs", "sha256": "0a3344aa8f11ea2768169b64f3d7b887260bc7fd53e818c8bfff3b55b01ee394", "actual_EOF": 573, "material_ranges": [[1, 340]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/275"}, {"scope045_index": 1210, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/development_gallery.rs", "sha256": "95917e848a7696eed59a6878365b3b9171c9257d530a6254819270c59cead7e7", "actual_EOF": 312, "material_ranges": [[1, 312]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/1210"}, {"scope045_index": 1211, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/development_scenarios.rs", "sha256": "0a3344aa8f11ea2768169b64f3d7b887260bc7fd53e818c8bfff3b55b01ee394", "actual_EOF": 573, "material_ranges": [[1, 573]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/1211"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh P16gallery312 and exact scenarios1\u2013340 (truncated96\u2013112 independently reread96\u2013114); actual corresponding PR roles compared, gallery six typed error alias changes only, scenarios shared1\u2013340 identical actual bodies/current roles. PRfull341\u2013573 separately freshly read from allowed PR source after premature P16tail explicitly uncredited QUAL145-PREMATURE. No current P16tail341\u2013573 proof or semantic verdict from accidental display.", "contracts": ["DevelopmentScenario slug is scenario identity; scan_id hashes that same identity for native scan index, labels/category/description/entry_route are authored catalogue presentation, while primary_character_id is bound actual scenario actor. register87 validates actual actor and retains primary identity on repeat; fixture metadata is a recipe, not current gameplay character state. Subject membership binds exact generated problem/case/occurrence identity to scenario, not derive it later from a heuristic recurring flag. No second mutable completion flag in scenario metadata.", "Gallery GALLERY_PUZZLE_KINDS is explicitly a curated ordered set for fixture indexing, with fixed scenarios preceding and dynamically enumerated road catalogue following. GALLERY_ROAD_BASE derives from that roster length; per-item dispatch returns false when actual road enumeration ends. Scenario labels and IDs repeat as fixture references but are not additional current game authorities. Do not replace independent acceptance scenario/oracle values by the implementation output or infer curated order equals every canonical enum variant. Existing fixture constants and user-visible narrative remain authored data.", "Scenario provisions compare current actual party inventory to desired fixture target, then add only deficit. Target quantity is recipe intent, not cached current quantity; awareness max6000 is deliberate seeded starting state. Gallery raises attributes/skills for deterministic scenario and relies on actual item/capability/condition shared lifecycle; connected F022 needs actual downstream refresh comparison, no arbitrary blanket fixture exemption. This pass does not claim every seeded numeric value is accepted by every later gameplay consumer.", "PRfull backend development quests derives supports_incident_action/status from actual current problem state on each view, uses current contract stage or road challenge.is_open, and fetches public symptom projection. No stored duplicate quest completion flag is introduced. Immutable update receipt471\u2013517 owns exact request replay after a committed incident and records historical ordinal/time; current incident_count can advance later without rewriting past receipt. P16scope1\u2013340 includes only receiver prefix, not its implementation/trigger; no PR wholeview or mutation verdict transferred to P16tail. Local_problem/road_challenge authoritative operations remain queued shared graph."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F022"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep fixture recipes and historical receipts distinct from current gameplay projections. Use stable typed subject identities and derive current views from their authoritative owners; preserve curated ordering, exact replay and true native scan adapters. Do not synchronize recipe intent to live state or widen P16bounded source credit.", "status": "Exact4 scoped source inventories, including partial P16role with explicit uncredited tail and shared lifecycle dependencies"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-146", "at": "2026-10-23T01:43:41.396184+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope045_index": 279, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/dialogue_schema.rs", "sha256": "aad9a8d85274246ec4a34ceaf33f869f44d80b116f75b304767d290aa15fe576", "actual_EOF": 781, "material_ranges": [[1, 781]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/279"}, {"scope045_index": 280, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/dialogue_sessions.rs", "sha256": "bf32ce83dd633973a32cabdb638590e85dca6b4b06eec2a45d135f6c1c138cf0", "actual_EOF": 351, "material_ranges": [[1, 351]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/280"}, {"scope045_index": 1217, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/dialogue_schema.rs", "sha256": "aad9a8d85274246ec4a34ceaf33f869f44d80b116f75b304767d290aa15fe576", "actual_EOF": 781, "material_ranges": [[1, 781]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/1217"}, {"scope045_index": 1218, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-stdb-module/src/strategic/dialogue_sessions.rs", "sha256": "86473c2872a35a61a69775dc2578440eeefe4b620a5414c4aa044ca98bacf412", "actual_EOF": 351, "material_ranges": [[1, 351]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-045.json#/files/1218"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full P16session351 and complete schema production1\u2013696; personally reanalyzed substantive RIG-CAMERA-ADM03-597/598 actual all-route facts and source-only original697\u2013781 tests. Complete actual counterpart diffs: schema identical current roles, session one typed error alias. Current07 social137 witness receiver and population133 presence facts joined only for exact roles.", "contracts": ["Session conversation/catalog revision/settlement/location/owner party bind one encounter context. Factory start129\u2013151 constructs it and participant records together after actual world/presence gates. Live mutation boundary549\u2013658 checks current character party/settlement, current personal clock and each bound NPC current presence/representative role against that fixed context. Session context is deliberately not silently moved when actors move. Current validation fails rather than trusting old location as current presence; no stale co-location conclusion from stored session fields. Actual dialogue mutation callers must all use this boundary, still queued binding/effect/prompt operations.", "DialogueParticipant display_name and DialogueEvent resolved fragments/source refs are captured encounter/transcript observations. Start copies actual current character/NPC identities, then resolves authored greeting and records event once; backend views copy those snapshots, not independently regenerate old speech from later catalog/profile/personality. Whether participant heading should reflect later renaming requires actual observer purpose, not inferred from field name; no stale-name finding claimed. Free chat captured sender_name/body/time is separate historical message from scripted authoritative effects; text must not become executable current authority.", "Prompt mode/choices/cardinality/policy are authored prompt capture under the bound catalog revision, while answers are per-participant responses and resolved choice IDs are group resolution. They are different facts, not arrays to force equal. Open/resolved state plus resolved payload are one correlated current state; actual prompt creation/resolution operations remain queued for coordinated-update proof. DialogueAction resulting_revision is historical replay outcome, session.revision current serialization; later session changes should not rewrite old action receipts. Topic knowledge history differs from refreshed session topic-option availability; actual refresh/effect callers remain pending.", "Schema state stable_id/parse tables manually repeat active/open/resolved closed keys; actual factory uses the canonical helper, backend merely projects raw codec fields. Support existing F010 canonical wire vocabulary consolidation without inventing a new equivalent owner. Participant actor identity strings versus character_id Option also repeat identity/role classification; factory emits canonical player character:ID and numeric NPC forms, live boundary parses every NPC. The final connected representation must retain canonical identity through first-party records to native codec, preserving player-versus-NPC role meaning; no public raw table seal inferred.", "Start existing-session retry matches conversation/context/catalog and rechecks live presence. It does not recapture old participants under a new selected NPC argument; existing actual participant set owns that session. This is request-retry identity qualification, not proof two current NPC authorities disagree. Greeting/referral/witness records carry exact event-local provenance and preserve observer-safe discovery distinct from accepting a contract or revealing hidden cause. Existing013/014 dialogue validator and F019/F020 source parser graphs remain separately scoped."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F010", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F019", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F020"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep fixed encounter identity and transcript/answer history, derive current availability through actual canonical owners, retain typed state/identity through first-party operations to native codec. Close prompt/effect/topic/binding mutations before whole07 acceptance; do not synchronize historical snapshots to current world or add duplicate raw-success compatibility paths.", "status": "Exact4 source inventories with explicit remaining dialogue mutation/refresh dependencies"}
