128]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/338"}, {"scope050_index": 344, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/targeting.rs", "sha256": "d98b3d7ac9f2dd1dfd08f9eaa0442053cdc84b0e110c02d79de04eadafa0529f", "actual_EOF": 103, "material_ranges": [[1, 103]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/344"}, {"scope050_index": 1498, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/player.rs", "sha256": "e58cbe13aa543aebd82995383e999d55e0e47b9885396f958282313316f4e37c", "actual_EOF": 944, "material_ranges": [[1, 944]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/1498"}, {"scope050_index": 1499, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/player/action_clock.rs", "sha256": "1b21e39987ef8116d961373662e3566233e45bff974103bf29e399d4defaa9dd", "actual_EOF": 201, "material_ranges": [[1, 201]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/1499"}, {"scope050_index": 1500, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/player/attack_start.rs", "sha256": "9217876cb451796dde9e82c22f7a9533fbe263ebe21068756fb672e66eb622cf", "actual_EOF": 453, "material_ranges": [[1, 453]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/1500"}, {"scope050_index": 1744, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/targeting.rs", "sha256": "d1d12b0de4fd11d6e6b88a8a2c5b8f61ef2e05121c72a09853d745dc7db54f5c", "actual_EOF": 84, "material_ranges": [[1, 84]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-050.json#/files/1744"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed RootCamera007 source_roles60-64 full P16 player/acquisition/clock/attack/contact facts, NativeRootSupport001 trace/targeting actual source narratives and Rig674/675/676 full PR facts. Fresh P16 player1-160/260-398, action_clock1-164, contactfull82, acquisition1-110/180-336, attack_start1-280/299-454, tracefull128/targetingproduction1-54; actual PR player73-158/320-373/523-679 critical retention/consumer paths fresh. Complete actual attack_start/action_clock/targeting counterpart diffs read, and PR monolithic acquisition/contact versus P16 staged typed split explicitly compared from actual bodies. Original tests fullsource facts consumed from exact suppliers; no execution or verdict carry.", "contracts": ["Client AttackState is local prediction of accepted user intent, distinct from transient authoritative server combat and replicated SkeletonState. PreparedMeleeAttack computes current viewer timing/target/AttackState before begin_attack_timed and only after its success inserts state/removes buffer/sends MeleeActionRequest. Predicted ranged likewise prepares target/clock/timer before begin and publishes only success. Private staged product reuses same spec/timing/target for local playback and request; no second independently authored melee policy established. Actual begin_attack_timed internal mutation/error atomicity is separately scoped new Root015 body, not proven simply by Result or private Prepared name.", "Buffered melee retains requested family/hand only. Flush reselects current attack spec, reads actual current equipped viewer, reach, incapacitation, timing, target and clock before publication; it does not replay stale prepared geometry. Missing viewer/busy/downed cases are explicit no-action/wait behavior, distinct from accepted attack. Ranged versus melee bool comes actual viewer+selected hand observation, alongside melee support/style; these orthogonal capabilities can both be true for hybrid weapon, so do not force complement or erase melee fallback.", "Acquisition target/bodypart/local strike point and scene point describe one selected hitbox in different frames. Normal producer creates them from one resolved choice; during predicted attack it reprojects local point through current hitbox transform before facing/contact, keeping moving hitbox dependency current. Missing hitbox retains last observed intended point, while final actual obstruction/body lookup determines local hit/miss; no current hit authorization inferred solely from old target point. Public sibling mutability remains aggregate/admission scope, not proof normal source creates inconsistent target-position pairs.", "BodyStableChoice ideal point ranks preferred body and resolved point selects an actually reachable hitbox within that same body. These are different optimization facts; exhausted bodies are explicitly excluded and iteration ends when no eligible body. MovementPrevalidated bypasses range filter only after actual movement-arrival closure/collider-clearance gate; PR uses f32MAX numeric sentinel for that context, P16 explicit enum preserves meaning. Do not call ideal point versus resolved point stale duplicate position or blindly replace selection priority with nearest hitbox.", "Playback sample ticks and native AttackState timers are different clock ports for same prepared contact. Contact_from_input_seconds uses replicated locomotion sample delta for continuation, ordinary prepared seconds otherwise. Timing constructors share sequence_start/contact/end derivation once, then timers consume same contact delay. animation_ticks enforces minimum one sample; delay_ticks permits zero; finite product integer conversion intentionally saturates. Native render Time tick sample is client prediction clock, not official strategic clock or exact server tick identity. Server operation acceptance remains its own receiver source.", "LocalBodyFacing explicitly smooths render frames between replicated samples: cached rotation is current local visual integration state and copied to local Transform only on successful BodyFacingTurn. It resets on downed/posture transition and reads current camera/velocity/action/guard/target deadline every frame. Replicated rotation and render prediction need not equal each frame; this does not establish competing server authority. No explicit network-correction rebase is visible here beyond initial fallback/reset; reconciliation ownership remains actual netcode/replication dependency, no current bad correction or gameplay result claimed from this source alone.", "At contact the system reobserves collider geometry and actual obstruction, removes expired local attack state, prepares one PredictedAttackContact then uses its result for ranged request and its ray for debug event. Ray length and hit/miss are correlated outputs of same observation, not independently maintained classifications. Target bodypart is selected target identity, while native obstruction test checks target body membership; server hit/damage validation remains authoritative and must not trust local report. PR keeps raw ray/positions and inline observation; P16 checked completed positions/lengths and staged contact preserve actual error-before-event order.", "Quickstep trace captures observed action/actuator/start tick for change logging only. It intentionally retains start tick even inactive; old observation is history, not a live actuator copy to drive physics. Discrepancy log compares dodge or quickstep lunge to actual push.active but does not repair source state. Rendering transform and snapshot translation are independently labeled observations; no second tactical position persisted to strategic DB. Targeting kernel computes alignment/range/stable tie on read and returns input candidate, with no retained derived authority. Independent existing tests preserve target-body priority, continuation delay and predicate endpoints as source evidence, not executed acceptance."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve client intent/prediction, replicated server state and native debug observations as distinct facts; retain one staged spec/timing/target product to publication. Propagate canonical geometry/range context through the complete split instead of raw f32MAX sentinel. Explicitly own network correction/rebase and actual begin-attack failure lifecycle in their source scopes before any stronger cache claim; keep authoritative server hit validation, all-word clocks, zero-delay and stable-body targeting semantics.", "status": "Eleven source variants inventoried with actual per-snapshot role differences; lower skeleton mutation, netcode correction and server authority receivers remain separate queued contracts, no overall clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-177", "at": "2026-10-23T02:57:52.751811+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope051_index": 339, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/presentation/environment.rs", "sha256": "b6c219d19f45e18cf058bfa3ec4a06e826e50c2ae83d122e8d421f418dc31dbc", "actual_EOF": 577, "material_ranges": [[1, 270]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/339", "role_qualification": "P16 environment1-270 only; apply_active_environment_fog269-270 signature context;271-577 uncredited forP16, PRfull577 separately compared"}, {"scope051_index": 340, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/strategic_scene/equipment.rs", "sha256": "a5276f1904f7b2072d0b173663ed3592075960f11ef193b5ffc0688023523a41", "actual_EOF": 150, "material_ranges": [[1, 150]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/340", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 341, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/tactical_scene_viewer/view_camera.rs", "sha256": "b8ca7d503b8d6de9b9f0892346e97eb71f3a801b68012337f4943be7e7057af9", "actual_EOF": 265, "material_ranges": [[1, 265]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/341", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 342, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/tactical_scene_viewer/view_camera/landscape.rs", "sha256": "0ca70d46d9aafbe4f1fef2e245b771e23fd6a79eb7263b7937c6306ed1068a11", "actual_EOF": 101, "material_ranges": [[1, 101]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/342", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 343, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/tactical_scene_viewer/view_camera/placement.rs", "sha256": "6f16515e0ef35ed320d6c8b862676bb68e853ba485c30454c7c049a6c61bfa0c", "actual_EOF": 60, "material_ranges": [[1, 60]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/343", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 1532, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/presentation/environment.rs", "sha256": "b6c219d19f45e18cf058bfa3ec4a06e826e50c2ae83d122e8d421f418dc31dbc", "actual_EOF": 577, "material_ranges": [[1, 577]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1532", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 1683, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/strategic_scene/equipment.rs", "sha256": "bcfd6571ac4b5c7fb271cfb50e5ef79c08b7110bc649364f23abd31c44799bdf", "actual_EOF": 150, "material_ranges": [[1, 150]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1683", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}, {"scope051_index": 1722, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-client/src/tactical_scene_viewer/view_camera.rs", "sha256": "17a9a24f5d15cbd9db474bed73f9cecc39d1dddb1af6a7ff2d9d74a83ae13461", "actual_EOF": 350, "material_ranges": [[1, 350]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1722", "role_qualification": "Exact original full role; no child module expansion"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed substantive Rig062/446/RigRoot238 and Native026 capture-camera/022 SceneCameraView+Vista plus RootCamera009 per-source actual narratives. Fresh P16 strategic equipmentfull150, environment1-58/177-270 exact, PRenvironment269-285 actualreceiver, P16landscapefull101/placementfull60, view_camera1-93/160-265. Complete actual PR/P16 strategic equipment/environment/view_camera diff explicitly compared (physical-leaf projection, no environment delta, camera formatting only). Earlier Native048 exact1-270 scope retained forP16, no full577 by equalbytes. No prior-lens verdict credit.", "contracts": ["Wardrobe retains original EquipmentAppearance vector plus generated ECS entity IDs as one presentation cache. Actual sync runs when strategic view or retained scene changes, compares current person.equipment and replaces all listed item entities if appearance differs. Each snapshot resolves catalogue physical proxy, copies immutable weapon/holder recipe transport and derives held slot from actual occupancy. Strategic display entities intentionally have striking_head_length0 and do not become tactical combat authority. Native projection of same appearance into handles is justified at renderer; semantic appearance/occupancy stays typed until that port.", "Wardrobe source appearance equality includes placements, occupancies and recipe identity; current owner is actual retained person model. Catalogue is current static embedded definition lookup, not a live asset revision input established here. Duplicate presentation IDs overwrite HashMap entries and missing parents filter occupancy, retaining existing admission/aggregate qualification; neither Vec nor generated IDs certify accepted graph. Raw alternate mutation/despawn and possible later dynamic catalogue require explicit cache ownership if introduced, no current normal stale catalogue or orphan result claimed from this source alone.", "ActiveTacticalScene activation_order is historical selection priority while entity is derived current selected live member. Activate deduplicates then pushes latest and updates selected; refresh removes dead/non-environment entries and selects latest remaining. These are coordinated current selection plus temporal priority, not competing scene-data authorities. SceneEnvironment remains on scene entity; resource stores only which scene presentation should read. PR apply_active_environment_fog checks actual selected entity and current component change before deriving fog, so it does not maintain separate copied weather policy. P16 exact269-270 contains signature only and does not receive PR271-285 body credit.", "Initial TacticalCameraSetup is setup input copied to native camera projection/Transform, not continuously authoritative live view after controls run. Atmosphere and fog are separate native transport/presentation phenomena; atmosphere note explicitly avoids installing a duplicate live EnvironmentMap producer on camera. Full native lighting producer graph remains separately scoped, no two-producer behavior inferred or cleared from this comment. MSAA enum maps browser-supported Sample4 deliberately, not duplicate independently edited active sample count.", "Capture camera helpers derive view position/target once from capture state and pose; lookup errors and optional fallback to actual ground view are explicit. Fixed offsets/radii are independently authored inspection intentions, not cached classifications of terrain. Landscape vista minimum/maximum point/elevation, terrain maximum and city half extent have different sampled geometric coverage; max() framing combines them intentionally. No assumption every maximum or extent measures identical source range. Optional missing Vista errors rather than inventing height0; actual extrema producer remains separately inventoried.", "SceneCameraView distinguishes LookingAt with up from Fixed rotation. In LookingAt orientation derives from position/target/up at native Transform boundary; in Fixed mode target is independent focus/report evidence and need not dictate orientation or differ from position. Therefore retaining target and fixedrotation is not redundant authority to collapse. LookingAt public sibling point mutation can violate relation after constructor, existing Native03F005 encapsulation/aggregate support preserved without new07finding or badcaller/run claim. No separately stored quaternion competes with a changed LookingAt target.", "CaptureCameraPlacement view and optional obstruction are requested final camera placement versus observation explaining displacement, not equal copies. RequiresLiveQuery modes reject static helper path; missing authored/building indices return errors, preventing guessed static view from masquerading as live capture. Completed positions/directions admit before native rendering. Public capture metadata/typed finite leaves do not certify all terrain/grid/scene state, and native compare/FP failure policies remain their own operation/admission graphs. Original source tests are independent oracles, never executed here."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": ["native/admission03/findings.jsonl#NATIVE-ADMISSION03-F005"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Retain explicit appearance->render cache ownership and current scene selection update; preserve history priority versus authoritative scene data. Seal LookingAt relational fields through mode-aware update APIs while leaving Fixed focus independent. Keep optional measured obstruction/extrema and authored review intentions distinct, and only unwrap typed data at actual native math/render ports. No new duplicate validation/owner or blanket native cache waiver.", "status": "Eight exact variants with boundedP16/fullPR environment qualification; child catalogue/scene/capture/lighting graphs retain exact separately queued obligations"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-178", "at": "2026-10-23T02:59:30.060428+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope051_index": 347, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/animation/mod.rs", "sha256": "75fc12083762ad42e6fa03e9dbbd10e448c72c7940847b8c105add09c96e3c66", "actual_EOF": 86, "material_ranges": [[1, 86]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/347"}, {"scope051_index": 354, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/doors.rs", "sha256": "daf461a37ebe8f9ef72ac67aa98842c02bd8239ca43087f5c4d285f70df1ca34", "actual_EOF": 132, "material_ranges": [[1, 132]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/354"}, {"scope051_index": 357, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory/quantity.rs", "sha256": "6a0acac145fbe06b57ecbe43504dae3eca6d0923f65aedccf72c98c9e7977e33", "actual_EOF": 28, "material_ranges": [[1, 28]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/357"}, {"scope051_index": 358, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory/timing.rs", "sha256": "d02da5117e785f6425ae9d21c2d48a30f0fb7818e22df987fa787f88a3cbab04", "actual_EOF": 17, "material_ranges": [[1, 17]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/358"}, {"scope051_index": 359, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/lib.rs", "sha256": "f0f319e706f85bf05b038d8e0387be8085c488aaa4b736609cb386eff9bd51e6", "actual_EOF": 160, "material_ranges": [[1, 160]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/359"}, {"scope051_index": 363, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/scene_coordinates.rs", "sha256": "e3b88b223ae8d99d6fbcb634fbb1dd3990f9f42f4440309a341f3da3b8c0a0ce", "actual_EOF": 122, "material_ranges": [[1, 122]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/363"}, {"scope051_index": 364, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/scene_coordinates/velocity.rs", "sha256": "f961ea0bc8da4a4bb23bba732b32f43172c9ab2aaa83bd4ff8319efb4faaf077", "actual_EOF": 38, "material_ranges": [[1, 38]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/364"}, {"scope051_index": 1881, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory/timing.rs", "sha256": "d02da5117e785f6425ae9d21c2d48a30f0fb7818e22df987fa787f88a3cbab04", "actual_EOF": 17, "material_ranges": [[1, 17]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1881"}, {"scope051_index": 1882, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/lib.rs", "sha256": "244fd713d736e5e7da01d379afdcae5c77cd5705016504d882221057490eef26", "actual_EOF": 159, "material_ranges": [[1, 159]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1882"}, {"scope051_index": 1907, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/scene_coordinates.rs", "sha256": "1aae0147a71b5bf6e93b486a289dc31681517aef7b8638f8307bc221a3accab1", "actual_EOF": 122, "material_ranges": [[1, 122]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1907"}, {"scope051_index": 1911, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/scene_coordinates/velocity.rs", "sha256": "f961ea0bc8da4a4bb23bba732b32f43172c9ab2aaa83bd4ff8319efb4faaf077", "actual_EOF": 38, "material_ranges": [[1, 38]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-051.json#/files/1911"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full P16 animationmod86/doors132/quantity28/timing17/lib160/scene_coordinates122/velocity38, complete actual corresponding PR timing17/lib159/scene_coordinates122/velocity38 diffs compared. Personally consumed Rig063 actual door receiver/predicate facts, NativeRootSupport001 module/source role and RootCamera010 quantity/timing facts; reanalyzed07 independently, no previous-lens verdict credit. Current client grab/contact actual174/176 and complete focus175 supply actual consuming roles, not speculative source graph.", "contracts": ["animation/mod and tactical lib bind/reexport actual canonical owner types and register physics plugin, with no independently stored/recomputed current factual values or alternative constructors. Reexported Core elapsed/speed/UnitInterval/AnimationPackId remain the same owners. P16 geometry result/epsilon exports and PR EquipmentSequence/Revision exports differ with snapshot API; do not add compatibility aliases or mistake missing name for concurrent second type. include tests.rs invokes child source and gives no child body credit.", "ScenePlanPoint and PlanDisplacement are distinct affine roles; offset_from_origin explicitly converts a point to origin displacement, and translated computes a new point. 3D Position<Scene>->ScenePlanPoint deliberately projects X/Z and discards elevation rather than maintaining a second current vertical position. SceneVelocity stores three independent signed speeds for east/up/north; its Vec3 getter is actual math port projection, not a mutable cached duplicate. Coordinates, velocity and elevation have different meaning and cannot be collapsed solely because each uses metres-shaped vectors.", "Constructors/manual decode establish component finite policy; no additional redundant boolean/classification or independently edited bounds table is stored. Completed translation rechecks resulting point, focus caller175 reuses the resulting full typed velocity/position. Lower Position pub(super) fabrication qualification RootG007 stays intact; output projection does not repair a fabricated invalid Self. Original local signed/zero/nonfinite tests are independent source evidence; opaque reflection/admission routes retain prior03 qualifications, no new07finding.", "TacticalItemQuantity is an ECS representation wrapper around the same canonical ItemQuantity, not another raw count plus independently maintained nonzero flag. new delegates exactly once, Default reuses ONE, get returns inner count; no copied maximum or local validation threshold to drift. Count may equal u32MAX and zero denotes absence elsewhere, preserve exact canonical policy. InventoryView melee_timing_for reads currently selected equipped weapon inertia and delegates one Core timing policy. Inertia0 when None is paired explicit unarmed fact, not a failed-load substitute inferred here; parent selection policy remains separately scoped355.", "Door/window grab share one actual interior predicate; window delegates door geometry function rather than maintaining separate thresholds. Inclusive depth[-1.6,-.05] and lateral halfwidth+.6 define interaction affordance, not an acceptance certificate or server permission. Client174 currently derives window/door halfwidth and frames from typed current source; raw native vectors occur within actual spatial kernel. Shared constants apply same physical policy, no different duplicated table established.", "DoorPassageExemptions stores explicit per-character temporary collision permission, independent from physical door pose/open state. grant/revoke update one native entity set and pair filter reads it symmetrically; no parallel cached contains flag. Membership is not proof entity is live door or authorized at grant; granting lifecycle/recipient remains actual server source obligation, not automatic public-helper clearance. Default empty and exact per-door tests are deliberate authority isolation evidence. Native layer bitmasks are engine collision ports, not strategic IDs or duplicated gameplay truth."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Retain one canonical leaf/owner and explicit affine/frame/quantity meaning through actual native ports; remove repetitive downstream validation/classification owners rather than adding wrappers. Keep module exports as bindings, zero/absence/unarmed distinctions and local passage permission separate from door physical state. Whole child definitions, inventory selection and server grant/revoke lifecycle remain their own exact queued roles.", "status": "Eleven exact source variants inventoried; reexports have no independent runtime authority, leaf projections and passage state explicitly analyzed without whole-family clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-179", "at": "2026-10-23T03:06:25.701631+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope052_index": 355, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory.rs", "sha256": "a1b3b6e0f7f1d9884a53f8306a3e0e9e6c1a8deb26e2b13fb163f73edd39900d", "actual_EOF": 858, "material_ranges": [[1, 858]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/355", "role_qualification": "Full original source, original tests source-only"}, {"scope052_index": 356, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory/armor.rs", "sha256": "49cd8bc000aa19cd346741cd36179b1477050c9c1949bcddc4696e486cd0461c", "actual_EOF": 53, "material_ranges": [[1, 53]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/356", "role_qualification": "Full original source, original tests source-only"}, {"scope052_index": 1877, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory.rs", "sha256": "513ea2b3aa9c0322422e9cea57e10c00c00fe2046f10ce6d9d0cf6460c93957e", "actual_EOF": 862, "material_ranges": [[1, 862]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/1877", "role_qualification": "Full original source, original tests source-only"}, {"scope052_index": 1878, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory/armor.rs", "sha256": "49cd8bc000aa19cd346741cd36179b1477050c9c1949bcddc4696e486cd0461c", "actual_EOF": 53, "material_ranges": [[1, 53]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/1878", "role_qualification": "Full original source, original tests source-only"}, {"scope052_index": 2813, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory_armor.rs", "sha256": "6eccc859a14c75eb9734e96267595d482c3216028bda7e2f4cd113b8312a996b", "actual_EOF": 205, "material_ranges": [[1, 78]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2813", "role_qualification": "Production only1-78; blank79/tests80+ excluded; P16 prospective REG032 before actualbody, Root052 narrowing preserved"}, {"scope052_index": 2818, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/inventory_armor.rs", "sha256": "6eccc859a14c75eb9734e96267595d482c3216028bda7e2f4cd113b8312a996b", "actual_EOF": 205, "material_ranges": [[1, 78]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2818", "role_qualification": "Production only1-78; blank79/tests80+ excluded; P16 prospective REG032 before actualbody, Root052 narrowing preserved"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally reconsumed actual Camera033 full P16inventory858/complete PR862 body comparison and RootCamera010 armor53 source facts. Fresh P16inventory35-155/233-351/352-381/402-478/520-545/586-648; complete actual PRinventorydiff read. Fresh P16ArmorItem full53 and actual PR counterpart bytes/body comparison; P16 REG032 prospectively registered before fresh full production1-78, actual exact PRsameproduction comparison. Fresh source-specific server projection/equipment/transfer/defense focused roles are support only, not whole-source coverage. Root052 blank79 exclusion preserved.", "contracts": ["InventoryItems.items is the Bevy relationship target of ItemOf, while holding_weapon/holding_shield are derived hand indexes with independent update hooks. Rebuild explicitly scans current ItemOf+EquipSlot+kind and is queued after actual reconnect/disconnect rebind. Normal equip slot hooks publish selected native handles, not durable identities; scene restore deliberately transports both relationship sides because hooks may be suppressed. This is a real cache contract with dependency ownership obligations, not a reason to forbid caching or assume private fields make every restored graph valid.", "Actual current per-hand striking_item scans owned inventory and selected hand slot; equipped_weapon requires WeaponItem on that current item. Holding_weapon cache does not control this path, so do not claim every cached weapon error affects ordinary weapon selection. Equipped_shield instead trusts cached entity without rechecking owner/slot. Normal drop removes ItemOf before EquipSlot and leaves dropped entity alive, so owner-dependent slot removal can miss cache cleanup: F032 records observable positive cached bonus versus no held side, with explicit native hook-order qualification and no runtime claim.", "EquipmentTopology occupancies and EquipSlot held-hand label describe overlapping current placement. Actual spawn derives both from same source occupancy; transfer_hand/pickup writes same hand_topology+slot together, slot-transfer removes slot when becoming worn, and drop clears topology+slot. These normal focused producer paths currently coordinate their facts. Raw public topology/slot independent mutation remains accepted aggregate/encapsulation concern, no additional normal mismatch from duplicate fields alone. Broad server lifecycle must preserve one coherent placement owner; source400/405/411 whole inventory still queued.", "WeaponItem carries combat handling/material/reach and physical proxy carries bounding dimensions/grip/head/anchor, with some projections of common generator geometry. Overall bound length, signed grip-to-tip, effective interaction reach and striking head length have distinct meanings, so equality is not universal policy. Current getters intentionally select physical proxy when present and explicit unarmed/zero otherwise. Appearance recipe/hash represents render generation source, not identical to conservative collision proxy; exact source validation/generation and fallback semantics remain actual connected scopes, no blanket raw SDK exemption.", "ArmorItem covered_parts mask and coverage_geometry per-part entries are parallel representations of protected membership. Actual projected_armor takes mask from admitted protected_body_parts and geometry from selected authored placement.protection, so their normal equality depends real connected-player validation. Contact chain expects Some geometry for every covered part, while fold only consults mask/scalar values. Public mutation can break relation; retain existing admission/aggregate strengthening rather than invent normal bad projection or duplicate07count without actual admitted producer discrepancy. Canonical per-part accepted optional geometry should own membership rather than separately editable boolean where semantics permit.", "Scalar coverage in fold is aggregate probability estimate combined as independent overlap, while coverage_geometry.contains(sample) chooses spatial contact interval. They are not automatically equal surface fraction or same current fact; RootCoverage policy distinction preserved. layer_order orders physical outer surfaces, slot is nominal first protected-body label and covered_parts may include several body regions. Each item enters armor fold once per queried part; first intersected outer layer selected and every row reports intersected separately. Those booleans are actual derived observation returned once, not retained mutable classification cache.", "Current layer/contact producer constructs surface/material/identity from same armor row and geometry. New P16/PR production receiver1-78 actual comparison preserves all computations and expect preconditions; original tests80+ excluded forboth newbounded sources. Original inventory tests/source-only assertions show intended unarmed timing, rebind cache reconstruction, multi-location topology and mapping, not proof ordinary drop invalidates cache. Canonical chronology remains PRtyped EquipmentRevision/Sequence versus older P16rawrevision, preserve clean integration and no compatibility aliases."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F032"], "existing_finding_support": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F011"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Derive current shield from canonical ownership+held-slot/topology on read, or give ownership/slot/cache one coordinated mutation owner that clears previous cache before ownership loss and handles rebind/removal/type changes. Do not add a raw compatibility fallback or only patch one consumer with a stale-positive mask. Preserve native Entity remapping/world-dump relationship restoration, per-hand weapon selection, all-word identities, zero/no-shield and tactical transient authority. Conceptual existing-source acceptance: after drop, previous owner has no shield bonus/side; pickup/hand swap/reconnect still reflect actual same owned held item. No new tests/cases/assertions/helpers.", "status": "Six exact source variants inventoried, new32 role qualified production1-78. Focused server source support not counted whole; actual drop/cache discrepancy pinned with native ordering qualification"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-180", "at": "2026-10-23T03:07:31.012009+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope052_index": 350, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "98f3cb6b60b6672e3bdb730f6c922c012120f3763add4beb906040f1be122c2f", "actual_EOF": 310, "material_ranges": [[1, 310]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/350"}, {"scope052_index": 1858, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-core/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "6da9d5558329053c0ceaadbcb7a19730884fc55bbc50cdd90af9b9305346b48c", "actual_EOF": 290, "material_ranges": [[1, 290]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/1858"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh P16combat1-210 production full; actual complete PR/P16 bodydiff including original test adaptations read. Personally consumed RootCamera010 role68 full310 actual source facts, actual client acquisition/playback source176 current07 receiving-body trace reused with explicit same lunge/contact contract. PR292 versusP16310 raw/typed numerical and error-policy changes explicitly compared; no old verdict/hash credit.", "contracts": ["MeleeLungeGeometry separation, interaction_range and maximum_travel are distinct geometric facts. melee_interaction_range adds nonnegative arm and weapon reach once; maximum range adds allowed movement separately. No cached total reach or derived lunge label is stored beside mutable neighboring geometry in this module. Actual range/quickstep thresholds read canonical runtime_melee_authority_config on use; no independent default table duplicated here. Epsilon1e-5 is numerical comparison tolerance, not gameplay range owner.", "MeleeLunge None/Forward/Quickstep is result of one current geometry classification; MeleeLungeArrival NotNeeded/ArrivesIn/CannotArrive is independent timing feasibility over drive speed/acceleration/duration. Nonpositive drive prevents moving arrival but not an in-range swing. None can represent either already-in-range or beyond allowed movement while ordinary attack remains valid; do not equate inability to move with forbidden attack or collapse NotNeeded into failure. Distance of quickstep and timing duration are physical intent versus configured fixed temporal profile, not two measurements expected equal.", "MeleeContactTiming.delay/contact are coordinated outputs from one authored windup and predicted arrival calculation; contact=max(authored,arrival), delay=extra beyond authored. Actual client176 constructs native timers and sample deadlines from this same prepared product, not an independent guessed contact time. Continuation replicated tick observation remains separate. Both typed elapsed fields remain live product only and expose no independently stored original arrival state needing invalidation.", "Conservative lunge acceleration is intentionally reference/fallback estimate with minimum healthy strength, mass and traction cap; it is not a cache of current actor-specific force. Actual current collider clearance in acquisition constrains travel independently. Do not synchronize reference acceleration with every player strength or erase physical actor-specific motor calculations as duplicate authority. Root/Native actual controller motor owners separately queued.", "P16 completed range/gap arithmetic readmits SignedLength and preserves structured Geometry/Animation/Timing/Performance causes; PR raw helpers use nonfinite->None policy and explicit float threshold. These are snapshot migration differences, not concurrent independent canonical owners to preserve in final API. Attack/Dodge input marker and reexported MeleeAttackKey introduce no copied current state; attack-key definition separately scoped. Original tests independently assert anatomy once, lunge thresholds, ordinary windup/arrival delay and tick safety without becoming runtime policy table or executed proof."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one canonical geometry classification and explicit arrival/contact result across both client/server recipients, propagate actual typed lengths/errors through complete graph. Preserve anatomy once, signed max-zero policy, beyond-range ordinary attack, nonpositive drive, independent conservative reference versus actual motor facts and exact tick timing. No compatibility raw-success path or duplicate thresholds.", "status": "Two exact source variants inventoried; actual controller/runtime config/attack-key child/source recipients remain separately queued, no whole combat clearance"}
