l-052.json#/files/2035", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}, {"scope052_index": 2036, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/ingress/attack_start.rs", "sha256": "d00a98bfffa50eabd877d4ec5d96667e98aa85c161639a074f7f3ec2a4046aa7", "actual_EOF": 295, "material_ranges": [[1, 295]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2036", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}, {"scope052_index": 2037, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/ingress/lunge.rs", "sha256": "6ce3ba9b4f6c1fef1cd90580466b74bde537c4ec2dac0f1cecec0fcda437c12b", "actual_EOF": 298, "material_ranges": [[1, 298]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2037", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}, {"scope052_index": 2038, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/ingress/timing.rs", "sha256": "8e06350841fdbea99a6cf45ab7c1aca53485273d5b07a064c11ee956cee446f7", "actual_EOF": 168, "material_ranges": [[1, 168]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2038", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}, {"scope052_index": 2039, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/ingress/work.rs", "sha256": "6be424d70d473190c8983c7f8657d117cf7aedd39c7e13c8e3d0cd6021d8a3fa", "actual_EOF": 50, "material_ranges": [[1, 50]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2039", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}, {"scope052_index": 2043, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/protocol.rs", "sha256": "bdc79a977759c6bc89210af417c605af95bdf23d383bcf29a3e1f49552590c6a", "actual_EOF": 86, "material_ranges": [[1, 86]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2043", "role_qualification": "Original full current source and existing source-test role; lower child definitions remain separately scoped"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed RootCamera actual substantive012/014/015 narratives for complete P16 source bodies and original tests, separately reanalyzed here for authority rather than inherited admission verdict. Fresh P16 authority1-372/564-672, full nativeclock62/ranged54, ingress1-535, full attack_start292, lunge1-242, timing1-115, fullwork50/protocol86. Complete actual PR/P16 textual differences for all nine files personally read (first combined output truncated; ingress and attack_start/lunge recovered separately in full); same nativeclock/timing/work/protocol actual roles compared explicitly. Fresh actual active_defense86-150 used as bounded cancellation/transformation receiver support, not whole-source credit.", "contracts": ["MeleeAttackAuthority retains ObservedMeleeWindup and ActiveMeleeAttack with overlapping target; PendingMeleeContact repeats attackkey/target/bodypart/precision and contact time. Fresh observe204-230 installs windup and active from the SAME arguments. authorize_started_attack212-246 uses ONE now/contact_windup to install authority.ready_at and pending.resolve_at, samekey/selection/precision, preserving contact samples only in pending. These are guarded permission state versus scheduled execution payload, not independent authored current classifiers. Duplicate fields are a connected ownership/granularity candidate, but actual normal writer is coordinated and no normal disagreement established.", "Actual resolve_pending_melee_contacts286-315 waits pending.resolve_at then removes pending and emits selected payload; untargeted path complete_miss clears BOTH authority halves. Private authorize341-369 consumes BOTH halves and advances cooldown only after exact target/bodypart/inclusive ready/expires/cooldown gates. permits and authorize contain matching predicates; repeated check is preflight versus consuming gate, not distinct adjustable policy. Default None/None and zero cooldown deliberate. Original authority fixtures independently describe those semantics; no generated test or whole finite/identity admission claim.", "Fresh actual defense cancellation active_defense110-127 clears authority via commit_attack_to_defense, commits skeleton defense, removes pending and lunge together. Offhand block129-141 changes retained power only and emits actual resulting power; pending precision is unchanged because original client precision and subsequent power loss are DIFFERENT facts. Consecutive intercepts historical counter distinct from active attack existence. No stale-authority finding merely from duplicated phase fields; arbitrary crate-visible protocol mutation and native deferred ordering remain explicit encapsulation/scheduling qualifications, no executed hostile caller.", "AnimationSampleTick is animation timeline coordinate while CombatInstant is native server permission clock, and MeleeAttackKey is occurrence identity. ObservedMeleeStart observes one native Time/f64 word for key and sample; delayed continuation schedule must not redefine identity from later contact. for_attack derives start/contact/end jointly, max(authored,arrival), recovery endpoint, with minimum one duration sample but zero permitted arrival. Authority permission uses actual now+contact duration separately from the rendered sample timeline. Quantization, continuation history and network allowance intentionally permit distinct coordinates; do not force numeric equality or substitute keys for clocks.", "PlannedMeleeLunge P16 computes collision-clearance/separation/interaction geometry once in MeleeMovementPlan; its movement drives arrival calculation and actual install. reach/closure/maximum_travel in PlannedMeleeLunge are captured diagnostic facts; current final contact geometry is deliberately recomputed later because opponents may move. PR counterpart separately duplicates geometry calculation between PlannedMeleeLunge::admit and planned_melee_lunge; P16 already consolidates that exact computation and adds checked frame/length/direction leaves. Preserve one computed plan without claiming every raw external collider/transform is sealed. pub(super) arrival/movement may be separately mutable internally; actual current construction shown coherent, not normal failed lunge claim.", "StartedMeleePreparation::admit clears target/bodypart together when CannotArrive, derives timing/work/measure BEFORE publication. on_melee_attack_started264-283 admits skeleton attack then charges ONE general work and publishes facing/movement+authority+pending from prepared facts. ReportedPrecision finite only, includes negative/>1, intentionally trusted animation input rather than headless geometric reclassification. Missing transforms scheduled_measure fallback to actualweaponreach remains explicit untargeted/unavailable-data policy; no invented universal current-distance guarantee. Skeleton begin_attack_timed lower body/failure atomicity remains its separately scoped role, not inferred from Result.", "Ranged windup has animation authored duration and minimum permitted duration after bounded jitter, both prepared from ONE authored input; not competing editable defaults. RangedAuthority grants one permission window but doesnot bind target, because completion chooses current aim and validates current target separately. Actual ranged start computes all fallible schedule/allowance before skeleton start and authority.observe. A Miss is deliberate projectile-consuming result. Client actor identity comes actual client entity; accepted defense event distinguishes attempted intent from real admission. PendingDefenderResponse is latest captured request/time consumed at attack, not current animation/action identity.", "WorkDuration combines actual contact-windup and recovery once; incapacitation-adjusted recovery and actual fatigue charge are distinct outputs. No hidden parallel fatigue pool or direct fatigue speed penalty introduced. CombatInstant/Duration native Duration ports preserve full range/zero/saturation; AnimationElapsed is checked semantic conversion before native scheduling. P16 pose/geometry values retain Position/Scene and checked lengths through calculations; PR raw equivalents and changed rejection paths remain migration graph, not compatibility dual paths to retain. Numeric overflows/admission/correlation findings remain their existing source-specific lenses; no new current07 disagreement from those verdicts."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": [], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Keep one prepared attack occurrence with explicit selected target/contact and one coordinated lifecycle for schedule, authority, animation and movement. Preserve independent permission/animation coordinates, original precision versus transformed power, pending historical defense and latest live geometry. Centralize truly repeated geometry/predicate policies without collapsing intentional observations. Any future split-state change must reconcile all observed/active/pending branches and cancellation; no runtime validation or source repair performed.", "status": "Eighteen exact variants inventoried for current07 with coordinated normal lifecycle and explicit lower/native scheduling limits; no whole combat-family clearance"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-186", "at": "2026-10-23T03:32:06.969647+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope052_index": 381, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "a21f436f16e7c331c844e120198460cd485a9342d6d9c41ff79fc039c913e0c5", "actual_EOF": 1165, "material_ranges": [[1, 1165]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/381"}, {"scope052_index": 385, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/consequence.rs", "sha256": "9e767c76aa28c3742a0d11658983b2ce4abfd2fb63bc89962d5f1c02b3e396d0", "actual_EOF": 308, "material_ranges": [[1, 308]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/385"}, {"scope052_index": 386, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/contact.rs", "sha256": "c92333b6813f028d894f8de669a20b823341813213103079ddb3c038388e44d6", "actual_EOF": 161, "material_ranges": [[1, 161]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/386"}, {"scope052_index": 387, "source_id": "physical-p16:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/defense.rs", "sha256": "68cb46b9efe6c4f44ba41fe4386c02fa7000314c52d6e10b7d33fa9742290d8e", "actual_EOF": 255, "material_ranges": [[1, 255]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/387"}, {"scope052_index": 2026, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat.rs", "sha256": "847551347ed20961db50cd3ef65998a772b1d732f26b4810f4ccb725685547ba", "actual_EOF": 1148, "material_ranges": [[1, 1148]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2026"}, {"scope052_index": 2032, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/consequence.rs", "sha256": "9e767c76aa28c3742a0d11658983b2ce4abfd2fb63bc89962d5f1c02b3e396d0", "actual_EOF": 308, "material_ranges": [[1, 308]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2032"}, {"scope052_index": 2033, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/contact.rs", "sha256": "d36c444c66fafb2943291079bf5edcb5cb16e0890b1a078d655e838510cbac95", "actual_EOF": 161, "material_ranges": [[1, 161]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2033"}, {"scope052_index": 2034, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-tactical-server/src/combat/defense.rs", "sha256": "68cb46b9efe6c4f44ba41fe4386c02fa7000314c52d6e10b7d33fa9742290d8e", "actual_EOF": 255, "material_ranges": [[1, 255]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-052.json#/files/2034"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed RootCamera actual complete012/013 source-specific narratives and independent original test intent; fresh full P16 parent production1-534, full consequence308/contact161/defense255 including existing defense source tests. Complete actual PR/P16 bodydiffs read for allfour (parent P16typed positions/lengths/errors and existing testadaptation, contact typedreach, consequence/defense identicalbody compared for current caller role). Existing full parent tests535-1165 supplied actual012 proof, here independently reanalyzed as gates/aggregation/provenance oracles, not dynamic checks or source-verdict credit.", "contracts": ["CombatPlugin registers actual authority ingress->resolvers->applyconsequence observers and postSpawn Condition/ragdoll/pendingcontact systems. TacticalWounds is server-only transient injury state; TacticalConsequenceAccumulator is bounded strategic consequence history rather than persisted per-tick positions/HP/enemies. No new competing strategic combat authority introduced. Imported childmod functions do NOT grant blanket whole-child inventory; condition/ragdoll and outcome recipients remain separate exact scoped cells.", "ApplyMeleeAttackResult contains preapplication resolved contact/impact metadata; MeleeAttackResolved mirrors the observation fields AFTER apply_transient_attack_result and consequence recording. Actual consequence16-75 copies directly from same event after mutations; it is an observation seam, not independently edited gameplay authority. Event AttackResult can differ from remaining limb health because damage is clamped to current remaining health; original raw contact energy/damage remains the historical resolved collision. Do not replace result with applied damage or force diagnostics/currenthealth equal.", "apply_transient_attack_result272-308 uses one applied limb damage and apportioning result to update limbhealth, acute trauma and wound records. Those represent structural injury, immediate incapacitation and ongoing bleeding/recovery respectively, not synonymous values. TacticalConsequence injury sums retain ONLY appliedcut/blunt across contacts; max_single_hit_blunt records peak distinct from cumulativeblunt (actual record_party_injury176-200). Existing repeated-hit and blood/pain/recovery source tests distinguish these facts. Bloodlossfield updated by other scoped condition routes is not inferred from this source alone; no entire transient/receipt lifecycle clearance.", "Equipment provenance records actual owner, slot and TacticalInventoryItemId before emitting resolution. Canonical armorimpact may carry exactitemID, in which case owner+provenance+ArmorItem match supersedes generic bodypartslot; otherwise defender response selects shield/weapon slot. Accumulator deduplicates by itemID and retains first character/defenderrole while summing stress. Actual ordinary inventory IDs intended durable identity; cross-character reownership during one consequence accumulation would require separate owner/time contract before calling firstrole stale. No invented normal transfer or duplicateID event. Bounded stress/ammunition/count caps are receipt policies, distinct from actual inventory remainingquantity.", "ImpactEffects is freshly derived from actual strikingmaterial and resolvedcontact: sparks require metal-on-metal; blood requires positivecut; sound can be body/weapon/no-contact. Native velocitychange is separate derived collision transfer with finitepositive energy/onekgminimum/cappedvelocity and zero-horizontal fallback. It is intentionally not the local contact energy itself or another healthdamage field. Source comment341-348 explicitly distinguishes joules from newtons/impulse. P16 partial Position migration still passes through raw native surface/velocity kernels; preserve actual source/API gaps, no native boundary excuse for retained semantic fields.", "InitialMeleeContact captures TWO independent RNGsamples (contact and defense alignment) once. Bodypart initially selected at start becomes deliberate forcedbodypart on contact; resolve_melee_contact recomputes current anatomicalsurface and armor for that selectedpart. That is a stable authored attack target with live armor observation, not duplicate contradictory target classifiers. When forcedpart supplied, one MeleeContactLocation::new recomputes correlated anatomicalsubregion/surface/armor together. Missingview/holding side canleave bodypartNone; actual ingress untargetedmiss handling is already compared185. Donot reroll sample/order or reconstruct selected bodypart from later hitbox.", "PreparedMeleeDefense separates response preview from independent FinishTrade countercommit; actual commit updates authority only after parent preparation, not a second gameplayresponse. Ranged requested dodge evaluates age since request to currenttime; melee requested dodge evaluates reaction delay after incomingattack start, rejects earlierinput. SAME reflex config but DIFFERENT temporal observations; copying one formula wholesale would changepolicy. Zero window explicitly yields1 onlyat allowedinstant; defaultblocking requiresraisedguard+neutralaction+blockingitem. Live shieldbonus versus holding side joins existing F032 actual stalecache graph, not another defect count.", "Raw Facts contain derived side/liveness/range/cone/permission projections of one current query and are consumed immediately into validated attack payloads; these are preflight observations rather than independently refreshed retained truths. Public/crate mutable event/factfields remain admission/aggregate encapsulation concerns (including target Some with missingpose API shape); actual normal receiving constructor and wrappers must be compared before asserting stale authority. Existing finite trusted precision includesnegative/>1, >1shieldbonus intentional, no arbitrary globalunitfraction strengthening. Existing tests are independent intent evidence; no runtime execution/assertion added."], "findings": [], "existing_finding_support": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F032"], "connected_repair_acceptance": "Preserve one resolution-to-consequence publication and exact applied-versus-contact/history distinctions; reuse canonical typed identity, energy, scene geometry and injury owners through actual consumers. Fix shield placement/cache graph under F032 without collapsing guard/response, armorgeometry versus aggregate probability, or wound/acute trauma/health. Any change to consequence dedup must explicitly settle item ownership across receipt interval and keep peak versus cumulative fields independent.", "status": "Eight current variants inventoried for redundant-authority lens; child condition, final receipt and resolver sources remain independent scoped obligations"}
