ope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/548"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh exact detail1-190 only (QUAL171 withdraws191-815), full glazing93/archtest46/cuboids254/kit130/kittest80; initial truncated output recovered exactmissing glazing/tests/cuboidsprefix, all SHA checked.", "contracts": ["compile_detail124-155 reconstructs meshes from accepted resolved solids once, dynamic exclusion source comes from actual operable opening closures/windows79-100, not renderLOD classifications. Roof faces/material projection158-182 is one geometry-to-render projection. BuildingDetail.mesh_mut groups actual material with an immediate linear lookup, no independent material index cache; public meshes are output product rather than canonical physical geometry. Native UV metres-per-unit2 is render sampling convention, not tactical dimensions.", "glazing8-92 derives crown piecewise from SAME ArchStrip polygon passed by archcompiler; pane pitch/lead width/projection are independent decorative policy not second aperture dimensions. Transient crown/rectangles feed both sides of lead mesh, no later mutable cache. Source archtest checks closedsolid topology; no runtime predicate or executed validation inferred.", "cuboids3-100 derives rendering orientation and seam-cover geometry from current resolved solid/wall. Role-specific yaw negation is explicit native representation convention; render expansion/missing-depth wall seam cover is intentional visual projection, does not update physical dimensions. Current append31-46 fachwerk roster controls one renderer helper and is reused by kit, not an independently editable duplicate current member tag. Face material/UV164-200 derive from same wall ownership/orientation/room topology; canonical tangent sign resolves direction reversals without a cached source frame.", "BuildingKit49-117 captures borrowed immutable plan, derives component size/interior, matrix, UV phase, facade membership and two exclusions in same iteration. Stored native placement matrix versus canonical source ID is legitimate compiled snapshot. Actual kit detail120-121/facade124-125 subsequently use PRIVATE captured exclusion sets, while instances46 is PUBLIC mutable Vec; independent instance removal cannot coordinate exclusions. F044 records this exact API-only gap. Existing kittest9-80 compares fresh complete kit products to fresh direct detail/facade and counts triangles but does not remove competing mutable authority."], "finding_refs": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F044"], "acceptance": "Retain common render_cuboid_placement and deliberate seam/UV projections; make kit instance membership and residual exclusions one owned coherent snapshot or derive exclusions from current owned instances; no new tests/runtime.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
