", "actual_EOF": 143, "material_ranges": [[1, 143]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/558"}, {"scope061_index": 559, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/apparatus/weaving/motion.rs", "sha256": "f46f864d8f240d94ec4116de2c28490950b2c65589a3b7d99a3a29271a633669", "actual_EOF": 119, "material_ranges": [[1, 119]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/559"}, {"scope061_index": 560, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/builder.rs", "sha256": "502686dec923c61c5544f2249c9ba10f0a1ec2fac5db68afbb55a5426698570d", "actual_EOF": 305, "material_ranges": [[1, 305]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/560"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full furniture345/apparatus61/commerce112/household93/printing124/weaving143/motion119/builder305, all SHA verified.", "contracts": ["FurnitureKind closed50 and explicit OUTDOOR5/INTERIOR45/ALL50 current rosters mirror enum membership; this is maintenance-policy duplication support for existing F010/F011 roster graph, not current omitted kind. FurnitureVariant compact/broad is orthogonal design envelope. Key.recipe235-245 immutable OnceLock is keyed by complete FurnitureKey::ALL position and stores compile errors as errors, never converts failed replacement to prior success. Actual recipe returned shared static reference; no later mutable cache entry exposed. compile248-317 has exhaustive kind dispatch and attaches access clearances from actual interior spec. Kind classification/ALL lower owner remains separately scoped; no whole lower-body proof from this call.", "FurnitureRecipe meshes/colliders/bounds/support/clearances333-345 are one compiled local-space product with distinct meanings: visible bounds include all visible vertices, collider IDs are local per runtime instance, support points represent feet, clearance reserves additional usable space. They are not alternative measured exact physical volumes. Public cloned product permits broader edits and requires coherent ownership, but immutable catalogue recipe route has no independent mutation/invalidation. No normal stale layout claim from public fields alone.", "Builder8-17 retains private mesh/collision/support/clearance accumulators and first construction error. member74-154 derives meshcorners, support points and admitted collider from same input geometry; Decoration explicitly suppresses collider while retaining visual shape. finish242-303 first rejects any stored error, computes visible bounds from all actual vertices, derives one XZ recenter origin, translates EVERY mesh/collider/support/clearance (and test members) before publishing completed recipe. No cached bounds keyed by independent object transform; transactional return prevents partialfailedbuilder publishing here. into_meshes26-31 deliberately preserves caller origin for architectural components, a different output contract.", "Apparatus18-29 obtains one actual interior spec size and routes exact kind. Table/metal helper geometry is one authored design, solid versus decorative choice explicit. Commerce balance3-73 derives pans/chains/single upperpost collider, nesting weights separate decorative objects; reckoning inlaid lines/counters are visual representation of powers not a second game economy value. Household candle/spinning construct designs from same input envelope, distaff/spindle parked outside sitting space; proportions are design choices not independent furniture size authority.", "Printing press4-83 uses same size to produce joined uprights/platen/helical screw and simplified collider; typecase86-124 partitions a shallow case and decorative type pieces, no retained mutable machine simulation state. Loom5-125 builds one static hand-operated apparatus from input width/depth; fiber128-142 is crossed ribbons vs closed volumetric collision deliberately. Motion seat9-19/beams21-42/suspension44-82 use same geometric arguments, wheel94-119 derives collider radius from ACTUAL supplied outline plus mesh faces, so six-sided visual approximation and cuboid envelope are projections with one radius source. Ratchet/roller/arc counts are independent tessellation details, not duplicated current mechanism state."], "disposition": "Complete exact furniture construction/canonical cache/product roles; intentional geometry/clearance distinctions, no new redundant-authority finding beyond existing roster support.", "acceptance": "Keep complete FurnitureKey cache ownership, error retention and coordinated recentering; single source rosters may derive enum iteration while preserving authored selection order/design distinctions. No source edits/runtime/testing.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-229", "at": "2026-10-23T05:12:39.944646+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope061_index": 561, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/containers.rs", "sha256": "69797c4c1e665521772738012a24b7ff39ba3fb6dfcdacc1624b5fb1ecb6c32f", "actual_EOF": 234, "material_ranges": [[1, 234]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/561"}, {"scope061_index": 562, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic.rs", "sha256": "5516f86959c5882f08e110cd9e31e26b1c6bbaa91775771a8f5356a476cfaece", "actual_EOF": 61, "material_ranges": [[1, 61]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/562"}, {"scope061_index": 563, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/bedding.rs", "sha256": "ae6e94031101a1d47906e6348859359820275511d2bc527d9544283dd3d1d1fa", "actual_EOF": 85, "material_ranges": [[1, 85]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/563"}, {"scope061_index": 564, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/beds.rs", "sha256": "672e6f75c36fc5e1035b008729730b996cbf88750e50a9dad93da625ee6792a1", "actual_EOF": 66, "material_ranges": [[1, 66]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/564"}, {"scope061_index": 565, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/cabinets.rs", "sha256": "7b1e10c04d5b546327546fe91b9cfdf00a016a3400c999041cbd1d341b83a464", "actual_EOF": 127, "material_ranges": [[1, 127]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/565"}, {"scope061_index": 566, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/seating.rs", "sha256": "60facf0fb58c1f95483d67ae6f8728ecbcba3201d86083849e20c86c4e72a36d", "actual_EOF": 48, "material_ranges": [[1, 48]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/566"}, {"scope061_index": 567, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/tables.rs", "sha256": "0e914056126923ef4e2fda70b44a4e8f1e594bc1fb2b39d81791e9d853484eb7", "actual_EOF": 94, "material_ranges": [[1, 94]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/567"}, {"scope061_index": 568, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/tests.rs", "sha256": "0beb9e346f5abced5bce012949f47dcff2e3f98f38dd6c6a2161da688e0a5d75", "actual_EOF": 128, "material_ranges": [[1, 128]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/568"}, {"scope061_index": 569, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/domestic/washing.rs", "sha256": "6191dfec93ba83baedf5eb42cd9fbcfbacee02d9769db16db87ef58289ffb2bc", "actual_EOF": 71, "material_ranges": [[1, 71]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/569"}, {"scope061_index": 570, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/finish.rs", "sha256": "dac29dae17db4b4f9d76d11d1b0abef36af636b365631f550a9fa90a4f81f072", "actual_EOF": 193, "material_ranges": [[1, 193]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/570"}, {"scope061_index": 571, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/finish_tests.rs", "sha256": "85e4b7e1566dd001bdbae642f55c1453fea3a09135e4d50d6cc5885f2a404a26", "actual_EOF": 86, "material_ranges": [[1, 86]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/571"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full containers234/domestic61/bedding85/beds66/cabinets127/seating48/tables94/domestictests128/washing71/finish193/finishtests86 with allcurrentSHA verified; originaltests read source-only.", "contracts": ["containers barrel11-67 one compact/broad radius+height drives staves/caps/supports/hoops/collider/access reservation. Hoop inner/outer thickness69-105 is actual ornamental metal, not another barrel radius. Cargo107-132 and crate_box134-187 deliberately model visible slat gaps with one bounded collision proxy; sack189-234 uses one level profile for mesh and conservative elliptical box dimensions. No stored mutable radius/height or cached classification survives independent design change.", "Domestic assemble14-39 selects closed actual furniture kind from one interior_spec size, then delegates joined geometry. Fourlegs43-56 derive feet/positions and dimensions from same size/thickness. Bedding dress6-31 calls one chamfered cushion33-85 profile; mattress support cuboid intentionally inset0.86 to leave chamfered corners, no second mattress measured width authority. Beds3-52 select one/two actual deck heights by BunkBed and derive all rails/ladder from same envelope; deck54-66 shares size/height with bedding. Communal rail design differs from ordinary Bed by intent.", "Cabinet chest16-52 yields joined shell/boards/hardware from one size. Standing54-75 has shelves/back with cupboard-only doors; door77-127 computes meeting reveal/inset/width/height once and reuses hardware positions, no independently retained closed/open state. Furniture static cupboard leaves are different purpose from operable architectural DoorSpec. Seating3-48 derives backed/seat height from closed kind and one size; chair splats vs churchbench slab are design distinctions, not competing current posture facts.", "Tables trestle6-29/desk31-46/lectern48-60/altar81-94 build from same canonical envelope. slope62-79 derives angle, length and centre from front/back/depth then sends one solid geometry to builder; no separately editable pitch cache. Washing tub9-50 preserves real open basin via segment walls and inset bottom bars; decorative hoops independent from physical wall supports. Washstand52-71 deliberately has no loose basin, and projection furniture kind does not promise gameplay contents.", "Finish boards30-52 uses wood_state to choose actual replacement member/handled patch and one pitch/reveal, while face54-87 projects canonical grain and finish to material. worn_face89-163 REPLACES original face with recessed ring+octagonal patch; does not retain original duplicate skin. Wear patch/local normal is authored treatment, not physical collider authority; handled_timber167-182 forwards same wood_state and natural_timber184-193 intentionally preserves natural material on designated members. Physical member geometry and surface appearance are orthogonal.", "Domestic tests5-22 roster is fixture coverage selection, not production membership owner. Remaining tests compare envelope/feet/open-interior/lectern clearance to actual construction. Finish tests5-86 compare ALL key roundtrips and natural-vs-finish envelopes/colliders/clearances, expected finish material and winding. These source predicates document coherent design; equality tests are not the source of truth and were not executed. Existing fullkey immutable recipe owner228 is actual route, not verdict carry."], "disposition": "Exact immutable geometric recipes/intentional physical proxies/surface treatment roles compared; no new redundant current authority demonstrated.", "acceptance": "Keep one canonical input size/profile and coordinated builder output; preserve open interiors, decorative vs solid geometry and finish-only surface changes. Existing test fixtures are not new runtime authorities. No edits/execution.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-230", "at": "2026-10-23T05:14:02.707039+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope061_index": 572, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/horse_stop.rs", "sha256": "c912d7782b20603d3658528b6eb6b704dc8dea59daea250fde1dabc45fbeb5db", "actual_EOF": 66, "material_ranges": [[1, 66]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/572"}, {"scope061_index": 573, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/key.rs", "sha256": "68560fd1d33b92db2a172c28b5f9c20be60302d1251f468f861368384fac6b34", "actual_EOF": 174, "material_ranges": [[1, 174]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/573"}, {"scope061_index": 574, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/placement.rs", "sha256": "3046dce9dd37537c97964d0329a71828e4312db4cbfd7828e582a5716dbe213d", "actual_EOF": 37, "material_ranges": [[1, 37]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/574"}, {"scope061_index": 575, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/seating.rs", "sha256": "8d36b46a7aedc90cfe1ae2337dc58055b84b5e032ce7c8992e1436235d389586", "actual_EOF": 89, "material_ranges": [[1, 89]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/575"}, {"scope061_index": 576, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/spec.rs", "sha256": "a00ea9a2b6d58eddb090e18a78a9ef0c3b205ab9329ea61d2f4f3a7faf8ce2c6", "actual_EOF": 143, "material_ranges": [[1, 143]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/576"}, {"scope061_index": 577, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/stall.rs", "sha256": "5b82553e30a9eb80b27718205a79b793c11975d8db18ce9d453f9ecafe144515", "actual_EOF": 127, "material_ranges": [[1, 127]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/577"}, {"scope061_index": 578, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/stall/stock.rs", "sha256": "5f4859c84a4369dc1bb3f94402adb82d1425e024140b61768522778cb2371fb8", "actual_EOF": 73, "material_ranges": [[1, 73]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/578"}, {"scope061_index": 579, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/tests.rs", "sha256": "1656026306b4403e83e63f74b395479f8bccaec9c510ccc45f372c4218411113", "actual_EOF": 382, "material_ranges": [[1, 382]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/579"}, {"scope061_index": 580, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-building-generator/src/furniture/trade.rs", "sha256": "2f720c25a8f2e4eca05908e821f89b4e643124d1db3a7d09440b21f7df61e655", "actual_EOF": 60, "material_ranges": [[1, 60]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-061.json#/files/580"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full horse66/key174/placement37/seating89/spec143/stall127/stock73/tests382/trade60, every SHA checked. Supporting current furniture enum/rosters/recipe228 and builder228 actualsource facts personally compared; no prior lens verdict.", "contracts": ["FurnitureKey67-71 stores kind/variant/wood_state independent authored axes; valid finished combinations use FinishableFurnitureKind as restricted selector and checked KeyFields decode163-172. COUNT104-107 and ALL108-142 derive cartesian product from actual rosters, so there is no second separately authored list of all130 keys. However kind enum, ALL/OUTDOOR/INTERIOR, finishable roster and bidirectional kind mappings still independently declare membership; F045 records current agreement and concrete future omission effect in actual immutable recipe lookup, not current missing entry.", "InteriorFurnitureSpec1-143 intentionally owns independent PLACEMENT envelope and required access policy. Current geometry builders consume same size to construct fitted objects, while working depth0.75/loompress1.1/spinning1 are purposeful usable space outside visible bounds. required_faces is authored per kind, not inferable from current mesh triangles. placement_role133-141 follows catalogue role not geometry. Do not derive envelope from mesh or remove access reservation as duplicate bounds. Actual access_bounds22-49 projects same enum face+dimensions+depth into one admitted local rectangle.", "ArchitecturalFurniturePose10-35 stores only target centre/yaw and transforms each local cuboid on demand, preserving sourceID/local dimensions/crossfall/longfall and re-admitting transformed centre/summed yaw. Local frame versus architectural frame is real owner distinction, not duplicate current position. No native matrix retained independently in this helper.", "Horse assemble8-40 derives beam/trough/access+working space from one variant length. Trough42-66 deliberately renders contained water without solid fill, retaining physical rim/ends/bottom. Seating table_and_benches8-31 derives all components/clearances from one length, individual tables33-55 and benches57-73 use common slatted top75-89, explicit solid collisionproxy for decorative gaps. Width/depth/height are distinct design dimensions, not competing policy tables.", "Stall canopy13-78 uses actual one halfwidth/eave/ridge, shared counterheight/centre constants10-11 passed to table AND stock. Canvas91-127 adds visual sag from same supports; no solid cloth roof collision. Stock5-73 derives supported bins/sack from same variant/counterconstants, grain heap visually projected with simplified collider, authored stock decoration is not strategic inventory quantity authority. Tests5-382 use independent geometric projections/SAT/support fixedpoint plus known expecteddimensions to assess outputs; fixtures do not introduce another runtime authority. All tests source-only.", "Trade12-33 obtains same canonical interior spec then exhaustive-category dispatch to counters/work/racks/storage. Fourleg helper36-49 and beam51-60 are direct geometric construction, no saved mutable derived frame. Remaining delegated lower recipe bodies remain own later scoped obligations, not covered by module declarations."], "finding_refs": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F045"], "disposition": "Exact key/cache membership, independent placement envelopes and design geometry compared; F045 maintenance-authority strengthening with no current mismatch.", "acceptance": "One canonical kind/finishability declaration should drive rosters/partition/lookup/inverse adapters while preserving authored order, complete key cartesian product, errors and distinct mesh/placement/working space policies. No implementation/runtime/testing.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
