explicitly overwritten246-256 with same computed depth_sign before function returns, not an independently retained wrong branch.", "Clerestory8-122 derives actual masonry walls/host solids/support nodes from same roofhigh contour with deliberate0.24 upstand and0.90 thickness, not synthetic proof plane. Temporary lower_supports snapshots sorted dedup IDs from current immutable inputs before each newwall. Wallframe/host geometry assigned together. allow(dead_code) means no actual live caller established; do not infer current active cathedral route from source presence.", "Churchground resolve18-36 consumes whole BuildingPlan by value, derives temporary Envelope from current exterior walls/apse facets/tower metadata, replaces occupiedstorey, relabels BOTH actualwall frames and opening roomframes93-100, and replacesfloor solids plus interface records216-286 before returning plan. No returned partialplan on Err. ROOM_KINDS and room IDs0-4 are local encoding policy shared by room() and occupied_storey, currentexactmapping explicit; finefloor tiles versus majority-voted coarsecells deliberately different resolution. Cached envelope is private temporary with no independent updater. Floor refs church.floor_solids and choir.floor_solids are assigned together283-284. Interface ID removal uses oldlow+1 while new IDs use index; repeat-invocation identity stability is not proven by this one construction body, so no idempotency or actual normal staleinterface claim. No unrelated future geometry graph expanded.", "Window schedule7-87 authors one profile per real bay/range/facet; distinct nave/clerestory/choir/transept/apse sizes are intentional design content. Actual churchwindows14-485 receives that profile, binds all repeated widths/spring/apex/radius/sill through local values, removes previoushost solids/interfaces35-43, constructs checkedmembers/supports/voids/reveals/glazing, updates wall.host_solids/openingIDs438-439 and returns OpeningAssembly440-484 with same profile/frame/