or snapshot. Portals635 ensure_node128-146 coordinates insertion across nodes/edges/lookup in one operation; existing keyed nodes retain their original point. connect148-152 coordinates both undirected edges. Room-node membership is collected AFTER all doorway/stair insertions (Navigation45-65); new67-69 verifies fresh flood. Floors/nodes are module-visible but the actual builder/query paths examined do not mutate coordinates after building these indices. No current hot-edit or stale-cache defect follows from visibility alone. Exact bit keys intentionally retain signed-zero/bit lookup policy, not approximate geometric identity.", "Occupancy634 owns immutable &Navigation plus private node/edge counts and precomputed same-storey edge sweep rectangles. add59-85 increments each affected occurrence and returns an owned Change containing those exact indices; remove88-95 consumes that receipt and subtracts the same occurrences. Multiple simultaneous blockers are counts, not redundant booleans. Actual furnish63718-74 owns nav, occupancy and layout together: records previous placement length, validates architecture against already-accepted prefix, adds ONLY new suffix, on failed room/access verification removes exact Change then truncates exact suffix. Accepted suffix stays in both layout/counts. Fallible add failure propagates out of furnish and drops private local state, not an externally retained partially published graph. Final paths derive from final occupancy.flood; later finish assignment changes finish keys, while current finish/spec contract229 keeps physical envelope independent of finish. No normal transition with one collection changed and another retained was found.", "Footprints631 validates accepted prefix optimization only under explicit precondition6-7. Actual637 previous=len satisfies it, with no previously admitted placement mutation in candidate loop. New objects recheck old required-face access17-29; each new object checks physical support/room/obstacles/old footprints and all current access intersections31-94. Public validate_layout63776-88 deliberately uses accepted=0, rebuilds Navigation and floods actual placements; serialized layout.paths are NOT trusted. Cached returned paths remain useful output/history of compiled layout, not the authority for revalidation. Existing incremental/full and occupancy/reference tests were read as independent source oracles, not run or used as replacement proof.", "Portals635 derives entrances from current workplace passage or actual exterior Door/Gate opening, wall thickness, current sill/profile. Threshold vs inset approach are different navigation points, not competing door locations. represented_storey351-360 delegates current elevation and plan storey-height. Straight and spiral transitions are real different topology contracts; no attempt to force spiral landings into straight stair arithmetic. Portal elbow/sweep checks construct transient rectangles from same coordinates before insertion; no retained route-exists flag detached from graph.", "Obstruction636 consumes cuboid by value, computes corners and bounds/vertical extrema/footprint from the SAME topology17-72 and keeps all private, no independent source mutation or setter. footprint is a cheap broad rejection; rectangle/projection clips actual corners+edges at requested height before exact overlap135-154. Whole horizontal bounds vs height-clipped projection intentionally differ. Source ID is diagnostic provenance, not mutable owner identity. Current test tilted beam demonstrates intended different height projections, source only.", "Placement637 candidates derive all members from canonical FurnitureKey/spec and room cells. Desired budget versus count of accepted GROUPS is intentional (composition may produce multiple furniture pieces), not an incorrect member count cache. Prototype group bounds locate candidates, final compose(current placement) reconstructs actual group before validation, no mutable prototype is retained as accepted output. Candidate score/seed/tie are selection policy and not authority for final validity. RoomFacing638 derives current room-cell mean and audience/chancel direction on demand; preferred facing vs per-position WardBed opposite is deliberate placement policy, not stale duplicate yaw. Pulpit opposite orientation and forward location score represent different relationships."], "disposition": "Actual authoritative architecture -> immutable navigation/prepared geometry -> coordinated candidate add/remove -> regenerated access paths compared; no new redundant-authority finding in exact roles.", "acceptance": "Retain private immutable prepared snapshots and actual Change ownership; externally edited/serialized layouts must rebuild proof from authoritative plan and placements. No source edits/tests/runtime.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
