may have been written first. Tests source-read for alias rejection/reload, never run. Invalid path/source error is not a second stored design state.", "Metal692 classifies exact catalogue plate-steel materials then constructs Metal from canonical clothing_material714 pbr color/roughness, remaining procedural finish settings from Metal::default. Author-editable metal versus catalogue steel with own engraving are intentionally different choices. UV scale uses actual current surface/texture edge lengths and canonical TILES_PER_METRE; trim coordinates use SAME scale with actual trim period/origin. Decoration versus geometry/skin remain orthogonal, no requirement material UVs equal anatomical UVs.", "F049: shared polished-steel default color and roughness independently hardcoded in7145 and220631-32. Metal::default explicitly polished steel27-28;69295-99 test expects exact equality with catalogue PolishedSteel, current values agree. Actual69225-33 builds retained catalogue Metal by overriding default fields with palette, so one-sided edit to either declaration makes two intended same default products differ. Equality test detects but does not eliminate duplicate source policy. Scope is common polished color/roughness ONLY: full procedural Metal contains additional scratch/engraving semantics and other palette materials are distinct. Do not collapse whole Metal and RGBA/metallic/roughness tuple, or silently change artist color space/oxidized metallic policy.", "MetalTextures220688-103 public native texture products carry output size/channels/depth; these are codec/render buffers, not evidence an independent gameplay material owner. Full688/689/690/692/693 scoped tests read source-only, no execution and no admission/geometry guarantees swept clear by this07 comparison."], "disposition": "Authored override/placement and frame/morph distinctions compared; current polished-steel default policy duplicated F049 with present values agreeing.", "acceptance": "Use one canonical common polished-steel base preset for both products, retaining authored override precedence, procedural finish additions, color-space and material distinctions. No source/tests/runtime.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-251", "at": "2026-10-23T05:58:25.063767+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope063_index": 694, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/armory.rs", "sha256": "aa66e0b18f919eb3351635241249df969eeed4c36c36aa302888c320222a54df", "actual_EOF": 485, "material_ranges": [[1, 485]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/694"}, {"scope063_index": 695, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/armory_scene.rs", "sha256": "ece71ad33e583d6908d9ad2db842ffa724b97e8d498a19258602836608b093a3", "actual_EOF": 288, "material_ranges": [[1, 288]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/695"}, {"scope063_index": 696, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/armory_ui.rs", "sha256": "5c519edc1b220e1bdb7d874160b997ffb77a98266e5f6c5de49565d4ab5e9ada", "actual_EOF": 332, "material_ranges": [[1, 332]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/696"}, {"scope063_index": 697, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/bare_body.rs", "sha256": "68cef7d12e388a580394d74d3162513902fc9a8c6539ae328aac33e1240bd4cb", "actual_EOF": 71, "material_ranges": [[1, 71]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/697"}, {"scope063_index": 816, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/lib.rs", "sha256": "dc0c4f7b59ecd62d3a8a4a6b00c5bfecfc15470df833fe4294e486d1ffa5393c", "actual_EOF": 238, "material_ranges": [[1, 238]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/816"}, {"scope063_index": 820, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/model_controls.rs", "sha256": "f52b873a70ee6fd3ac34fc78e3acb63fac9b6466d973114ca313fe066105b5ae", "actual_EOF": 40, "material_ranges": [[1, 40]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/820"}], "supporting_exact_roles": [{"scope063_index": 819, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/main.rs", "sha256": "41961ead92363687fdd3286fe6e6d55a11fb00fc67c53a64cf5dada05d4090b9", "actual_EOF": 667, "material_ranges": [[98, 103], [408, 455]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-063.json#/files/819"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full694485 two chunks/695288/696332 with Unicode output recovery88-332/69771/816238/82040; hashes verified. Fresh bounded already-global81998-103/408-455, no whole667 credit. Original scoped tests source only.", "contracts": ["Armory694 Exhibit.loaded is actual catalogue design when armory opened, explicitly temporal revert snapshot, not expected to track future catalogue edits. Current catalog.design plus each placement fitted Result are active outputs. Region/steel/name copied from canonical immutable catalogue identity on exhibits406-430; current UI only edits design, not item material/slot/identity. Display grouping manual Region::ALL is ordered UI policy, current all six variants present; no actual present missing region or extra gameplay classification authority. Stale flag is pending work request, not equivalent to fitted Result success.", "Actual696 editor184-210 obtains current design, performs controls/revert, calls set_default; ONLY successful setter calls armory.refit(index), which marks exhibit stale and defaults_changed694197-200. Current694354-365 refits exact stale list against same cached body and actual current catalog design, writes fitted Results and clears pending flag, resets arranged. Both-sides display695185-188 compares current selection to cached arranged value, while fit changes reset it, so normal geometry/bothside dependencies are explicitly covered. select requests camera frame but does not silently change same frame metadata. Body/OnBody versus wall offset are different projection purposes; native current entity transforms derive same actual exhibit.offset195-202.", "Body697 private key retains recipe minus inventory/name, plus model LOD/corrective selection. Inventory/name do not define generated bare body. Key is captured with actual generated character and is_current compares desired inputs, no separate ready classification claiming equal current recipe. Enter694296-299 checks key before refit; normal model controls820 change selectedLOD/correctives. Fresh exact main81998-103/408-455 shows model owns actual Mhr plus LOD/correctives, actual reload skips identical selection, uses process Args.assets, replaces whole model only on success and dirty=true; on failure resets requested selection to loaded model. This closes ordinary model-setting dependency, NOT arbitrary external Mhr/file hot replacement or asset revision guarantee. No new foreign source graph or body model equality inferred from same counts.", "Full refit694335-352 consumes pending request then attempts new BareBody. Failure emits explicit status and returns retaining last good body/output, rather than publishing new generated body with old key. ready is merely body present, not a seal it matches every requested input. Construction/finish respawn removes old entities then spawn_exhibit695 may fail/partially enqueue;694384-387 records error in fitted[0] and memoizes attempted finish. This is attempted success/error result handling, not a proven successful-applied finish bit. No unconditional automatic retry or rollback promise established; manual Refit all remains available. Preserve qualified partial publication/error-source limitations for operation/type-granularity review, do not call finished successful geometry when failed.", "FinishFor694208-216 only selected steel gets temporary construction/decoration, others plain default; changing selection re-evaluates actual finish equality and respawns previous/new selected items. This is deliberate preview override, separate from inventory article construction. Body material caches ghost application plus actual material handle, updates coloralpha AND alpha_mode and remembered flag together695204-217. Native asset resource mutation outside owning preview not proven. Scene display reapplies active tab visibility to character/pieces/body/light each call, no cached active boolean surviving tab changes.", "Scene695 spawn_exhibit uses actual fitted placement and actual selected design/material/decoration, then construction/trim native geometry; present entity marker binds exhibit+placement indices and transform only adds current wall offset. Labels696300-331 derive current bounds/errors and marker ID, no stored alternate rendered name. Bounds/tris are computed from current fitted product; camera target distinct wall versus actual-body frame. Fitting failures are explicit Result and red UI, no substitution unknown item defaults from this path.", "Lib816 exports canonical Core item schema/rig APIs, not parallel schema copy. CharacterRecipe stores authored desired shape/identity/expression/inventory and version; DEFAULT sets current version constant14, coefficients count from canonical IDENTITY_MORPH_COUNT and local EXPRESSION_COUNT72. IdentityGroup ranges form UI partition, no copied second body geometry in this file. Actual validation/reset helpers operate stored recipe, not generated output. README249 version13 is stale versus current816 RECIPE_VERSION14; documentation synchronization debt retained, no compatibility reader or runtime multiple-version authority added. Default new adventurer inventory versus canonical naked mhr_base fixture are different authored starting presets.", "Existing full695/816 inline tests and all688/697 source facts compared without project execution. Main819 only exact98-103/408-455 supportive read; surrounding imports/Studio prefix85-112 and previous-function tail404-407 and testmodule prefix457-464 displayed as context, not analyzed/credited. Whole main667 remains pending inventory. Global063 new Native keepcore/bearings/tests remain independent pending07 despite source metadata publication."], "disposition": "Actual armory requested state, last-good/failed outputs and compiled snapshot lifetimes distinguished; normal design/body/finish/bothside update paths compared. No new redundant-authority finding; exact failed-publication limits retained.", "acceptance": "Retain loaded temporal snapshot versus current catalogue ownership, explicit invalidation request/result distinctions and captured body key. Do not label failed finish as successfully applied or assume transaction/retry promises; exact later lens limitations preserved. No edits/tests/runtime.", "source_repair": "frozen", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
