}], "prospective_registration": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-REG043 studio_ui202-302 read only AFTER registration, old350-430 not implied covered", "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete698-706,786 before compaction; fresh complete762312/763131/79493/831192/832187 in this continuation. Fresh bounded819408-455 and2321 exact stated ranges, no whole819/2321 credit. REG043 output202-302 freshly read after prospective registration. UTF8/CP1252 failed-output recovery completed. Original test source699/703 only, no execution.", "contracts": ["Forearm698119 typed side resolves canonical rig family; owns_forearm family versus supports_boundary including wrist/upperarm are distinct query purposes. Morph samples pair name/positions/normals/exact globals/body inputs, input validation compares actual row/joint lengths. No independently mutable cached validity flag.", "Original ignored chainmail export test69988 explicitly requires MHR/measured drape. Its one fitted garment belongs to one loadout and checked generated body, not proof for arbitrary lists or installed runtime. It is read source only. Production700248 generates current loadout/body/morph/armor/lining once, prepares fitted garments, validates actual body/inner topology as warnings, then emits native export products.", "Actual78637-69 processes ordered inputs and appends only successful garment; FIRST error immediately returns finished prefix. It never skips a failed middle article and resumes later successes. Thus normal701 None->drape_outfit export and worker outputs remain the prefix associated by ordinal in700224-248 current loadout. Missing garment warnings are deliberate partial-result policy, not a false success seal. The earlier potential middle-hole material mismatch is closed for this actual normal producer.", "762 DrapeJob.request24-27 queues request and clears ready. 763 request55-59 marks old worker cancelled, replaces pending, clears latest; poll104-108 publishes ONLY noncancelled completion. Queued tags unzip with inputs113-114, and actual762201 preview zip uses those tags. Finished outcome190 may be a success prefix with problems; documented running is pending/running, deliberately not all-success. Mail refresh actual762299-308 resolves current article by ID, cache keys actual full MailWeave77/124, retaining only four entries is eviction not alternative material truth.", "831 drape key129-142 stores serialized current body key, lining fit keys, ordered article ID/selection/drape, so successful832 regeneration sees relevant loadout/order/body changes and requests new job before publication71. Private request signature only exposes ordered inputs; current UI supplied-ready path834248-258 is guarded by dirty/running and explicit producer chain, not arbitrary trust from a Vec name. 701 Some(fitted) is a raw supplied artifact API; it does not prove correspondence to an arbitrary caller recipe. Existing body/inner validation reports warnings rather than inventing a new hard acceptance promise.", "831 fit_keys152-182 follows canonical LayerPlan order, keys actual piece item/selection/design plus lower SUPPORT finished keys; finish key185-192 includes decoration/construction. Lining depends on ordered rigid-fit keys, body change clears all dependent caches50-54. These are coordinated actual positive invalidation paths; fit cache remove on fallible processing can lose memoized work, no successful wrong-output proof from removal alone. One model dependency omitted, F050 below.", "832 clears dirty35 BEFORE fallible preparation38-59. On preparation failure status changes and old scene/ready can remain; UI834237 thereafter may enable export when no worker active. Actual700 export regenerates current data and may itself reject, so this proves completion/eligibility flag is request-consumed rather than successful-current-artifact seal, not unconditional bad exported output. Connected cache ownership should retain successful generation key separately from request dirty and bind ready to that key; failure must not certify currentness. No normal failed export/run reproduced.", "703 MorphDelta target names and deltas derive from SAME ordered sample generation. SkeletalFitMorph body target zero and per-clothing/hair remove_skeletal_translation are complementary residual versus bone motion, not duplicate full-motion authorities. Same strongest_four output policy computes removed bone term. 704 fixed barycentric transfer samples are captured from the same current base garment/body and reused only within that immutable morph conversion; deformed normals recomputed per target. 705 actual carried head placement similarly subtracts skeleton term. No mutable persistent body-keyless sampling cache defined here.", "700 full Metal value equality deduplicates operation-local baked maps. Actual current palette overwrites temporary703244-246 polished color/roughness before shell export at700177-179, actual trim override195-197. Therefore those temporary defaults are not a proven third live F049 owner. Hardware materials are explicit component overrides. 702 process OnceLock headless GPU result is immutable backend lifetime/error memoization, no promised hot shader replacement; groom/head fitting and generated morphs own current target rows, flat normals are native format policy.", "706 CLI LOD default/range reuse canonical constants; args paths and requested export artifacts are independent request configuration, not alternative current simulation state. No CLI launched."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F050"], "qualifications": ["Cancellation/prefix normal route established; no generic list-hole defect. Failed prepare flag semantics retained explicitly without unconditional export claim.", "Current-source own07 comparison only; no other lens credit."], "status": "Discovery complete exact stated roles; repair/project execution frozen"}
