 [[1, 79]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/752"}, {"scope065_index": 761, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_wrapped_tasset.rs", "sha256": "dc575790bf67f066d6c4dfd64c61f158383fc04efb95bc5dfd3633fe2ce17033", "actual_EOF": 339, "material_ranges": [[1, 339]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/761"}, {"scope065_index": 2202, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/fabelgeist-armor/src/gpu/wrapped_tasset_carrier.wgsl", "sha256": "d2769977cd06ab462c3180b8faf97efd4b55c067d626ff300078d8a6baa6409d", "actual_EOF": 64, "material_ranges": [[1, 64]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/2202"}, {"scope065_index": 2203, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/fabelgeist-armor/src/gpu/wrapped_tasset_shape.wgsl", "sha256": "6bf36983d7b2fe90b22fd0e5bccd860aa4e951be3fd90828a85c87438f8f6c40", "actual_EOF": 55, "material_ranges": [[1, 55]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/2203"}, {"scope065_index": 2204, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/fabelgeist-armor/src/gpu/wrapped_tassets.rs", "sha256": "e3b42051512367ece0bf95da50fe255586f90159da138fc22385ba5304ba62b9", "actual_EOF": 154, "material_ranges": [[1, 154]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/2204"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete747327/748212/74934/75059/75146/75279/761339/220264/220355/2204154. Source fingerprints verified. Original source tests only, no native/project execution.", "contracts": ["747 head frame deliberately uses fixed-order host_float native arithmetic for finite-difference sensitivity, while generic732 Head rule has ordinary native arithmetic. Both derive the same semantic frame purpose but numeric execution policies are explicit and need not be collapsed by textual similarity. Current producer allocates fresh frame/reductions, records TOP->ORIENT->BOUNDS->FINISH and shares actual generated failure/threshold constants. Head envelope uses owned skin, whole-body top bounds orientation: distinct measurements, no stale stored head size independent of current inputs.", "748 limb fit creates a current frame and part, then proximal trim bounds from actual current shell carriers and immutable shell range map. TRIM_BOUNDS dispatch precedes TRIM in same batch; changing carriers after measured bounds is the operation itself, not a cached input claiming to remain current afterward. Cuisse/rerebrace trim followed by clearance fit, generic device_fit records final shells after modifications. Positive minimum remaining span is shape policy, not an extra body-length authority. Left/right outward sign is explicit numerical port of canonical side.", "749 DeviceRecording retains pending part, frames and deferred checks. Its docs explicitly say validity known only after batch run; it is not an accepted completed token. Actual device_fit254 reads frame/device checks before finished part and mesh checks after staged materialization. Deferred validator closures carry needed original facts, not independently editable success flags. No success inferred merely from recording creation.", "750 hull sorts/deduplicates current sample list, then produces convex envelope and radius query. Hull is an operation-local conservative projection, not equivalent editable copy of original support point set. 752 sections choose current thigh/waist/layer samples or actual triangle slices, write hull count and corresponding hull coordinates in same invocation, reject fewer than3/excess corners. Count is actual output size for native variable-layout read, not a redundant cached business classification.", "761 Support is private and constructed once from immutable wearer/design/layers/suspension. Current point prefix bounds thigh_end/waist_end are assigned immediately after append; metadata spans, node counts and geometric arrays are paired in one factory. Layers include an intentional copied waist region in shared layer fitting envelope, not pretending duplicated points are independent actors or inventory items. Checked top>bottom and support span are actual local gates; arithmetic/all-API finite limits remain other lenses, not claimed by type names.", "761 record_wrapped_tassets constructs actual left/right products separately with matching order, passes exact fit/status pair to canonical2204; copies both statuses into final part and captures original per-side measured spans for final mesh validation225-230. This closes original versus post-extrusion support correlation: validation uses final shell positions, deliberately does not recompute a weaker new allowable span from output. Captured span is immutable constraint history, not stale current geometry cache.", "2204 layout defines actual measured26 including final waist, radii64, derived word counts and hull stride, emitted for current751/752 producers and actual2202/2203 consumers. Literal 25/24 in current control selection describes first25 thigh rows plus special waist endpoint; current coherent. No assertion arbitrary row-count edit is already installed or all row groups are semantically interchangeable. Native fixed layout coordinates remain explicit source-level coupling, not whole-unit type inference.", "2202 carrier_point combines measured quadratic controls, exact body hull envelope and optional lower-layer envelope in distinct stages. 751 controls derive a deliberately compact quadratic approximation plus outward allowance from measured rows; original samples/hull and approximation are different-purpose constrained products. 2203 rejects final points outside captured support and nonpositive sections; exploratory bracket probes can use signed extrapolated radii without poisoning final status, as actual220240-43 docs specify.", "2204 record_boundaries solves inner angle once per course row and stores it in SAME actual fit;2203 chart_point reads cached row solve to avoid recomputation across columns. Caching itself is justified. But host repeats course span/overlap policy in recipe creation and precompute dispatch, F054; one-sided edits can separate cached solve axial from actual chart axial. Current duplicated expressions agree and no current wrong output is asserted."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F054"], "status": "Exact current07 inventory WITH_FINDING; no other-lens or execution credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-262", "at": "2026-10-23T06:25:06.870142+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 753, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_torso.rs", "sha256": "78af7acbb8b527b1d3f6ee10c15b101334e9423e7da77ad40283325c2e9579a5", "actual_EOF": 342, "material_ranges": [[1, 342]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/753"}, {"scope065_index": 754, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_torso_wgsl.rs", "sha256": "4dffbe38bb680f965cffc46852aae9e943835b6757ac34145233a7cc8c25d467", "actual_EOF": 258, "material_ranges": [[1, 258]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/754"}, {"scope065_index": 826, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/rig_parameters.rs", "sha256": "f16955ae53a597eebce8b190c050f47e10671e50fb6f8426ce7bbed3164f14cc", "actual_EOF": 81, "material_ranges": [[1, 81]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/826"}, {"scope065_index": 836, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/torso_domain.rs", "sha256": "d00dd8818cff04db09a6da07ec1bb8e88270b85d88677532a01352ce9ad68209", "actual_EOF": 188, "material_ranges": [[1, 188]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/836"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full753342/754258/82681/836188 actual source, fingerprints verified, original tests source only. No compute execution.", "contracts": ["753 TorsoSurfaceInput is a borrowed current realization; check validates paired counts before required landmark resolution. LANDMARKS and JOINT_PARAMETERS are different facts: authored rig identity versus shader parameter role, joined by fixed slot in actual record_torso296-298. 826 explicitly documents distinction8-9 and maps typed roles to native joint0..8 with checked ordinal conversion78. They must not be unified as one semantic name just because current TorsoLeftClavicle happens to bind actual L_CLAVICLE. A paired table may improve association clarity, but no current duplicated authority defect established from two different-purpose lists.", "753 SUPPORT_JOINTS includes upper arms/thighs as conservative per-vertex front fitting support. 836 TorsoSkinDomain uses torso eight plus explicit limb exclusion and per-triangle mean thresholds .08/.35 to choose candidate faces. Its docs3-4 explicitly exclude bearing footprint/attachment/sliding authority. 754 WIDTHS and SUPPORT additionally use current normals, frame coordinates and support weight .2. Thus these rosters/thresholds are separate candidate topology, width measurement and fitted front region policies; do not collapse them into one body-part classification or call current disagreement a defect.", "836 triangle_indices enumerates ORIGINAL face indices, retaining duplicate triangles as distinct original identities. It validates current topology/skin values, computes per-vertex torso/limb totals, then mean per face in one call; returned ordered candidate list is an immutable projection of supplied skin, not an independently editable retained eligibility cache in owner. Actual753 maps those indices to current faces and passes BOTH exact indices and current face geometry to native breastplate fitting. Duplicate geometry does not mean duplicate triangle identity here.", "753 fresh GpuBody upload and seams/atlas inputs are created for the same current body; 754 FRAME->WIDTHS->RANK->HALF_WIDTH->SUPPORT executed in actual317-323 order. Counter is actual number of eligible width samples in that batch, frame[13] is ranked ninetieth percentile chosen with original vertex-index tie ordering. Normalized lateral semantic coordinate derives that width only AFTER width status check; these are temporary exact staged projections, not competing enduring measurements.", "754 torso frame is lower-spine origin/vertical extent/clavicle lateral/eye-facing front, distinct from standard PartFrame half-extents layout despite both native arrays. Rig anchors are separate downstream fitting inputs, not required identical to fitted envelope. Native status constants come from canonical753 definitions through formatting50-52; error messages retain original class. No independent manually editable status code mirrors like F053.", "753 morph loop uploads current sample positions while native breastplate owns its established topology/semantic domain; names gathered from exact same input slice256-260. Final read then canonical skin_rules applied to returned armor. Base versus endpoint coordinates and rig ownership are intentional different facts; no current source-backed stale per-morph domain promise inferred without lower algorithm proof. Native breastplate deep body not newly credited here; actual current constructor/operation/receiving adapter is explicit.", "826 RigPassParameters converts only at actual native uniform port. Parameter Display is machine ABI token, not localized human prose controlling game behavior. Joint label/part matching remains in canonical authored RigJointName owner. Error propagation from u32 conversion preserved; no early raw primitive retained state is introduced in this adapter."], "findings": [], "status": "Exact current07 inventory; distinct authority purposes preserved, no new finding or other-lens credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-263", "at": "2026-10-23T06:26:49.267942+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 755, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer.rs", "sha256": "b42e82c29ce8e08f7e378abc16f0f9823aea7c2580456c37cbaa4084ea781591", "actual_EOF": 416, "material_ranges": [[1, 416]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/755"}, {"scope065_index": 756, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer/plan.rs", "sha256": "7eb172df559ec4825c756c36b416e163b5703de648a9e6a84af309ca71c56fe9", "actual_EOF": 156, "material_ranges": [[1, 156]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/756"}, {"scope065_index": 757, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer/shell.rs", "sha256": "705ca4896f9e3b459881a3ffb190e7878f3f3a34b348b2ec7e2c248bb977d4b3", "actual_EOF": 274, "material_ranges": [[1, 274]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/757"}, {"scope065_index": 758, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer/tests.rs", "sha256": "fd8179b3a282dda66fc89a706bc4941a3153e9d96fa03dbe3519734534090a31", "actual_EOF": 341, "material_ranges": [[1, 341]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/758"}, {"scope065_index": 759, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer/wgsl.rs", "sha256": "073d5ef4150b8cb02e931b270d6618caef2445135a7357482eb0e848d4aa8719", "actual_EOF": 86, "material_ranges": [[1, 86]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/759"}, {"scope065_index": 760, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/device_underlayer/workspace.rs", "sha256": "7e94d4b4a91f817e93d5b64d77f218425609896af1cada1ab2ef7aa2b1f6160a", "actual_EOF": 90, "material_ranges": [[1, 90]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/760"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh complete755416 in1-240/241-416,756156/757274/758341/75986/76090, fingerprints checked. Original fixture source only; no native/device/test execution. No child direction/gap/standoff/sweep/weld implementation body credit from mod declarations.", "contracts": ["755 public fit_async builds current device wearer, resolves actual required frames, creates CutPlan once from current design/body/domain, then passes immutable references into private Fit. Cut topology is intentionally frozen from base body, while each realization only moves matching barycentric source points. It is not expected to re-cut every morph, because that would break common vertex/triangle correspondence. Current positions and captured topology describe different shape versus connectivity facts.", "756 CutPlan::from_cut constructs point table, two-layer indices, cut-edge shading sources and point_count in one operation from same SurfaceCut. Additional cut-edge vertices intentionally share physical layer source points but have independent shading normals; duplicate positions are not competing physical identities. point_count equals cut.points length, table rows each9 words, while vertex_count uses sources length and triangle_count derives indices length. Distinct cardinalities must not be collapsed. Public plan fields are raw and independently editable API data, but actual public fit path never accepts an externally mutated CutPlan: it constructs then borrows it into private Fit. No fabricated bad normal producer claimed.", "756 incidence derives actual ascending triangle lists once from immutable shared faces; current body connectivity is explicitly fixed across realizations. 760 Workspace borrows plan and uploads corresponding table/sources once; vertex/face counts come from actual input lengths at construction. Scratch buffer reuse is documented submission-order lifetime, not persistent body-revision-free cache. No ability to mutate borrowed original plan while workspace uses it in this actual private path.", "755 normal/proportion/morph positions have matching counts checked before work. It records base constraints, all static proportion constraint sets, then constrained directions and standoff; sample-specific weld/standoff updates feed one frozen compression envelope by documented design. Morph-specific constraints/directions are separately produced, while offset envelope remains intended conservative shared fit. This is temporal constraint accumulation versus current per-realization geometry, not two current state owners. Exact implementation/termination/collision guarantees of unscoped child helpers are not inferred from comments or recorded calls.", "755 shells iterates actual ordered realizations, writes same shell scratch then copies positions/normals/status into per-realization offset slices BEFORE next overwrite. Complete final read creates base then ordered endpoints from those buffers, actual status and finite positions checked. Source normal arrays are shading directions, final area-weighted normals are computed output geometry; they need not equal input. Stored endpoints versus base are intended distinct morph states, not duplicate same-time position authority.", "757 actual record_layers sends plan.vertex_count and point_count for different roles: output source row versus physical cut point modulo/layer division. Native table stride derives canonical POINT_WORDS, skin stride derives canonical INFLUENCES and SKIN_FLOATS. Both generation and conversion consume same constants; no separate editable numeric mirror established. record_skin merges actual three-corner influences by joint identity, chooses strongest8 with lower-joint tie policy, normalizes retained weights, and reports no-influence failure. This is lossy native influence projection by explicit policy, not unrestricted duplicate source skin.", "759 FitFailure defines bits once and generates WGSL status constants from exact variants, with actual755 check_status iterating same declared list. Current ALL lists all5 values; no current absent flag or differing native discriminator. This is positive shared source pattern distinct from F053 manually repeated selector values. Message text is diagnostic, not a classifier controlling behavior.", "758 fixtures deliberately test a frozen topology and envelope against base/proportion/morph deformations; input normal tilts and duplicate seam vertices are intentionally varied observations. assert_closed recomputes independent verification from final output, not cached gameplay authority. All original tests were read only; no assertion execution or new cases."], "findings": [], "status": "Exact current07 source inventory; intentional frozen constraints and private immutable lifetime distinguished; no new finding or other-lens credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-264", "at": "2026-10-23T06:28:55.550410+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 764, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/equipment_catalog.rs", "sha256": "da3139ef3625393db9041ad0680dc244b0f81235b86ea4519a87c9299763bdd6", "actual_EOF": 146, "material_ranges": [[1, 146]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/764"}, {"scope065_index": 765, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/equipment_export.rs", "sha256": "a8541e9383d61945925725c89b8c8c6cc448ddd898fa2538379cf18a075d19e3", "actual_EOF": 343, "material_ranges": [[1, 343]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/765"}, {"scope065_index": 766, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/equipment_layers.rs", "sha256": "2b9b34141b3bd8d1b9bc98b9db3af749035fa68190e135d31183a2c89fd70b86", "actual_EOF": 244, "material_ranges": [[1, 244]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/766"}, {"scope065_index": 922, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-core/src/equipment_assets.rs", "sha256": "0c7bd7e45c9a145954daf97ac6f0c2caa23bda96e9731a5ff033a2a3ce4a9365", "actual_EOF": 107, "material_ranges": [[1, 107]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/922"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full764146/765343/766244/922107 with actual fingerprints verified. One shell process-launch failure produced no source output or writes; identical read retried successfully. Original tests source only, no export/filesystem mutation/application run.", "contracts": ["764 EquipmentItemSelection stores references into immutably borrowed catalogue IDs and tests current CatalogItem identity by spelling; Rust borrow prevents editing those catalogue strings while selection lives. Empty filters deliberately mean all, duplicates in source catalogue remain selected by documented policy18-19. Selection is a request subset rather than one mutable competing copy of all catalogue state. ItemCatalog public items/designs remain raw authoring container, no automatic private accepted seal from constructor name.", "766 LayerPlan builds private direct dependency graph and topological order in one factory from exact supplied placements, rejects reciprocal or nonlocal cycles. Supports are direct geometric surfaces, ancestors transitive reconstruction prerequisites, and order stable for unrelated inputs; these are different derived graph queries. Original placements can be owned elsewhere but plan is explicitly indices into supplied slice; current831/765 callers construct/consume same invocation. No actual later changed-placement reuse path established here.", "766 authored layers_over intentionally overrides channel rank, permitting boot enclosing hose despite ordinary channel layering. Geometric supports_location extends shoulder/limb/neck contact beyond equal occupancy location; it is not the same as equipment occupancy conflict/parent attachment policy. Do not collapse separate predicates just because their enum tags overlap. Existing831 fit-key producer incorporates direct lower finished keys recursively, matching actual plan dependencies; original source tests read only.", "765 exporter owns one current model/recipe/generated/morph batch; per-item armor fits current selected placement/design, derives manifest metadata from same returned product. Native rigged shell color/roughness/textures override temporary defaults before export and component hardware may override again by explicit actual role. Coverage scalar is summary estimate versus detailed physical protection, not equivalent full geometry. Article trim intentionally absent for catalogue defaults, not stale omitted current decoration.", "765 garment path generates exactly one specification/shell from current catalogue selection and body; targets same shell, actual socket calculation uses current attachment tangent/location/canonical anatomical UV domain and returns both captured UV provenance and computed transform. These are input anchor versus output fitted coordinate products. It rejects unsupported domain instead of retaining incompatible cached transform. No current separate mutable socket success flag.", "765 actual generation lists generated files and asset rows only after successful writes; removes obsolete GLBs then writes manifest from same collected rows. Filtered export requires empty staging so an incomplete selected set cannot silently overwrite complete active manifest. The function has no atomic directory-publication promise: failure can leave partial staging artifacts, and no external concurrent reader/committed bad scene demonstrated in this lens.", "Exact duplicate-catalog qualification:764 intentionally retains duplicate identities;765291-315 can overwrite one file path for duplicate item/placement keys and pushes multiple manifest rows. Actual922from_json resolves each through canonical catalogue and REJECTS duplicate selection keys66-69. Hence there is a source-level public/API producer-to-receiver acceptance gap if duplicate catalogue rows are supplied, but not a proven pair of live resolvers using different truths. No installed duplicate catalogue/run claim or new07unique finding. This is preserved for admission/authoring reconciliation rather than silently clearing duplicate policy.", "922 wire manifest fields such as coverage/material/triangles/hash/release/version are broader authored transport metadata. EquipmentAssets currently retains ONLY checked canonical selection+file, deliberately discarding other record fields; no assertion those ignored fields independently control live gameplay. Private entries sort by canonical item/placement and exact file_for/default_file_for observe same order. Unknown item/placement and duplicate keys return error. default lexical placement is explicit policy, not another arbitrary first mutable source order."], "findings": [], "explicit_limits": ["Actual duplicate public producer path is rejected downstream; no two-live-authority defect inferred.", "Other deep export/GLB helpers remain own07 pending; current receiver comparison does not grant their body coverage."], "status": "Exact current07 source inventory with producer/receiver acceptance qualification, no new redundant-authority finding or other-lens credit"}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-265", "at": "2026-10-23T06:34:08.719825+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 767, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export.rs", "sha256": "ee364aaa0d304eb120d6f91216c6da3e186f5e20809e28ffa74f5864e568d72d", "actual_EOF": 1841, "material_ranges": [[1, 1841]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/767"}, {"scope065_index": 768, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/assembly.rs", "sha256": "18536af7cd15eb7df601912a927e135d22188621101eeeeef3df177185e4df5e", "actual_EOF": 312, "material_ranges": [[1, 312]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/768"}, {"scope065_index": 769, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/compact.rs", "sha256": "4aa7045f30b54218cf1897ee3f74e1d8831a35debb7905ad3365a796e20f7ca9", "actual_EOF": 104, "material_ranges": [[1, 104]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/769"}, {"scope065_index": 770, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/glb.rs", "sha256": "99b359ccf03e94e704e08e8f66f7b23c4dcf00a358ac7b1fabd98993530d26f8", "actual_EOF": 38, "material_ranges": [[1, 38]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/770"}, {"scope065_index": 771, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/morphs.rs", "sha256": "011541992d2e75b8667bab9997cf8a277922440568411095d1a1f4a20ea22ee7", "actual_EOF": 163, "material_ranges": [[1, 163]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/771"}, {"scope065_index": 772, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/rigged.rs", "sha256": "2f337baa2edb2356e1f086aacf549696c63bfac639d03c5f0a9b564d675bb397", "actual_EOF": 60, "material_ranges": [[1, 60]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/772"}, {"scope065_index": 773, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/shell.rs", "sha256": "6d0c444527f9a25d6aaf8e23e15ab8d973c489f6edb3a75429444c15c4132038", "actual_EOF": 80, "material_ranges": [[1, 80]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/773"}, {"scope065_index": 774, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/skeleton.rs", "sha256": "ac761936db58c742f2c58ab7381b8e26a8b6f819bfb91c0b29c54170fe96abff", "actual_EOF": 69, "material_ranges": [[1, 69]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/774"}, {"scope065_index": 775, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/skinning.rs", "sha256": "7ddf91c41655775cc2ac55844fa884d4f06dd8ba6951ee0d45b4550bbde5b199", "actual_EOF": 63, "material_ranges": [[1, 63]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/775"}, {"scope065_index": 776, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/sockets.rs", "sha256": "d51e531f136697d43d673cc1e6d16764b2c6fd35661d83d9a46b45a4eb5facdf", "actual_EOF": 57, "material_ranges": [[1, 57]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/776"}, {"scope065_index": 777, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/textures.rs", "sha256": "94523800edefb10ca1a28ebdf93b14b034f2b22b0900e406857bbfc8a5dbf99b", "actual_EOF": 170, "material_ranges": [[1, 170]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/777"}, {"scope065_index": 778, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/textures/tests.rs", "sha256": "3443c2f0ebaff8646fa3ac613ba770ea48024c53e850ce0dc8fbad014bc48072", "actual_EOF": 191, "material_ranges": [[1, 191]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/778"}, {"scope065_index": 779, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/export/validation.rs", "sha256": "61a7e389db804f2c17d7e619c27bb5bfc88f873f11e00d05097c85b6121518fb", "actual_EOF": 164, "material_ranges": [[1, 164]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/779"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full export1841 completed in five bounded reads, and all twelve sibling bodies 768-779 read fully with fingerprints verified. Original tests read as source only; no exports, filesystem test actions or checks executed.", "contracts": ["767 stores no independently mutable exported geometry cache: one borrowed RiggedMesh and shells feed buffer positions, skin, bounds, hierarchy and metadata in a single call. Input authored surface UV and resulting fitted pelvis-local socket are provenance versus a geometry-dependent output, not equivalent competing facts. Runtime socket resolution checks canonical UV domain and current fitted face membership; bootstrap ray utility is explicitly authoring-only, not a second normal runtime resolver. Original full tests demonstrate intended per-LOD UV anchoring but were not executed.", "768 assembly pairs primitives with body-if-exported plus each independent shell in the exact construction order used by 767 and 771 channels. Export metadata names and native mesh nodes are emitted from those same borrowed shell records. Hinge/plate edge extras retain physical reference-body facts separate from UV seams. Attachments metadata and hierarchy parent entries originate from the same actual selected names/parents/transforms at 767741-769; no later independent mutation is exposed before serialization. Native JSON remains an output projection, not a mutable gameplay authority shown here.", "769 CompactShell owns one sorted used-vertex set and remaps positions, normals, faces, selected joints, weights, texcoords, plate edges and morph deltas together. It retains original source immutably for material/hinge/name fields. Body-topology skin fallback is explicit only when both independent shell skin channels are absent; 779 enforces matched counts and joint bound. This is derived topology plus source appearance, not two independent current geometry caches. Surface UVs versus explicit texcoords have explicit precedence in 77353; source.surface UV slice is retained unchanged by compact.rigged, so compaction consistency for surface-only UV input is a separate admission/projection qualification, not proven competing authoritative resolver behavior. No installed malformed export claim.", "770 binary header total and JSON/BIN chunk lengths derive immediately from padded actual byte vectors; format constants are native ABI. No independent stored editable total-length authority. Large-length representability is a separate operation/admission issue; no new07 defect inferred. Filesystem write is final after document assembly, without an atomic publication promise.", "771 derives body/shell morph channel order from the same export_body flag and shell order, validates exact identical ordered names plus unique nonempty names/finite matching deltas, then emits names, zero initial weights and each primitive channel together. Names denote shared semantic dimensions while per-shell delta arrays intentionally differ with geometry; do not collapse these independent effects. 768 copies the already generated common extras/weights for each exported mesh.", "772 RiggedMesh explicitly distinguishes source body faces needed for socket location from export_body rendered membership. Independent shell topology and optional independent skin differ deliberately from shared body-topology clothing; material sRGB differs from linear native factors. global_transforms derives current ordered typed states rather than a separately mutable cached transform table.", "774 builds children and local node transforms from current parent/global tables, and append_attachment extends names/parents/globals together. Proportion bases are construction metadata rather than current global translation; they are checked for cardinality/finiteness and attached only to original covered joints. Inverse bind generation in 767 follows all actual attachment additions. No separately stale inverse-bind cache.", "775 obtains one strongest-four result stream and emits joint indices plus normalized weights from that same stream; eight authored influences versus native four are a deliberate codec projection. Original translation test preserves intended lost-mass policy; no run or new lower strongest_four implementation claim from the call alone.", "776 socket native nodes and document-level socket extras derive the same input records and naming prefix. Children append to the actual canonical pelvis ordinal, preventing a parallel root-name lookup. Captured UV provenance versus computed transform remain different stages; validation rejects duplicate attachment IDs but does not prove every externally fabricated public RiggedSocket transform matches its UV. That raw input correlation limit is preserved, not a demonstrated normal producer drift.", "777 TextureImages is local to one export. Content-addressed sibling filenames derive from actual PNG bytes, and finish verifies an existing filename has exactly the proposed bytes before reuse; standalone embeds exact current bytes. Material texture indices come from the same append sequence. shell_cache uses borrowed ShellTextures addresses only while original shells are immutably borrowed during this call, so no mutating/recycled source lifetime is established. Surface textures and metal procedural maps are explicit separate material channels; apply_shell_textures intentionally replaces normal/metal-roughness and sets factor1 to avoid double roughness. Current ordered precedence is not accidental two live authority demonstrated.", "778 original fixtures compare exact URI bytes, material channels and corruption rejection; they are source-only acceptance evidence, not audit results. 779 validates the current borrow before any native assembly, sharing existing morph validator rather than duplicating its channel policy. Public raw export records remain broader than fully proven relationships; no new checks or tests are authored."], "findings": [], "remaining_qualifications": ["No actual glTF consumer behavior beyond these emitted native records is inferred. Surface-only compacted UV relationship is preserved as an explicit projection/admission limit, not invented07 coverage or a normal rendered failure."], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-266", "at": "2026-10-23T06:37:45.301973+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 780, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment.rs", "sha256": "d6b09524be811c5e4202be50af529c941a917ff8f31ea61e2a73e4da17dc103e", "actual_EOF": 702, "material_ranges": [[1, 702]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/780"}, {"scope065_index": 781, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/conform.rs", "sha256": "4c3ee7c251ed1a4d18681e0b05c0fcf35b3b61e7d6dd0decfda0708577469162", "actual_EOF": 324, "material_ranges": [[1, 324]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/781"}, {"scope065_index": 782, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/drape.rs", "sha256": "c26b0508ccce30c3c2ca164e46327764ca4b133b418b5ea49e008b0a45613421", "actual_EOF": 334, "material_ranges": [[1, 334]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/782"}, {"scope065_index": 783, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/dressing.rs", "sha256": "a5b190694f00f1dbc5e1895f5b40f65b6c1f7242da45ea844b59a6b6d6932523", "actual_EOF": 145, "material_ranges": [[1, 145]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/783"}, {"scope065_index": 784, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/fitted.rs", "sha256": "90a73376395b601a39a8d4a51fe9004d62176ce2ac236c578bee720bab2007a6", "actual_EOF": 588, "material_ranges": [[1, 588]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/784"}, {"scope065_index": 785, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/lining.rs", "sha256": "693fb7bf790d8bfebd26304241c8dfd0e2b338bc37225a4d0795b0fe754e8b70", "actual_EOF": 227, "material_ranges": [[1, 227]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/785"}, {"scope065_index": 786, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/outfit.rs", "sha256": "571784773d4506fa741fed5d4dab85c61bbf9dee836fab1833987b233a4ecdb9", "actual_EOF": 82, "material_ranges": [[1, 82]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/786"}, {"scope065_index": 787, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/placement.rs", "sha256": "7e744958c7df65097784318b313e51c658edae89fde9e0f80ba70ddce4fcaa81", "actual_EOF": 76, "material_ranges": [[1, 76]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/787"}, {"scope065_index": 788, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/settled.rs", "sha256": "3dbafb11ea673b81b72c6d8599bf9c1ac4c55b3e456982e39d16d38faef2e42d", "actual_EOF": 308, "material_ranges": [[1, 308]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/788"}, {"scope065_index": 789, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/settled/packed.rs", "sha256": "ca95a83317547915bbd839018cd6b1c766ff327327877fc02c6978d1bcaee0f7", "actual_EOF": 78, "material_ranges": [[1, 78]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/789"}, {"scope065_index": 790, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/settled/tests.rs", "sha256": "18961b0116bbc93358501df011ca5a6a31d912a61f357c201ed56f9ff61f3476", "actual_EOF": 244, "material_ranges": [[1, 244]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/790"}, {"scope065_index": 791, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/shading.rs", "sha256": "8d9236c7e60922d5e12987557077f6554b1061d171f0b4d783576711c71f56b3", "actual_EOF": 70, "material_ranges": [[1, 70]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/791"}, {"scope065_index": 792, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/stages.rs", "sha256": "ccbbca63f8954cde1d15934b057edc40dfe382d36c273fed0acd0316f9a2fe2a", "actual_EOF": 352, "material_ranges": [[1, 352]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/792"}, {"scope065_index": 793, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/garment/validation.rs", "sha256": "26ab01120c442d3d0f7fece4c338f28680fafcd633314036aeb853dc263e637e", "actual_EOF": 179, "material_ranges": [[1, 179]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/793"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full780702,781324,782334,783145,784588,785227,78776,788308,78978,790244,79170,792352,793179. Truncated784 conformal/rigid solver output297-368 explicitly recovered before credit. Existing full786 source proof CON252 personally compared to current stage calls, with fresh actual37-73 receiver reread; no hash/verdict carry. Fresh762247-280 actual preview receiver supports name finding within prior full source proof. All original tests source only.", "contracts": ["780 measured_body converts current mesh and joint landmarks metres to centimetres for pattern measurement; supplied Body measurements are a derived local product, not independently editable long-lived authoring authority. SewnSurface groups, compact faces and render-face ordinal map derive together from exact seam graph. Separate material seam copies intentionally share simulation positions/normals but retain render UV vertices. Fresh normals and orientation routines recompute from current surfaces; geometric area normals differ from semantic skin and original stitch adjacency.", "780 transfer_skin reads actual canonical named joint ordinals, current source body triangles and eight influences, combines barycentric weighted influences, deterministically keeps strongest eight and renormalizes. Skirted transfer explicitly blends hip-side samples for continuous central cloth motion; it is not a competing lookup for the same physical rigid attachment. Public raw DrapedGarment positions/normals/skin fields are not a sealed validated token; actual finish recomputes dependent normals and skin after geometric edits.", "781 SewnCloth owns sewn groups, edges and neighbour adjacency derived together from the same immutable supplied mesh. Rest edge limits intentionally derive from historical settled geometry, while current positions vary during stretch/clearance: independent temporal reference versus current state. Draw-in retains original dressed membership and edge limits for this bounded solve by design; clearance is repeatedly recomputed on current points and immutable collision surface. The local solver caches are not independently mutated public semantic state.", "782 stage pipeline records completed sewn and settled states BEFORE final fairness/body-fit/keep-out/tuck-under. Reuse therefore intentionally repeats finish on current body_fit and under_plate inputs. Current finish recomputes normals and skin after all geometry modifications, then reports contact warnings without rejecting usable cloth. Stage labels report simulation progress or saved-drape wearing, not independent proof that all clearance warnings disappeared. Preview partial stages and final result have explicit different purposes.", "782 SeamClosure captures placed seam gaps and original bending weights, temporarily disables across-seam bends while open, then closes rest lengths and restores original weights together. Colour-order reorder is applied to both streams using the actual solver collection. Historical open gaps and rest material hinge weights are independent reference constraints, not stale copies of current positions. STEP_SECONDS is one local integration step; preview interval and solver substeps intentionally different counters.", "783 Dressing partitions canonical RigJointName structured parts into garment-specific body areas, picks strongest skin influence and tests current nearest surface corner. This clothing inclusion policy deliberately differs from rigid fit support-joint eligibility and equipment occupancy: wrist is hand here and excluded from drawn cloth, though useful in other frame construction. No forced universal shared body-part enum from coincident labels. BodyPart classification local and recomputed per current DrapeInput.", "784 fitted coif starts from current fitted_coif_carrier and PartFrame, produces cut mesh and material unwrap together; FrontCut preserves original indices, records each duplicated seam origin, remaps left faces and derives seams in one operation. Stretch edges/rest lengths, bending weights and masses derive from that same returned topology. Conformal initial map and rigid iterations deliberately use geometric rest gradients versus evolving flat coordinates; historical triangle metric is not a competing current UV authority. Test-only synthetic fit_words mirror is fixture source, not a second production resolver.", "785 PlateLining privately captures immutable combined inner faces and rim-use classification from actual GeneratedArmor pieces. UnderPlate standoff includes half own thickness and overlying garments, distinct from external body clearance and plate geometry thickness. The private surface/rim cache cannot be independently edited through its API. Current StudioCache model-dependency F050 remains separate: local PlateLining ownership is coherent once constructed from the intended generation.", "786 existing actual source is explicitly reconciled: each garment receives exactly finished prior garments as obstacles, no later independent obstacle classifier; saved.wear and simulated drape both return the current result with partial completed checkpoints. First failure returns successful prefix; it does not skip a middle garment and shift following identity. Warning prefixes consume result garment.name, providing F056 actual receiver.", "787 collision_surface derives one local BVH from current body plus every prior finished garment, offsetting indices with the actual vertex append length. Pattern placement uses current floor and hip centre; fitted coif is already in wearer space and deliberately bypasses pattern translation. Initial body collider and expanded body-plus-inner-garment collider have distinct contact roles. No public mutable cached BVH survives an input edit in this function.", "788 saved selection/drape settings are capture provenance; saved rest positions and local surface bindings support transfer to a new body shape, deliberately not replaying prior current world positions. Current skin/normals/contact warnings are recomputed after transfer and clearance. However same-topology identity is reduced to counts and actual saved triangle ordinals are consumed on current faces; F055 records the exact binding weakness. No normal installed topology change assumed.", "789 packed representation is lossless native words/bit serialization from actual arrays, fixed record width with decoded length divisibility. WORDS constants are per codec record and not a cached semantic collection length; SurfaceBinding pack/unpack layout is colocated. Decoder validation issues belong admission lens and do not by themselves establish redundant authority. 790 original source fixtures demonstrate same-topology shape/translation transfer, changed-count rejection, roundtrip and seam stretch policy; no fixture run or new tests.", "791 normals_for derives seam correspondence from reference positions and applies it to deformed positions intentionally to keep shared lighting across UV seam copies. from_pattern initializes current name/form/fabric from selection only at fresh construction; reuse path does not refresh name, F056. Historical seam copies versus deformed new coordinates are not duplicate current fields requiring one value.", "792 checkpoint input privately owns exact historical producer snapshot. same_setup compares body positions/faces/names/joints/skin, construction/fabric/resolution, and obstacle geometry; sewing edit restarts placement, settling edit reuses sewn, body-fit or appearance edit reuses settled and repeats finish. Preview interval is presentation scheduling, not physical dependency. UnderPlate is deliberately absent because only final tuck consumes it and always reruns; saved settled override is handled at outer786 before checkpoint selection. Omitted current label remains F056, not a blanket all-cache dependency finding.", "793 contact intersections and strict body clearance are distinct intentional predicates: coplanar/endpoint contact excluded for intersections, wrong side can fail clearance without intersecting triangles. Contact issues are warnings; validate_body_clearance is a separate explicit acceptance gate. Both use current geometry rather than retained success flag. Repeated body-clearance formula at79327-28 and782277-278 currently agrees; one canonical fabrication/clearance policy can serve both construction and validation, without treating independent residual observations as the same stored state."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F055", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F056"], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-267", "at": "2026-10-23T06:41:46.678403+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 795, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair.rs", "sha256": "a9d4f30809a845df7b5e43bac564eb66824d90bb6cfed878e96c6afae8ff332c", "actual_EOF": 177, "material_ranges": [[1, 177]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/795"}, {"scope065_index": 796, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/cap.rs", "sha256": "f15aaadb4a376988994c92be34ee22767367490569bb5a1fec2dd21d0db5fdf8", "actual_EOF": 256, "material_ranges": [[1, 256]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/796"}, {"scope065_index": 797, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/geometry.rs", "sha256": "58e56192a203d08a0cff3e0d1b4a037df09a24a86b969555bb1f2b6faf8a5fa0", "actual_EOF": 172, "material_ranges": [[1, 172]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/797"}, {"scope065_index": 798, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/bake/mod.rs", "sha256": "2d8ba1f7658b0a709143467f73dc6b3f0a0eab31ad0a36a6a7436028b0ba4d7f", "actual_EOF": 448, "material_ranges": [[1, 448]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/798"}, {"scope065_index": 799, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/bake/wgsl.rs", "sha256": "7965432924278f1a7cbcf9a47a295a9c2b9fe4103783e8d641f54dbbd9bc70ec", "actual_EOF": 400, "material_ranges": [[1, 400]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/799"}, {"scope065_index": 800, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/field.rs", "sha256": "1f537b363a614847b1ddf760ac719c5ed099171646ce606649e8b7ca79390264", "actual_EOF": 545, "material_ranges": [[1, 545]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/800"}, {"scope065_index": 801, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/place/mod.rs", "sha256": "4197c4d14aeac409495f9d91e21e2e69439a4a62bd9991804a5b8fe59ebaad8d", "actual_EOF": 365, "material_ranges": [[1, 365]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/801"}, {"scope065_index": 802, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/place/wgsl.rs", "sha256": "21850bcf4f22d8cd055230bb6ac0c8b93f722a90a278d51568acb513894f88c3", "actual_EOF": 274, "material_ranges": [[1, 274]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/802"}, {"scope065_index": 803, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/strips.rs", "sha256": "018591fdd7fdc9288f16a0ed5ed2f2ef6e3649448afa564b58358a3987144bba", "actual_EOF": 511, "material_ranges": [[1, 511]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/803"}, {"scope065_index": 804, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/groom.rs", "sha256": "6be15ac30dc63fd83b87ed48442b9fa9d403bb875737c7bafe13bdc19ac6c4c9", "actual_EOF": 233, "material_ranges": [[1, 233]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/804"}, {"scope065_index": 805, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/placement.rs", "sha256": "95f08e95fd0815ac957cb0578ef7291036b5d4a9b047e38da1a9f16bdebd4a7f", "actual_EOF": 266, "material_ranges": [[1, 266]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/805"}, {"scope065_index": 806, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/shape.rs", "sha256": "d2da1edcace60e78eab855e992651bda223fcbab7bd832c0f00304ecdcbe7294", "actual_EOF": 229, "material_ranges": [[1, 229]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/806"}, {"scope065_index": 807, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair_preview.rs", "sha256": "800207ff944cfc7487b00bfbaa888dbe254ec85340094e9104c392b54b14ea78", "actual_EOF": 343, "material_ranges": [[1, 343]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/807"}, {"scope065_index": 808, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair_preview/assets.rs", "sha256": "1945aa84edf49348310989955b6f814cc19ae8cceaf87d85400f4bce8cf9a296", "actual_EOF": 225, "material_ranges": [[1, 225]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/808"}], "additional_sources": [{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-REG045", "at": "2026-10-23T06:39:31.832954+00:00", "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/scalp_map.rs", "snapshot": "pr-working", "snapshot_path": "target/774-snapshots/pr-working/crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/scalp_map.rs", "sha256": "717bbedb859bc7b5df413aeea35d20cccbdf1e08dc53f2f8d692b72dc2cc662e", "actual_EOF": 147, "material_ranges": [[1, 147]], "role": "Direct shared mapping definition for actual796 cap UV and798/799 GPU scalp bake coordinate recipient; compare one current texture-coordinate authority across host and native numerical adapter.", "authority": "continuation/root/parallel-initial-audits-081.json", "chronology": "Metadata fingerprint/EOF and declaration-only symbol navigation before registration; no body analysis credited before this append. Fresh bounded body read follows.", "exclusions": "No other file or foreign package; direct local production definition only."}, {"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-REG046", "at": "2026-10-23T06:39:31.833468+00:00", "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/mod.rs", "snapshot": "pr-working", "snapshot_path": "target/774-snapshots/pr-working/crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/hair/gpu/mod.rs", "sha256": "f8844fc7362364c5217079615e4459865865020ba4a36f5b25a8997cdd9c8f92", "actual_EOF": 138, "material_ranges": [[1, 138]], "role": "Direct actual KernelSource compile and per-HairGpu context/kernel owner used by798-804 construction and807 renderer device; compare cache/device identity and explicit native parameter producer, no foreign graph.", "authority": "continuation/root/parallel-initial-audits-081.json", "chronology": "Metadata fingerprint/EOF and declaration-only symbol navigation before registration; no body analysis credited before this append. Fresh bounded body read follows.", "exclusions": "No other file or foreign package; direct local production definition only."}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full795-808 and prospectively registered REG045147/REG046138. Truncated800455-545 and8011-200 explicitly recovered before credit. Body metadata/fingerprints verified. No kernels, renderers, new assertions or existing tests executed.", "contracts": ["795 HairDesign separates groom growth from pigment; groom() intentionally excludes pigment because geometry and baked greyscale scalp/atlas do not depend on current colour. HairPigment color derives canonical HairMaterial pigment equation at actual adapter; HairMaterial default supplies defaults rather than an independent repeated natural-colour table. Clamped constructor versus checked decoder NaN admission remains another lens, not duplicate authority from names alone.", "796 ScalpCap computes current mapped positions, UVs, tangents and opacity in one factory. Smooth scalp normals intentionally describe the original smooth scalp carried onto the wearer rather than coarse clipped body facets; these are different shading versus collision facts, explicitly documented54-55. Edge distance fade and analytic hairline fade combine by min, representing distinct independent boundaries. Current fit computes normals/tangents only once after clearance and returns a raw public product; no actual later cap mutation route demonstrated.", "797 native strand/cards versus host HairGeometry are codec/readback representations, with private GpuGeometry shape metadata determining exact returned faces and attributes. Ribbon budget draws a subset and widens it reciprocally to retain approximate coverage intentionally; requested share versus actual affordable count are different quantities. atlas mip dimensions derive from actual current base dimensions. carried() intentionally maps from old to new placement while retaining UV, baked source self-shadow and random identity; it is not a promise to rerun physical shoulder collision or lighting for each morph.", "798/799 scalp bake privately builds two different output textures: shade/coverage versus strand direction/shade. Both derive from the same packed topmost stream and shared PACKING source text, with deliberately duplicated shade channel as native texture payload. Actual parameters originate once on host; no independent editable colour policy in shader. Four blur passes alternate two scratch buffers and end at bare0 consumed by finish. One levels() function owns allocations, upload strides/offsets, mip dispatch and host readback; ROW_TEXELS64 is explicit 256-byte/four-byte native alignment, not another image width authority.", "799 packed topmost word sorts height first, with direction/shade tie bits, and shared decode uses same constants from the compiled PACKING text. It is an intentional ordering/quantized approximation, not full strand identity or a second gameplay fact. Longest measured strand atomic reduction clears output before dispatch; 804 stores captured reference longest for tessellation. No numerical bound/float correctness clearance follows from this07 comparison.", "800 BodyField privately owns one native buffer/header derived from current body and transformed hair bounds. Grid owns header and near mesh together; host Grid.params uses header fields for each actual dispatch. Seed/flood/finish are intermediate current approximation stages, not independent authoritative colliders that can be edited apart. Filtered near-triangle ordinal refers to exact uploaded face stream, and finish writes signed distance after current nearest field. Smooth CPU collider and sampled grid explicitly have different precision/performance roles; no exact duplicated live collision answers promised.", "801/802 current source distinguishes groomed and carried guides, equilibrium against actual body, equilibrium without body, and corresponding bust reference. Difference subtracts already-authored bust influence before adding character effect; these are necessary counterfactual observations, not redundant copies of current pose. Carried positions/attributes/roots emitted together. Draped output preserves carried roots and root point; later shrinkwrap operates on same constructed groom. Private Frame parameters derive origin/axes from actual HeadPlacement; normal inverse transpose deliberately differs from point/tangent affine transform.", "803 one private GpuGeometry factory stores actual rows/strips with all native arrays allocated from same derived count; readback and faces derive that metadata, and public accessors expose buffers without independent shape setters. Ribbon/card source layouts differ deliberately. Lift scratch holds current unspread requirements while final positions add maximum neighbouring requirement, an intentional constraint propagation stage. Original normals remain source smooth strip normals for shading rather than a claim to recompute exact post-lift geometric normals. No ordinary runtime shape/count drift established.", "804 normal grow computes look/head/scalp/map/bake/bounds/longest and retains them together; place creates actual body field, carried/draped geometry, LODs and fitted cap in one operation. Body field extent FIELD_MARGIN0.08 differs from root-only MAX_ROOT_SHIFT0.03 because different collections can move; equal-purpose collapse would be wrong. BODY_REACH0.1 and field REACH0.1 currently agree as intentional near-body query cutoff but have separate CPU/grid implementations. Public groom label, however, can be independently edited without regenerating private products; F057 records the actual cache recipient.", "805 HeadPlacement axes plus scalar scales derive in the same constructor and remain private, so their redundancy has coordinated ownership. head_joint is a separate skin binding ordinal, not derived solely from affine geometry; it is publicly mutable as raw API context but no normal incorrect rebind shown. HeadExtent derives from current skin share rather than stale head bounding box. Canonical name lookup and private affine inverse/normal transforms share the same axes; no separate mutable mirror route.", "806 HairShape is variation input rather than duplicate complete Look. apply constructs canonical preset Look once, replaces optional cut/arrangement/growth and applies each actual relative knob; default identity variation is intentional, not an independently maintained second preset. Recomputed drape flag calls actual resulting hairdo.drapes rather than mirroring preset switch. Typed Ratio/Metres ports preserve different unit meanings and no new owner semantics are claimed from this lens.", "807 actual cache uses groom equality and Arc identity of generated body, worker stores exact request/body and returns self-contained products. A new current request drops earlier handle; stale finished style may be collected but placed(groom,body) checks current wanted identity before drawing. Existing old shown HairMesh is removed on current design/form mismatch. Full body regeneration despawns character meshes by caller contract already observed in252; F050 insufficient model generation key remains upstream and separate. Cached groom identity is publicly mutable at library layer, F057, whereas no normal preview code mutates those fields.", "808 native placeholder mesh positions count vertices only; actual positions live in GPU buffers used by material shader. This is deliberately not a competing zero geometry truth. Skin binds entirely to current retained head ordinal, and source cap uses actual physical coordinates. Hair pigment changes rebuild material, leaving geometry reused intentionally. Card atlas greyscale and pigment multiplication differ from separate scalp directional texture; actual baked image roles and channels remain explicit.", "REG045 fresh full147 establishes ScalpMap fitted once to immutable bust scalp, with canonical centre/axes/rim shared as actual shader parameters. Host uv108-116 and799map_texel136-155 implement the same equal-area/concentric map with normalized UV versus texel-coordinate output; current branch boundaries/quarter-turn wrapping compared. The numeric host/native implementations are necessary separate execution ports, with no currently distinct authored policy or two installed resolver disagreement established. An algorithm change must preserve coordinated mapping; no finding from duplication of standard mathematical formula alone.", "REG046 fresh full138 establishes HairGpu private context/kernel/groomer ownership, source cache scoped to that context and Mutex serialization of shared scratch. params macro creates native named pass values in one place, not independent shader semantic ownership proof. Public methods accepting HairGpu alongside pre-existing buffers retain an explicit caller device-affinity precondition; no wrong-device actual caller demonstrated, no foreign backend graph expanded."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F057"], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-268", "at": "2026-10-23T06:43:33.084711+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope065_index": 809, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory.rs", "sha256": "0f820bca06e27b164da010e95dc7d3500a79a6feb0b7be9411ed8a41e88feb18", "actual_EOF": 442, "material_ranges": [[1, 442]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/809"}, {"scope065_index": 810, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory/loadout.rs", "sha256": "8b3ada636d68eaae16cf4ca2bab097cd918be93a52452d34dc3e2648add51691", "actual_EOF": 110, "material_ranges": [[1, 110]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/810"}, {"scope065_index": 811, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory/occupancy.rs", "sha256": "dbd62cb0c402bcb0903b4bcebdc159c2d2f35f266e4dff77c359796db40231b8", "actual_EOF": 287, "material_ranges": [[1, 287]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/811"}, {"scope065_index": 812, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory/tests.rs", "sha256": "3c8c66c5b49199d343845589bf635cd68c05dbd740656a1e33bdbc7c0534f4cd", "actual_EOF": 239, "material_ranges": [[1, 239]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/812"}, {"scope065_index": 813, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory_acquire.rs", "sha256": "38c1ff570b3617b06af25f869d5ccd0f82d4827a6c4d0f9c4298e14c04ec145f", "actual_EOF": 138, "material_ranges": [[1, 138]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-065.json#/files/813"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full809442/810110/811287/812239/813138, fingerprints verified. Personally consumed prior current07 CON053 actual Core EquipmentGraph predicates and compared actual current caller placement/support roles; no verdict-only lower carry. All original tests source only.", "contracts": ["809 Inventory retains one vector of articles with worn membership. worn() derives current filtered set and fit() rebuilds candidates/graph each call, so it does not maintain an independently editable active-item index. Article catalog spelling resolves current borrowed catalog and design_for verifies selection identity before combining per-instance override with actual default family. Instance design/decoration/construction are intentional authored variations, not stale mirrored complete catalogue defaults.", "809 wear stages a clone, changes requested membership, repeatedly removes conflicting existing article and dependents, and restores original on unsuccessful fit. take_off rebuilds actual graph until unsupported articles are removed, without retaining old dependency cache. Returned taken_off is operation history, not another current worn-membership authority. get_mut public ID/worn/article exposure remains admission/API exposure; actual reads recompute instead of trusting persistent validated flag. ID max-plus-one overflow is an operations issue, not two authorities shown by this lens.", "810 loadout validates current fit then resolves worn articles into immutable borrowed per-generator selections. Clothing/fitted/draped collections represent different production routes, not competing complete copies of all worn state. Stable sorting draped by canonical channel order preserves inventory order within same layer. Public vectors can be manually fabricated/mutated despite validated-fit documentation, the prior admission qualification; no persistent cached loadout normal mutation shown. Article variants own complete saved garments intentionally, not shared live wardrobe aliases.", "811 Occupancy is local derived snapshot of current catalog placement or actual garment construction plus selected layer. Declared pattern coverage and geometric draped vertices need not match one exact collision silhouette: occupancy is game equipment cells, not continuous visible coverage; do not make all garment triangles another gameplay authority. Coif Head/Neck and sewn upper/sleeves/lower source classification are current owning policy, not independent retained flag on article.", "811 WornGraph builds structural graph and supports map from same accepted edges after successful canonical graph.equip. support chooses actual compatible point/tag/location and current capacity; children_on derives counts from actual graph edges, including deferred attachment passes. CON053 actual lower structural graph does not itself enforce source point capacity; current caller supplies that role explicitly. Diagnostic conflict reconstruction uses canonical conflicts_with predicate instead of duplicate overlap formula. supports is publicly mutable and dependents reads it, but private graph has no post-build query accessor in this type; no demonstrated second publicly observable post-mutation source truth from that alone. Preserve raw accepted-product encapsulation qualification without inventing a normal transition failure.", "812 original tests exercise replacement, articulated fit zones, actual attachment dependency/side/capacity, sorting and raw article edit revalidation. Source only; fixture expectations do not remove any duplicated policy by themselves and were not run.", "813 acquisition UI derives catalog grouping from actual first placement outermost_channel as a presentation approximation, not current worn graph. Multiple placement buttons request independent articles; both requests are processed sequentially and current wear may displace prior items by explicit rule. Current wardrobe acquisition clones saved artifact and selection as independent owned article, deliberately allowing future wardrobe edits without retroactive inventory changes. Search/selection UI state does not duplicate current equipment authority. Native display labels are presentation port; item weight uses authored catalog weight, not measured generated cloth mass."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-269", "at": "2026-10-23T06:46:59.311266+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 814, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/inventory_article_editor.rs", "sha256": "bfaf8082b9b0e3aba214dbe23016ae3d83f78b3a66f777ea6e2601ddc5475cf9", "actual_EOF": 199, "material_ranges": [[1, 199]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/814"}, {"scope066_index": 815, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/item_design.rs", "sha256": "a33bdf3bde70ed5a647c3968c9e9c04dd60402bca585d47a4d2555ce9e3802aa", "actual_EOF": 232, "material_ranges": [[1, 232]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/815"}, {"scope066_index": 816, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/lib.rs", "sha256": "dc0c4f7b59ecd62d3a8a4a6b00c5bfecfc15470df833fe4294e486d1ffa5393c", "actual_EOF": 238, "material_ranges": [[1, 238]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/816"}, {"scope066_index": 817, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/library_name.rs", "sha256": "ecd978e94b850604d4345df1494e9536819e19d7a6d3b8921fde3d55bf54eb27", "actual_EOF": 52, "material_ranges": [[1, 52]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/817"}, {"scope066_index": 818, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/lod.rs", "sha256": "73ad82b91f4b15146231c922544a72466849407fc7fca6ebe2268d78f45d7fa3", "actual_EOF": 39, "material_ranges": [[1, 39]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/818"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full814199/815232/816238/81752/81839 verified source fingerprints. Fresh bounded existing8321-67,83155-107 actual invalidation recipients; MHR canonical model16-44 and existing current prior492 coefficient route reanalyzed for exact cardinality dependency. Bounded MHRlib2750 exports31-43 read only, no1-30 credit. Existing tests source only.", "contracts": ["814 separates article-owned design from live catalogue default explicitly. Use catalog shape removes override and triggers rebuild; editing design stores per-instance clone and triggers rebuild. Changing shared default intentionally leaves current article override unchanged. However successful Make catalog default mutates shared policy without dirty/revision notification for other default-following articles, exact actual F058. It is not remedied by correct fit keys if regenerate_mesh never executes.", "814 settled garment edit intentionally changes only current name/layer/appearance while retaining saved physical drape; shape/fabric edits excluded by UI. Worn versus carried controls whether dirty regeneration is needed. Name/material live presentation refresh versus physical fitting remains separate; F056 cache metadata is source API qualification rather than proof this exact UI rename always starts a drape.", "815 CatalogDesigns resolves default from dedicated item-family owner or authored recipe plus optional per-item/per-placement overrides. Explicit override precedence is deliberate authorship, not two active resolvers for the same current selected design. same_family gate ensures compatible construction, and set_default validates before replacing one selected source. Vambrace and breastplate are shared family defaults by declared role, so change can affect multiple articles while individual Some design remains owned history/variation. No independent invalidation signal emitted by setter; caller F058 supplies concrete missing update.", "816 CharacterRecipe format version intentionally retained and checked against canonical version; rejection of old versions follows clean API policy, not compatibility dual path. Defaults derive actual canonical identity count and inventory operations; inventory flags can be edited but loadout revalidates current article graph. IdentityGroup ranges label three semantic coefficient groups rather than duplicate physical features, so do not collapse them merely because their lengths sum to45. Expression cardinality87 is a manual second copy of actual MHR canonical NUM_FACE_EXPRESSION_BLEND_SHAPES18; F059 records exact schema-policy duplication.", "817 LibraryName wraps one private normalized String; Display and native String serialization derive it, no independent key/display spelling retained here. Normalization trims rather than preserving original authored space, matching canonical nonempty-name role. Independent library file key versus current garment label remains a separate collection contract, not automatically equivalent in this leaf.", "818 CharacterLod validation imports actual MHR MIN/MAX through reexport owner instead of independently checking a second numeric range; error/test text literal4-6 is diagnostic/fixture context, not another executable range. vertices table [2461,971,595] is a local published static asset-layout expectation; this body alone does not establish actual loaded asset cardinalities or a duplicated other authoritative vertex table. Preserve exact lower asset identity dependency, no invented source-proof or normal mismatch."], "findings": ["CAMERA-INITIAL07-F058", "CAMERA-INITIAL07-F059"], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-270", "at": "2026-10-23T06:47:58.630734+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 819, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/main.rs", "sha256": "41961ead92363687fdd3286fe6e6d55a11fb00fc67c53a64cf5dada05d4090b9", "actual_EOF": 667, "material_ranges": [[1, 667]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/819"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh actual full main667 including all inline original tests, two bounded complete reads. Includes referenced test module declarations only, not included child bodies or execution.", "contracts": ["BodyModel owns actual loaded Mhr, lod and correctives. load_body_model414-426 constructs them together from checked selected LOD/config; reload430-455 compares requested values, swaps only successful complete loaded result, and resets requested values on failure. Selected request versus accepted current configuration are distinct phases, not redundant authority defect. ExistingF050 remains exact downstream body-key omission, not failure of this coordinated model replacement.", "Studio recipe and UI selection/search/page/output paths are separate requested content and presentation state. dirty is explicit generation scheduling, not persistent certificate that all fields are admitted. GeneratedCharacter holds one derived physical body and private DeviceBody; normal immutable Arc sharing preserves upload ownership, while wider public RuntimeBody API F051 remains separate. ExistingF058 shared default mutator requires actual invalidation; correct update-system order cannot manufacture a missing dirty signal.", "App ordering explicitly reloads before generation, armor/wardrobe handling before generation, drape poll and hair refresh after generation, deform cloth after propagated skeleton. These orderings correlate intended live products but do not grant unseen child operation coverage. Current body and hair buffers remain tactical local preview, not durable strategic state. No scheduling runtime or deferred hook execution claimed.", "main CLI paths read one model/design/catalog/recipe, validate recipe and then choose distinct review/equipment/export/UI modes; generated geometry and metadata use that selected current model. write_armor_designs produces resolved per-item recipe defaults plus explicit placement overrides as authoring output, not another live active catalogue. The normal save recipe path validates immediately before JSON serialization; path text does not duplicate current game identity.", "placement_coverage381-395 computes a region-count-weighted authored surface summary. It intentionally differs from detailed physical exact hit coverage and does not claim disjoint region union. belt_mount_outward maps anatomical belt position to outward direction for current native coordinate frame, distinct from placement occupancy tags. Source-level zero denominator/float bounds are another audit lens, not evidence of two current authoritative values.", "Original integration fixture485 asks load_body_model LOD1 while current CharacterLod is4-6; this is a stale ignored fixture request, not normal accepted app behavior or a duplicate executable production LOD policy. Its tests/printing/file-writing bodies were read only, not run. Diagnostic test summaries and saved snapshot milestones represent historical solver stages; do not treat as current accepted geometry authorities."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-271", "at": "2026-10-23T06:49:01.516277+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 821, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/outfit.rs", "sha256": "4d3281fb80e63eeb57bf3caaec77e63eb33d75c62e6ec5d7053e2fd76ebd95f2", "actual_EOF": 104, "material_ranges": [[1, 104]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/821"}, {"scope066_index": 822, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/parametric_equipment.rs", "sha256": "fb8ed7e496fe124cf6ea6c4deb962b9602cf62f5b516d362b5e50ddca9829c49", "actual_EOF": 478, "material_ranges": [[1, 478]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/822"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full outfit104 and parametric_equipment478, fingerprints verified, including original ignored device integration fixtures as source only. Prior actual own equipment layer, clothing, device fit and current caches personally compared for these precise producer roles.", "contracts": ["821 loadout derives current worn selection from canonical Inventory.loadout rather than separate state flags. clothing_specifications maps exact actual placement names and borrowed catalogue geometry into current generation. drape_inputs traverses outer-to-inner for accumulated half-thickness standoff, then reverses to inner-to-outer simulation order. These opposite traversals are complementary algorithms over same canonical order, not inconsistent equipment ordering. UnderPlate clearance1mm is additional physical lining room, distinct from cloth own half-thickness and body exterior ease.", "821 lining selects actual is_rigid(piece) and current GeneratedArmor inner faces, not an independently reclassified generic metal boolean. Plate steel material controls construction/texture, whereas rigid EquipmentChannel controls whether cloth lies underneath; these are orthogonal facts and need not be collapsed. Exact actual822237-239 observes placement outermost_channel for rigid membership.", "822 fitted_design dispatches Underlayer/TrunkHose to specialised measured surface routines, other recipes to device fit; fitted_item dispatches dedicated Vambrace/Breastplate separately. Different producer families intentionally share GeneratedArmor output while preserving source-specific physical input, not competing type owners in this lens. Current placement borrowed source and generated global joint states feed the same assemble step; named morph list derives exact current sample order, and subsequent correct_armor_fit provides explicit skeletal residual adjustment, not stale geometry copy.", "822 fitted_catalog_item uses actual selected source material only to rescale plate-steel texture density; construction finishes are separate from physical fitting. SelectedArmor retains current FittedPiece plus derived Finish metadata, but new() computes name from exact piece and consumes a complete finish. Finish retains geometry/trim/lacing as one cache unit. Actual831 fit/finish keys distinguish those dependencies; F058 absent dirty notification is a higher caller issue, not missing key proven here.", "822 construct consumes currently selected construction for steel, deliberately Solid for other materials. Lacing generated geometry and cord description represent rendered product versus authoring material, joined in same returned product. trim applies current decoration after construction, deriving actual texcoords alongside trimmed geometry. Names derive once from current item/placement. Current Solid reference fit for lining versus final lamellar/scales visual geometry are intentional stage distinctions, not automatic authoritative disagreement.", "822 selected builds LayerPlan from exact current placements, fills lower support slots before dependent fit, then returns outputs in original selection order. Partial results are local and never returned on error. Geometric lower support dependency order differs from inventory draw order and remains coordinated by indices. Duplicate item/placement names may repeat for independent instances, but source IDs FittedPiece.piece.id remain distinct; no actual silent identity collision recipient established in this function.", "Original822 device integration test still requests LOD1 despite current4-6 admission, like819 ignored fixture; source-only stale fixture input does not create normal application policy or executed failure. Existing morph counts, trim ranges and skin weights are fixture observations rather than new assertions authored in this audit."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-272", "at": "2026-10-23T06:50:03.992874+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 823, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/preview.rs", "sha256": "c028a72d0f62e5d1f79d76d09e35a549de03dcbba566a0258e69fe8248023c09", "actual_EOF": 193, "material_ranges": [[1, 193]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/823"}, {"scope066_index": 824, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/proportions.rs", "sha256": "aa675179f3ddceae5646814bfc455eb8f45c96da71051a95324bd2e381ac92af", "actual_EOF": 73, "material_ranges": [[1, 73]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/824"}, {"scope066_index": 825, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/review_export.rs", "sha256": "e9ae7ed8089bca0317e77661168325bad4467de6bdc6ab5c08696808b15205f0", "actual_EOF": 125, "material_ranges": [[1, 125]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/825"}, {"scope066_index": 828, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/runtime_equipment/clothing.rs", "sha256": "72974a2d1ab294dcd4b04a06a153d9781a559e9478b7f429ff32909fd6a03f8e", "actual_EOF": 68, "material_ranges": [[1, 68]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/828"}, {"scope066_index": 829, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/runtime_equipment/warmup.rs", "sha256": "3129853d5e471b55c8d757b9904276bd5eb90404d662099db7012cd9961dcfb2", "actual_EOF": 85, "material_ranges": [[1, 85]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/829"}, {"scope066_index": 830, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/skin_rules.rs", "sha256": "79f4a9ac4e470e5788fd7d75fee1142c11da843d258e870a42249eca81ea957e", "actual_EOF": 475, "material_ranges": [[1, 475]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/830"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full823193/82473/825125/82868/82985/830475, all fingerprints verified. Original fixtures source only; no meshes, warmup, export or GPU operations executed.", "contracts": ["823 native preview clones current mesh attributes and selected material in one spawn. Component-specific material intentionally overrides whole-piece plate material, and trim has its own UV/material/range. These are separate physical surfaces, not two editable beliefs about one material. BodySkin stores reference body geometry for animation whereas native Mesh contains current visible/possibly occluded subset; difference is deliberate collider/deformation versus display role. Shared skin_material supplies both body and cap base appearance, avoiding an independent second skin palette.", "824 canonical BodyProportion::ALL and names select actual model columns. JointProportionBasis reference plus translation derivatives preserve immutable construction reference and coefficient response, different facts from current already-deformed joints. It explicitly checks actual pinned model limits match shared canonical limits, and rejects rotation/scale responses that portable translation basis cannot encode. Check detects upstream external-model drift; it does not make model and first-party limits one source. External pinned model adaptation is an appropriate dependency barrier, without inventing duplicate first-party policy. Centimetre conversion is native unit adapter.", "825 review export deliberately outputs original source body/recipe and each independently fitted catalog or worn design, WITHOUT current lower-layer support or decorative finish. This is reproducible isolated candidate review, not a claim to depict full worn outfit. Body and equipment records include current generator version and actual source IDs/design, all serialized from same call. Selected recipe mode resolves instance own design explicitly; catalogue mode resolves defaults. Captured authored design and derived mesh are provenance/output, not competing current authoring state. File publication atomicity is not promised; no concurrent consumer/run claim.", "828 RuntimeClothing uses current immutable RuntimeBody borrow and canonical static placement to generate one shell, then takes exact shell vertices/normals/faces while preserving matching body-topology skin/UV. faces metadata intentionally empty because offset cloth is not thickened plate; do not conflate physical PlateFace classification with native triangle indices. design_hash from item+placement names is a request design identity, not proven complete wearer geometry fingerprint; no consuming cache/hash-only geometry equality established here. Existing raw body upload ownership F051 remains separate.", "829 warmup performs actual temporary generation but discards meshes, retaining device kernel cache. WarmupReport fitted_placements counts calls, cached_kernels counts distinct compiled kernels: deliberately different observations. Lower-surface/alternate cuirass/wrapped tassets calls prepare additional algorithm branches, not hidden retained equipment or gameplay state. It intentionally uses canonical unposed body because kernels are shape-generic by contract; no body-specific generated geometry is installed for NPCs. No actual warmup execution or hosted acceptance credit.", "830 rigid skin policy selects canonical named joint once from current design/placement and synchronously replaces all eight joint words plus one-hot weights in selected ranges. Current anatomical anchors describe explicit physical motion policy: skull rigid, flexible caps/coifs keep skin, couter/poleyn distal joint, gorget and cuirass chest, individual waist sheets pelvis/side hip. These are intentionally different from fitting support region and nearest flexible body skin; do not merge merely by coincident joint names. Piece/component label plus geometric side is used for waist sheets as one construction step; no later independent cached anchor field.", "830 derives connected sheets from actual triangle connectivity each call, uses current pelvic X/mean sheet X to choose anatomical side, then fills indices and weights together. Private helper does not retain a stale sheet graph after mutation. Missing rig anchor errors remain fallible; a later error can leave partial raw mutable armor under this API, an operations/aggregate admission topic, not a demonstrated second current truth in07. Original tests compare intended flexible exclusions and rigid groups but were not run."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-273", "at": "2026-10-23T06:51:36.015809+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 833, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/studio_scene.rs", "sha256": "e486c21e58ee4c7f689bceed15e636afc2b11d12fc0989b02ca4a5e128c85fcf", "actual_EOF": 367, "material_ranges": [[1, 367]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/833"}, {"scope066_index": 834, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/studio_ui.rs", "sha256": "ab4430b01df6df4b77ee2e29a491531bd3a5782c92fd16b67a9aaba2d239b394", "actual_EOF": 435, "material_ranges": [[202, 302], [357, 429]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/834"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full833367 and834357-429; personally compared actual prior own252 complete202-302 UI output function for current result/export gate role. Root224 mandatory context boundaries retained: no350-356 material,430else context only,431+body excluded, no1-201/303-356/whole435 credit.", "contracts": ["833 current OrbitCamera yaw/pitch/radius/focus versus OrbitGoal requested endpoint are different temporal states. Transform derived every actual orbit update from current state; no independently editable successful-look flag shown. Pointer manual control clears pending goal intentionally; turn buttons target previous requested angles when glide is in progress. Source operation observation: approach97 clears goal based only on focus/radius, so angle-only turn from settled location can stop after one update; this is completion predicate issue, not reason to collapse current/requested state. Root04 notified as source navigation, no executed UI or07 unique finding.", "833 CharacterBounds is explicitly rest-pose source-body framing snapshot; it need not equal current animated outfit bounds. of() recomputes from generated vertices, and frame_shot consumes it for one requested framing. introduced Local<bool> records first-shot scheduling history, not a second bounds validity truth. RADIUS canonical local range drives actual user zoom and framing result. Portrait dimensions and full-body headroom deliberately differ.", "833 CreatorPanelRight current logical UI boundary supplies pointer exclusion, framing visible width and native physical viewport scale; separate units convert through window.scale_factor. center_beside_panel derives SubCameraView from current sizes and only writes on actual difference, not keeping a stale independently classified resize flag. Native camera default vertical FOV is assumed at337 while setup uses Camera3d default and does not own explicit projection field; exact external default dependency remains untraced rather than inventing matching foreign body credit or current mismatch.", "833 studio lights/environment map, backdrop/fog and physical stage have distinct indirect/specular/direct/ground roles. Dais geometry/floor elevations derive same DAIS_HEIGHT, different decorative band radius/height deliberate. Presentation initial pitch literal-.05 currently matches PRESENTATION_PITCH but initial state versus later shot policy need not universally match; no duplicate actual authored authority proven beyond coincident current calibration.", "834 scoped output202-302 actual save/export gates and warnings were already freshly read in252; current analysis preserves dirty/running/ready as scheduling and completed-result availability, with F050 insufficient upstream body key and failure-before-replacement qualification. Output function is complete current material; no rest-of-UI credit from source path identity.", "834357-429 delegates model controls, exposes animation physics/contact settings, and uses current ready/physics values to enable dependent controls. Physics choice versus actual playback state are separate. Pause label derives walk.playing then actual shown branch pauses native AnimationPlayer; the opposite else body431+ is outside scope and uncredited. Slider ranges describe UI authoring envelope, not another guarantee every public raw setting obeys it; per-second integration versus simulation-stage settings deliberately have different units/ranges and cannot be merged from same damping label.", "834 current parameters reset through Default, not manually repeated full default table. No cached text classification is retained. No all-UI or actual cloth solver settings application proof follows from this exact control slice."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-274", "at": "2026-10-23T06:52:54.791916+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 835, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/surface_cut.rs", "sha256": "a62fc268fef2024b832c7557c089daee6d948bfa8296b12f128bdbf5fea7b849", "actual_EOF": 277, "material_ranges": [[1, 277]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/835"}, {"scope066_index": 837, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer/mail_regions.rs", "sha256": "97d08f8f347891423424441d17e6d421f2b1855d184ac6c03aedc2914eab4dca", "actual_EOF": 94, "material_ranges": [[1, 94]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/837"}, {"scope066_index": 838, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer/pattern.rs", "sha256": "4b445b7dcd85806cde575fa40320b08412e87a18f12ff30c5e7de2648d8c3cab", "actual_EOF": 258, "material_ranges": [[1, 258]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/838"}, {"scope066_index": 839, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer_armor.rs", "sha256": "2e8a0fab854290874e3eda648d5a957f93d4ea0efe16bf0d12797d68099085d2", "actual_EOF": 186, "material_ranges": [[1, 186]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/839"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full835277/83794/838258/839186 verified against frozen source hashes; existing own263 private CutPlan caller and current device-underlayer pipeline personally reconciled to these actual roles. Original fixtures source only, child triangulation body not credited from mod declaration.", "contracts": ["835 SourcePoint stores triangle ordinal/barycentric correspondence rather than a second current world point. SurfaceCut derives point list and triangle indices together in one local construction from immutable reference body. Subsequent morph evaluation intentionally keeps reference cuts while recomputing actual positions, preserving identity through shape changes; no same-count topology replacement accepted by this constructor itself because no public wear method with a count-only gate. Existing saved-drape F055 is a different acceptance contract.", "835 include regions are unioned by partitioning only remaining uncovered polygons, subtract removes from already-kept set, and one correspondence key includes physical vertex ID plus UV vertex ID plus quantized weights. Physical borders later weld by actual position instead of UV identity deliberately, so material seams do not masquerade as physical trim edges. These are distinct equivalence relations, not rival authoritative definitions of one vertex. Public points/faces can be manually edited but actual current263 private fit constructs and consumes local plan rather than retaining externally mutable cut.", "835 snap distance, plane roundoff, area rejection and correspondence precision have different units and numerical purposes. They are not interchangeable duplicated tolerances merely because all address geometric robustness. Conforming triangulation direct call remains exact lower algorithm boundary with no unseen module/body proof. Full actual original tests illustrate overlap union and affine correspondence as source evidence only.", "837 derives mail anatomical clipping volumes from actual joint/frame and current design dimensions. Brayette uses continuous pelvic bridge instead of two thigh tubes intentionally; rear-knee strips, standing neck collar and ordinary cloth have distinct shape policies. Standard bib uses same depth scalar for lower bound and sloping planes in one invocation. No independently retained authoritative collar-height copy established here.", "838 required_frames enumerates actual fitting region requirements for browser readback; current regions dispatch calls compared explicitly: Doublet torso/two arms, hose sided leg, voiders none, brayette hips, knee sided knee, standard neck. Current membership agrees; this is an explicit preparation contract rather than a second stored runtime accepted frame map. Future dispatch changes must update dependency request or derive them from one plan, but no currently missing frame/normal failure inferred. Actual clipping planes and native placement remain independent authored geometry constraints versus game occupancy cells.", "838 tubes/boxes derive plane offsets from same current start/end/radius; no long-lived cached bounds beside mutable source. Authored cuts join procedural subtract regions intentionally, with clear precedence. Canonical structured joint names determine current landmark identity rather than text reparsing.", "839 fit_underlayer_async derives morph shape list and zips exact ordered results with same input names; actual lower263 fit returns endpoint per supplied shape. Base/endpoint direct positions versus deltas preserve reference and displacement, different observations; no same-list ordinal drift established. GeneratedArmor fields assembled together, output surface_domain is caller provenance and native domain data separately borrowed; raw API contract remains explicit rather than inferred checked relation.", "839 trunk hose intentionally reuses MailBrayette carrier geometry but replaces overall design_hash with full actual TrunkHoseDesign and applies alternate pane materials. Carrier shape and final product are different stages. Panes derive current angular centroid grouping, reorder indices once then create exact matching material ranges; positions/skin/morph correspondence do not change with triangle order. Empty physical PlateFace list denotes non-thickened layer, not missing native triangle data. No second live per-pane membership cache retained."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
{"id": "CAMERA-INITIAL07-CONTRACT-275", "at": "2026-10-23T06:53:53.974660+00:00", "lens": "audit-redundant-authority", "members": [{"scope066_index": 840, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer_equipment.rs", "sha256": "91acbb6c6ec41a6642c3ef9ab51d184ef615cb1cf631662d719f12a9b8f8b35d", "actual_EOF": 99, "material_ranges": [[1, 99]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/840"}, {"scope066_index": 841, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer_equipment/proportions.rs", "sha256": "b70d923027be5cb02b9771a3f8932728114177bc62c8b3b128a21c869cfeb651", "actual_EOF": 129, "material_ranges": [[1, 129]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/841"}, {"scope066_index": 842, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/underlayer_equipment/proportions/probe_bounds.rs", "sha256": "721a06c6ea10f1a278dacc94ffe003927da1662e139783ce5ac1f023d89ba7a7", "actual_EOF": 125, "material_ranges": [[1, 125]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/842"}, {"scope066_index": 843, "source_id": "pr-working:crates/adventuresim-character-creator/src/wardrobe.rs", "sha256": "41051202a9da2998dcf73b5a1e095088d6838c1a849a66d080631ac8304951b9", "actual_EOF": 154, "material_ranges": [[1, 154]], "scope_record": "continuation/cumulative-source-scope-parallel-066.json#/files/843"}], "actual_source_proof": "Fresh full84099/841129/842125/843154 verified. Current actual 839 construction and own263 fit caller contracts personally compared for static-sample versus morph endpoint role. Original tests read only, no device operations or new cases.", "contracts": ["840 with_body derives Wearer and SurfaceDomain from same current model/generated body, maps named explicit morphs separately from hypothetical static proportions, and passes both collections as distinct fit constraints. Correct_armor_fit then removes skeletal residual for exported portable deformation, different role from physical current fitting. Caller-supplied static samples do not become selected player body state.", "841 explicitly documents probes may be clipped before offset freezing and do not modify/certify editor body endpoints. It derives joint shifts from current reference bases, computes translated skin positions, limits same hypothetical pose by orientation and medial separation, then scales both vertex displacement and joint shift by identical fraction. This coordination keeps pose translation relation, while original normals are used as approximate orientation reference rather than a second selected live body surface. No actual selected body is silently capped by these probe routines.", "842 AreaPath stores linear/quadratic coefficients of oriented projected area along the entire hypothetical translation, not merely current endpoint area. Checked minimum includes stationary point, so equal endpoint orientations cannot hide an intermediate flip by this criterion. Binary search uses same immutable paths and rounds down before publishing fraction. Retained-oriented-area0.25 and retained-medial-separation0.25 coincide numerically but are independent geometric criteria, not one policy that must share a constant. No nonadjacent collision or editor-range promise inferred.", "843 Wardrobe privately owns canonical LibraryName key plus garment.selection.name. This is duplicated spelling with coordinated ownership: insert sets value name from key before validation; no mutable value getter, iter/get return immutable borrows; load/save explicitly enforce equality. There is no safe ordinary mutation of one retained value independently through API. Derived Deserialize can construct mismatched raw state, but load validates and get(key) versus displayed value remains an admission boundary rather than a normal mutation/cache defect. Existing initial03 raw adapter findings remain separately preserved.", "843 normal acquisition copies saved garment into inventory by explicit documented historical independence. A later wardrobe rename/replacement must not retroactively mutate prior owned articles; those copies are not redundant live authority. validate uses current canonical garment validation, not duplicate geometric finite policy. Original roundtrip/invalid fixture source proves intended contract only, not executed validation."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_other_lens_credit": true}
