ission03/contract-groups.jsonl#RIG-ADMISSION03-CONTRACT-395"}], "actual_source_proof": "All ten original fixture files freshly read in full, after personally consuming exact386-395 prior full actual-source narratives; current07 purpose compared to actual311 producer/receiver facts. No tests executed/added.", "contracts": ["1167 chronology expects one CharacterTime, no separate NPC personal clock, ActorLocal/PairwiseSoft no target synchronization and institutional wedding world time. These are acceptance oracles for deliberate different clock scopes, not separate active clock authorities. Include_str path references do not grant body coverage.", "1168 commitment expected unordered-pair symmetry and wedding notice equals canonical MINUTES_PER_YEAR reference. It references canonical constant rather than new numeric calendar policy. Terminal-release/event assertions are regression oracles, not alternative transition implementation.", "1169 courtship checks affinity at effective minute and typed rejection code roster. Literal line32 expects father_of_at(...StrategicMinute::new(minute)), while current typed-minute caller already passes minute; exact prior Rig388 static mismatch retained, no executed failing-test claim. Connected migration should update source assertions to final typed API, never introduce compatibility wrapper merely to satisfy old text. Expected rejection variants do not own live validator roster.", "1170 discovery explicitly requires frozen baselines, daily observer receipt and current-frontier penalty anchor, confirming independent historical attempt versus mutable affinity policy purpose. Original assertion lower helper bodies remain separately scoped; no finite raw skill guarantee from source string.", "1171 family four distinct-ID fixture asserts fixed roles and reciprocal parent/sibling edges, while short roster no edges and >4 errors. Actual factory311 has length contract, no arbitrary-unique-ID theorem from this example. Marriage preserves birth-family role versus residence/spouse household are different facts; referenced newborn copying not whole-body proof here.", "1172 lifecycle examples require stable Wedding-before-Birth ordering at equal effective minute, bounded nonstarving processable events and failure quarantine; no duplicated live scheduler. Death cleanup and personal-frontier assertions correspond active reservation/pregnancy closure versus immutable death/history. Current production transaction semantics not proved by contains checks.", "1173 marriage assertions expressly preserve effective history after active marker cleanup; current uniqueness index versus immutable marriage interval is intentional. Escrow/refund and outcome are different fund state/history, not conflicting amount owner. Actual311 normal transition coordinated, but text presence does not prove all late parsing precedes writes.", "1174 projections distinguishes active pregnancy from born-child projection and uses observer-time frontiers and gateway identity. These are derived view roles, no persisted second authority. Gateway predicate assertion cannot prove signed-in HTTP row filtering.", "1175 reproduction asserts reserved child identity, age-zero canonical construction before copied components, historical name/sex ordering and conserved leisure checkpoint; constants and snapshot expected values are fixtures, not another generator. Keep same full actor identity through connected migration; source assertions do not validate raw public Pregnancy aggregate.", "1176 socializing expects actor/day/target cumulative receipts, zero self-watermark, current slice historical availability and no-familiarity party path. Endpoint replay watermark and accumulated allocated minutes are independent facts. Current311 actual receiver confirms; original tests do not own or derive affinity independently. Every fixture is source-only, no runtime or new assertions."], "findings": [], "repair_status": "frozen", "validation_status": "not_run", "no_o