[[1, 133]], "prior_actual_source_proof": "continuation/rig/admission03/camera-support/contracts.jsonl#RIG-CAMERA-ADM03-622"}], "actual_source_proof": "Personally consumed exact585/594/596/621/622 full source facts, performed current07 purpose/construction/transition/recipient analysis plus listed fresh bodies. Autoresolve235/policy14/request133 freshly full read. Prior verdict/hash grants no07 coverage.", "contracts": ["1205 threat label parses canonical ThreatId and loot reads canonical profile; local quest encounter archetype subset groups Goblin/Kobold, undead and bandit concepts deliberately, other known threats None. This taxonomy projection is not a complete copy of ThreatId membership or same-fact threat identity; no broaden-to-ALL instruction. Canonical authored threat combatant owns scaling, wrapper delegates one owner. Imported large module symbol list is no body coverage.", "1205 record_autoresolve_report181 derives textual summary/log/resolution spelling and copies seed/rounds from one completed BattleOutcome. Historical report retains completed simulation, not a parallel live combat state resolver. Ammunition inventory mutation consumes actual available stacks separately from reported usage; caller resource sufficiency is explicit rather than equating requested and consumed counts here. No normal mismatching report/inventory demonstrated. Historical report fields/native SDK projections and summary text do not grant tactical HP/position state to strategic persistence.", "1214 policies is a codec boundary decoding two separately meaningful policy fields with canonical PromptMode/ResolutionPolicy parsers. No guessed default or text reclassification, no retained additional parsed cache. Raw stored words remain native representation, while first-party propagation should keep canonical owners through actual operations. Existing F011 shared vocabulary graph retains canonical parser ownership; no second unique defect from legitimate codec adapter.", "1216 runtime FactContext is recomputed from actual session/participant/current social roles/service and observer-known facts for one invocation. It is not persisted accepted authorization. Count derived from same participant set; public roles/presentation organization/local recognition differ hidden membership or legal power, no merge. Player age-band branch495 derives from cached Character.age_years, unlike effective birth-coordinate age gates in311; no proof of stale normal lifecycle here, so keep explicit cache-consumer dependency rather than infer current discrepancy. Open age-band/text versus canonical known FactValue cases retain shared-vocabulary concern F011 and canonical migration; no new authored demographic exclusion claim (F015 is separate solver policy).", "1216 referral flavor variant requires different source identity and display name, while original actual source receipt/context remains authority. Narrative wording and claim/lead evidence knowledge are different facts; alternate wording does not confer permission. Actual current generation/referral validates before delivery. Language compatibility explicitly sanitizes numerical hours/instinct and derives one presentation fluency/coefficient per call; local tier is presentation classification, not another persisted fluency authority. Actual business terms and relationship title are on-demand summaries, not legal membership tokens.", "1216 pairwise runtime address uses actual bound participants and canonical organization register; raw actor strings parsed then singular indexing retains existing raw malformed participant precondition (normal session factory creates valid actor IDs, earlier RigQUAL005 closure). No normal unsupported participant demonstrated. RuntimeSlot binding labels/prose are inert substitution values, not durable person/case/claim IDs. Source-backed full596 includes join/member/presence/current revision and exact cardinality paths, not merely visible text. No blanket parser/token seal from priv